[01:57:05] HARNESS: try 1: 10.9 s, exit 0, answer '{"proposal": {"CLOSE_GAP": 0.12}, "recruit": null, "why": "The median lost talk closed at a gap of 0.127 to the ask, above our CLOSE_GAP of 0.11, and the one 15-minute trial at 0.12 raised deals per hour from 160-228 to 256 and profit to 19.8M, though rank stayed at 19, so this is a single short run. No recruit is proposed because the lead\'s style (p25, MAX_RAISE 0.45, FIRM_GAP 0.05) already earns the most per talk and the evidence does not favor another style.", "ideas": ["Checkout refusals for \'unit ... is not in stock\' (3 of 100 recent payments) mean the buyer is committing to units the shop has already sold. Re-checking unit availability immediately before checkout, instead of at quote time, should remove these failed deals with no number change.", "C-grade goods break at 17.5% within 24 h, against 1.4% for A, and the warranty only refunds the price, so C-grade purchases look worth less than their list suggests. Prefer A and B SKUs, or only C-grade listings that include a warranty, is a routing rule for the team and cannot be set by any single number."]}'
