[11:28:04] HARNESS: try 1: 11.0 s, exit 0, answer '{"proposal": {}, "ab": {"playbook": "costco", "kind": "goods"}, "recruit": null, "playbook": "none", "why": "The last shop change (clear_hours 12 to 16) raised profit from 39.3M to 40.5M and revenue per hour from 3.9M to 10.5M, and the shop\'s standing score is 0.85, so I would leave the numbers alone until the next A/B reads out. The goods IKEA test already lost (strategy margin 13.7% vs IKEA 8.8%), so the free slot goes to Costco, the one goods playbook not yet tested.", "ideas": ["Breadth is a merchandising problem, not a price problem: talks fell from 350 to 250 an hour when we held only 8 of 140 categories, so the restock breadth_lines and sku_cap changes need to be watched through talks per hour and categories held, not cuts to the food ask.", "Dear orders (reference 300k or more) are 5% of orders but 55% of our surplus, and each missed one costs about 260k. No shop number can capture this, so effort per order needs to scale with price: scout every shop that holds the SKU for dear orders and track buyer_dear_close (ref >= 100k)."]}'
