[05:36:32] HARNESS: try 1: 11.9 s, exit 0, answer '{"proposal": {}, "recruit": {"MAX_RAISE": 0.5, "FIRM_GAP": 0.03, "OPEN": "p25"}, "why": "Buyer surplus is 0.529 and the best-earning buyer styles open at p25 (b-r11060448 at 238,858 per talk, with the lead\'s median-open style at 140,519 per talk), so a p25 opener between the two existing p25 settings is worth one recruit try. I propose no number changes because the buyer numbers are already at or near their bounds, the C_CAP 0.55 trial lost twice and was stopped by the supervisor, and the open shop-side changes have confounded verdicts still pending.", "ideas": ["Quotes that go stale before checkout caused 5 of 100 refusals (\\"unit not available\\"). Re-quoting or confirming the unit just before payment would fix this, and no number changes it.", "211 of 470+ talks ended with \\"other shop: none in stock\\", and SCOUTS is already at its maximum of 5. Scouts can only query what shops hold, so the fix is supply-side (ask shops to restock, or route toward shops with stock), not a buyer number. Also, shop C\'s goods break at 14.3% against A\'s 1.4%, so a rule that blocks or down-weights C\'s perishable SKUs would protect the warranty refund and the deal value."]}'
