[08:09:38] HARNESS: try 1: 10.0 s, exit 0, answer '```json\n{"proposal": {}, "ab": null, "recruit": null, "playbook": "none", "why": "We are 8th on the Players board with ALL 0.823, and the last two shop changes (ask_frac 0.93 and clear_hours 16 to 24) either lost margin or were confounded, so the current numbers are the best-supported set we have. Holding them lets the pending 23:28 clear_hours verdict and the ask_frac 0.9 result settle before any new change.", "ideas": ["Warranty demand is high: 45% of goods asks request one (287 of 637), but we offer only 6 h and a warranty line is not a shop number. A priced service plan at true cost, as the premium_service playbook describes, would monetize that demand without any grade claim, but it needs a product or policy change.", "Cheap goods under 100k carry about 439k of the roughly 1.3M/h margin and we hold only 2 units. The 07:08 restock cap change (sku_cap x2 for fast cheap SKUs) targets this directly, but it is untested and sits in restock, not in the shop\'s numbers, so it should be judged on its own 2 h window."]}\n```'
