t it; several later changes also moved stock_value together with a knob."}, {"rule": "Do not flip a knob back and forth hunting for a gain (ask_frac_food 0.72/0.75/0.8, clear_hours 16/20/24, max_turns 5/6/7, market_ask 0.9-1.05); these oscillations produced no verified result, so stop tuning them without an A/B.", "evidence": ["F9", "F10", "F12", "F13", "F14", "F15", "F24", "F25", "F37", "F47", "F48", "F53", "F56"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Each step looked like +/- tens of percent on raw margin, yet the next step reversed it (e.g. clear_hours 20 -> 24 gave +23%, 24 -> 20 also gave +23%), so the sequence churned without learning anything."}, {"rule": "Lowering floors and min_margin (min_margin 0.1 -> 0.06 -> 0.04 -> 0.02, floor_frac_food 0.7 -> 0.64) is unproven; test it by A/B before keeping it, since the readings are raw only.", "evidence": ["F33", "F36", "F39", "F40", "F43", "F50", "F60"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Raw margin rose after min_margin cuts (+36%, +154%, +119%) but the later costco bundle with min_margin 0.14 was reverted to 0.02 without a verified reading either way; the rises may just be hour-of-day effects."}, {"rule": "Seller-side model haggling (haiku via model_share) lost to the rules, so keep rules as the default and do not push model_share up without a share-based A/B.", "evidence": ["F1", "F3"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Letting the model see what the rule would do still lost and model_share dropped to 0 since 11/04 10:00; re-enabling it blindly would repeat the loss."}, {"rule": "Code changes without a verdict (scout wait, b-fast single-call haggle, food shelf-life shipping, kit v4 checkout workaround) should be treated as unmeasured; check them against paid-sales share before building on them.", "evidence": ["F2", "F4", "F5"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "They were shipped with no verdict, so a later drop or gain in sales cannot be attributed to them or ruled out."}]}'
