[12:38:29] HARNESS: try 1: 25.6 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Keep buyer CAP at 0.75, the latest kept value. Move it lower only through a new same-hours A/B and judge it on saved/deal.","evidence":["F43","F38","F34","F32","F22"],"status":"verified","trap":"F22, F32 and F34 rejected lowering CAP from 0.85, but F38 (0.85 -> 0.8) and F43 (0.8 -> 0.75) then won, with saved/deal 0.33 -> 0.3498. Close rate fell 0.667 -> 0.618, so a close-rate drop alone is not a reason to reject. Do not go back to 0.85 either."},{"rule":"Keep FIRM_GAP at 0.07, the value that won in two steps (0.03 -> 0.05, then 0.05 -> 0.07). Do not retry 0.07 -> 0.05.","evidence":["F23","F25","F31","F40"],"status":"verified","trap":"F31 and F40 both tried 0.07 -> 0.05 and neither was taken. F31 showed saved/deal 0.2949 -> 0.2988, a gain too small to count as a win. Re-running the same trial wastes half the orders."},{"rule":"Keep FOOD_MARGIN at 1.15. Do not try 1.2 again without a new reason.","evidence":["F33","F24","F45"],"status":"verified","trap":"The 1.1 -> 1.15 move failed in F24 and then won in F33 (saved/deal 0.2981 -> 0.3195), so one lost trial does not settle a value. The 1.15 -> 1.2 trial (F45) was not taken: saved/deal 0.3619 -> 0.3536, even though close rate rose 0.617 -> 0.678."},{"rule":"Leave MAX_RAISE at 0.4. Every alternative (0.5, 0.35, 0.3) was not taken, in five trials.","evidence":["F21","F27","F29","F35","F44"],"status":"verified","trap":"F44 (0.4 -> 0.3) showed saved/deal 0.3472 -> 0.3535, a small gain on uneven arms (149 vs 107 orders). It was still not taken. Differences of about 0.005 are noise, so do not chase them."},{"rule":"Leave C_CAP at 0.6. Do not restart the 0.55 trial, which lost five times.","evidence":["F13","F17","F18","F28","F36","F20","F30"],"status":"verified","trap":"At 0.55 the close rate rises (0.598 -> 0.683 in F17), which looks good. But surplus/order or saved/deal falls in most trials (23094 -> 11281 in F17; 0.2972 -> 0.2741 in F28). F36 had a small saved/deal gain (0.3132 -> 0.3209) and was still not taken. The supervisor already stopped restarts in F20. Grade C now follows the C_WARRANTY rule (F30), which drops the C_CAP price clause."},{"rule":"Raise close_gap (the gap at which the buyer closes) for expensive SKUs. Tune it by price tier, not with one global value.","evidence":["F8","F19","F14","F11"],"status":"verified","trap":"F8 (200k or more) and F19 (300k or more) won big on surplus/order (+243% and +65%), but that is the older metric, not saved/deal. A global CLOSE_GAP 0.11 -> 0.12 lost in F11 and won in F14, so it is noisy. Do not extend the tiering on the strength of those two numbers alone."},{"rule":"Do not add new candidate-ranking reweightings (break-rate penalties, per-list-price ranking). Their saved/deal came out negative, and two were reverted.","evidence":["F37","F39","F41","F42","F26"],"status":"verified","trap":"Each was predicted at +1% to +4% but measured -2%, -6%, -4% and -2% on saved/deal. F39 was reverted by the supervisor in F41, and F42 reverted itself. F37 and F26 were kept despite negative A/B numbers. Treat them as unproven, not as wins, and do not build on them."},{"rule":"Do not rely on the F6 and F7 conclusions (floor entries for lowest asks, taking the second ask outright). Their verdicts are weak.","evidence":["F6","F7"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Both were judged on raw before/after, which reads the hour of day. F6 measured -1% against an expected +5%, and F7 measured -10% against an expected +5%. Neither was checked with an A/B, so do not treat \'kept\' as proof they help."}]}'
