[18:05:06] HARNESS: try 1: 25.9 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Do not add reserves, room tests, surge cut-offs, own-sales caps or score-based drops to 300k+ goods lines. Change those lines only by adding depth to hot SKUs (sku_score at DEAR_HOT or more). Re-judge this on board points per hour before relying on it, because the evidence is weak.","evidence":["F26","F28","F42","F53","F64","F80"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Each guard was expected to help and was reverted on raw before/after verdicts, which read the hour of day. F28 reserve: shop_margin_h -24%. F42 room test: -32%, shop_deals_h 115.3 -> 67.7. F53 surge cut-off: -30%. F64 list-price surge cut-off: shop_deals_h -43%. F80 score-based drop: -36%, shop_deals_h 80.7 -> 41.3. The pattern is consistent but none of it was judged on our share of paid sales, so a guard might still be worth trying if paid-sales evidence appears."},{"rule":"Give a 150-300k goods SKU at DEAR_HOT or more depth scaled by heat capped at 2x. This is the one depth change judged on the board\'s terms, so keep it.","evidence":["F90"],"status":"verified","trap":"Measured shop_revenue_h +398% and shop points/h +613%, net of the market\'s own change, against +8% expected. Other changes (F91, F92) fell inside the same 3 h after window, so do not credit the whole size to this change or stretch it to the 300k+ cap."},{"rule":"Put depth on goods that keep selling and keep non-hot 300k+ SKUs small (1 unit). Scale hot cheap SKUs by heat. Size depth from the market\'s sales and sku_score, never from our own past sales.","evidence":["F26","F33","F38","F60"],"status":"unverified","trap":"All were kept on raw before/after verdicts that read the hour of day: F33 shop_margin_h +19%, F38 +107%, F60 shop_deals_h +13%. They show direction only. F26 capped 300k+ stock at 4 h of our own 300k+ sales, but those sales were low because restock had never bought the market\'s best sellers, so the cap locked in the bug and was reverted."},{"rule":"Free stock room from slow 300k+ units by sku_score: exclude them from the stock_value cap and the goods_frac room, and stop adding slow lines once 40 are held. Never exclude by age.","evidence":["F50","F57","F66"],"status":"unverified","trap":"The age-based version (unsold over a day) was expected +20% and measured -29% shop_margin_h, and was reverted. The sku_score versions were kept (F57 shop_deals_h +63%, F66 shop_margin_h +252%), but only on raw before/after verdicts, so the size is not trustworthy."},{"rule":"The hot 300k+ heat cap (5x dear_depth, 20 units a line) is undecided. Judge it alone on board points per hour before stacking more depth on 300k+ lines.","evidence":["F84","F88","F90"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Raising the cap from 3x to 5x (F84, expected +10%) measured -20% on raw before/after and was reverted. The supervisor restored it with no verdict (F88). F90\'s verdict covers only the 150-300k heat at 2x, so reading it as proof that 5x works would be wrong."},{"rule":"Do not count on the food shelf-life bar change (selling food categories need min(min_shelf_hours, 48)) to cut refusals. Check shelf_refused_h before building on it.","evidence":["F77"],"status":"contradicted","trap":"It was kept, but shelf_refused_h was expected -30% and measured +21%, the wrong way. Assuming it worked would hide a refusal problem."}]}'
