[11/09 19:59:13] HARNESS: try 1: 22.0 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [\n{"rule": "Keep goods haggling on slow concessions with more turns (step 0.4, max_turns 6 as restored at 11/09 09:21). Do not go back to fast concessions with few turns (step 0.5 with max_turns 3 or 4).", "evidence": ["F6", "F57", "F60"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "The only same-hours A/B (F6) had the fast IKEA arm at 8.8% margin over list and 17 of 31 deals, against 13.7% and 39 of 55 for the strategy. It was read on margin per talk, not board_pts_h, so it is weak. The 06:43 bundle with step 0.5 and max_turns 4 was undone in F60, which has no verdict of its own. Treat this as a direction, not a proven value."},\n{"rule": "Judge every shop change on board_pts_h and on sales paid on the ledger. Margin per talk, margin/h and deals/h are parts, never the aim.", "evidence": ["F6", "F60"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "A playbook can win on margin per talk and still lose paid sales. F6 was read on margin per talk, and the 06:43 bundle was undone at 09:21 (F60) for that reason. Raw margin/h before 11/9 11:13 reads the hour of day, so the -72% and +718%-style swings in the number rows are noise."},\n{"rule": "Change one shop number at a time, with no bundles and no stock or restock change in the same window. Let the 2 h verdict and the fast guard judge it. No A/B unless the change is risky and cannot be judged otherwise.", "evidence": ["F8", "F57", "F60"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Nearly every number row from F7 to F67 is MIXED, so none can be blamed or credited. F57 moved seven knobs at once and had to be undone as a whole in F60. F66 shows how little a windowed raw-margin reading means when stock_value and reserve_cash move beside it."},\n{"rule": "Do not flip a knob back and forth. Read its value now before moving it, never move it toward a value you think it already has, and leave it for its full window.", "evidence": ["F58", "F59", "F60", "F63", "F64", "F65"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "On 11/09 ask_frac went 0.85 -> 0.7 -> 0.85 -> 0.7 in about 2 h (F58, F59, F60). ask_frac_food went 0.7 -> 0.75 at 12:06 and back to 0.7 at 12:07 (F63, F64, F65). Each flip left the windows after it confounded and added no information."},\n{"rule": "Treat all number verdicts of 11/05-11/09 as no evidence either way. Do not hold or avoid a value because of them; retest a number only when it can be judged alone.", "evidence": ["F8", "F9", "F57", "F67"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "They are MIXED or read raw margin/h. The -33% for ask_frac 0.85 -> 0.9 was already shown confounded in F8. Quoting a past percentage as proof for or against a number repeats that error."},\n{"rule": "Do not cut floors, min_margin, aged_margin or final_frac as a general move, and keep final_frac 1.0. Sell under cost only to free stuck capital.", "evidence": ["F6", "F57", "F60"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Looser, faster concessions lost margin and deals in F6. The 06:43 bundle with floors at 0.45 was undone in F60. Book counts unsold stock at cost, so a sale under cost lowers Book at once."},\n{"rule": "Keep the rules as the seller\'s default haggler. Raise model_share (haiku haggling) only if paid-sales evidence from our share supports it.", "evidence": ["F1", "F3"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "The model still lost even when shown what the rule would do (F3), and model_share has been 0 since 10:00 on 11/04. That was never a formal verdict, so it is a weak reason to ban the idea, but it is no reason to bring it back without data."},\n{"rule": "Count these code changes as unmeasured: food shelf-life shipping, the 6 s scout wait with the b-fast single-call haggle, and the kit v4 checkout workaround. Do not credit or blame them for later swings in paid sales.", "evidence": ["F2", "F4", "F5"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "They shipped with no verdict and many changes landed on top. A later gain or drop in paid sales can neither be pinned on them nor ruled out, so do not rebuild or remove them on a hunch."}\n]}'
