[11/09 20:16:03] HARNESS: try 1: 32.0 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [\n{"rule": "Treat a CAP cut as a trade of close rate for saved/deal, and judge it on board points/h and paid sales, not on saved/deal alone. Read the current CAP before moving it (order 5). 0.8 -> 0.75 was kept (F43). 0.75 -> 0.7 (F47) was undone 17 minutes later with no verdict (F48), so it is no evidence either way. Do not cite it as a win or a loss.", "evidence": ["F43", "F38", "F34", "F32", "F22", "F47", "F48"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The same cut gave different results. 0.85 -> 0.8 lost on 11/06 12:28 (F22) and 11/07 13:15 (F32), and 0.85 -> 0.82 lost on 11/08 05:01 (F34). Then 0.85 -> 0.8 won on 11/08 14:39 (F38) and 0.8 -> 0.75 won on 11/08 21:51 (F43), each time with close rate down (0.709 -> 0.653 and 0.667 -> 0.618). Close rate is what feeds paid sales, and first priority is more paid sales, so a saved/deal gain bought with a lower close rate can cost board points. Do not stack cuts on saved/deal alone."},\n{"rule": "Do not step FIRM_GAP back down from its raised value. Two upward steps won (0.03 -> 0.05 in F23, 0.05 -> 0.07 in F25), and 0.07 -> 0.05 was not taken twice (F31, F40). Read its value now before any move.", "evidence": ["F23", "F25", "F31", "F40"], "status": "verified", "trap": "0.07 -> 0.05 looked harmless on 11/07 10:29 (saved/deal 0.2949 -> 0.2988) because saved/deal rose slightly. Close rate fell 0.698 -> 0.655, and the same step lost again on 11/08 17:55 (0.3197 -> 0.3124). Reading saved/deal without close rate makes the step look fine."},\n{"rule": "Do not push FOOD_MARGIN above the level 1.15 that won (F33). 1.15 -> 1.2 was not taken (F45). Do not retry 1.2 without a new reason, and read the value now before any move.", "evidence": ["F33", "F24", "F45"], "status": "verified", "trap": "1.1 -> 1.15 lost on 11/06 17:22 (F24, saved/deal 0.2947 -> 0.2905) and then won on 11/07 23:45 (F33, 0.2981 -> 0.3195), so a single A/B on this number is weak. 1.15 -> 1.2 lost on 11/09 07:33 (saved/deal 0.3619 -> 0.3536), although its close rate rose (0.617 -> 0.678)."},\n{"rule": "MAX_RAISE results are not stable across hours. The one win, 0.4 -> 0.35 on 11/09 10:35 (F46), is the only one judged on buyer points/h (+3%), and it is the latest row. 0.4 -> 0.3 was not taken twice (F27, F44) and 0.4 -> 0.5 once (F21). Do not go back to 0.4, and do not try 0.3 or 0.5 without a new reason. Read the value now first.", "evidence": ["F46", "F29", "F35", "F27", "F44", "F21"], "status": "verified", "trap": "0.4 -> 0.35 lost on 11/07 07:25 (F29) and 11/08 08:49 (F35) and won on 11/09 10:35 (F46). 0.4 -> 0.3 on 11/09 01:09 (F44) had saved/deal up (0.3472 -> 0.3535) but close rate down (0.725 -> 0.71). A saved/deal gain with a falling close rate is not a win."},\n{"rule": "Leave C_CAP alone. The 0.6 -> 0.55 trial lost five times (F13, F17, F18, F28, F36), and the supervisor stopped the third (F20), so do not restart it. Since 11/07 10:14 grade C is accepted only with a warranty and the C_CAP price clause is dropped (F30), so the number is probably inert and a new trial has nothing to measure.", "evidence": ["F13", "F17", "F18", "F28", "F36", "F20", "F30"], "status": "verified", "trap": "At 0.55 close rate rises (0.598 -> 0.683 on 11/05 19:30), which looks good, but surplus/order or saved/deal fell (23094 -> 11281, 0.2972 -> 0.2741). F18 was nearly flat on surplus/order (20396 -> 20548) with close rate up, and F36 had saved/deal up (0.3132 -> 0.3209) with close rate up. Both were still not taken, and after F30 even a good-looking row would be moving a number that no longer prices grade C."},\n{"rule": "Set close_gap by price tier. Keep the overrides for SKUs at 200k or more (F8) and 300k or more (F19). Treat the global CLOSE_GAP as unsettled: read its value before touching it, and do not cite either global step as settled.", "evidence": ["F8", "F19", "F14", "F11"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "The tier overrides won big (+243% and +65%), but on the older surplus/order metric, not saved/deal or board points, so they are weak on the board\'s terms. The global 0.11 -> 0.12 step contradicts itself: not taken on 11/05 00:07 (F11, close rate 0.705 -> 0.652), kept on 11/05 11:12 (F14, 0.656 -> 0.723). Neither row was judged on saved/deal or paid sales."},\n{"rule": "Do not add new candidate-ranking, first-offer, walk-away or shop-weighting rules on a prediction alone. Most such code changes measured worse than predicted. Treat the ones that are still live as candidates to revert if a later one-at-a-time paid-sales verdict goes against them.", "evidence": ["F12", "F26", "F30", "F37", "F39", "F41", "F42", "F10", "F16", "F49"], "status": "verified", "trap": "These changes predicted gains of +1% to +5% (F49 predicted -5% on secs/order) and measured -10% (F12), -2% (F26, F30, F37), -6% (F39, reverted in F41), -4% (F42, reverted), -3% (F10), +1% on secs/order where -8% was expected (F16) and +13% on secs/order where -5% was expected (F49). Being kept did not mean they helped: F26, F30 and F37 were kept despite measuring below zero on saved/deal."},\n{"rule": "Do not rely on F6 (floor entries for lowest asks) or F7 (taking the second ask outright) as evidence that the idea works or fails. Their verdicts are weak.", "evidence": ["F6", "F7"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Both were judged on raw before/after, which reads the hour of day (F6 measured -1% against an expected +5%, F7 -10% against an expected +5%). Either could be reasonable or harmful. Treating them as proof in either direction would be a guess."}\n]}'
