cession playbooks (fewer turns, bigger steps, low floors). Keep slower concessions with more turns unless paid-sales evidence on board terms says otherwise.", "evidence": ["F6", "F57", "F60"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "F6 is the only same-hours A/B: the strategy made 13.7% margin over list a talk and 39 deals of 55, IKEA 8.8% and 17 of 31, because fast concessions and fewer turns lost margin and deals. It was read on margin per talk, not board points, so it is weak. The 11/09 bundle (max_turns 6 -> 4, step 0.4 -> 0.5, floor_frac 0.67 -> 0.45) repeated the shape and was undone (F57, F60)."}, {"rule": "Keep the rules as the seller\'s default haggler. Raise model_share (haiku haggling) only if paid-sales evidence from our share supports it.", "evidence": ["F1", "F3"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "The model still lost even when shown what the rule would do (F3), and model_share has been 0 since 10:00 on 11/04. There was never a formal verdict, so this is a weak default, not a proven fact."}, {"rule": "Count these code changes as unmeasured: food shelf-life shipping, the 6 s scout wait with the b-fast single-call haggle, and the kit v4 checkout workaround. Do not credit or blame them for later swings in paid sales.", "evidence": ["F2", "F4", "F5"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "They shipped with no verdict and many changes landed on top. A later gain or drop can neither be pinned on them nor ruled out, so do not rebuild on them or revert them from a hunch."}]}'
