[11/09 23:47:23] HARNESS: try 1: 6.8 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [{"rule": "Do not keep or revert a forum change on a raw before/after reading of forum_votes_post (hour before against hour after). It reads the hour of day. Judge each forum change on its own, one at a time, on the forum rating (0-1, counted as itself), as standing order 6 says.", "evidence": ["F3", "F4"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "11/05 09:22 was reverted on -20% and 11/05 10:57 was kept despite -9%. Both were raw before/after readings, so both are weak. Neither shows what the change did to the forum rating, and forum_votes_post is not the board\'s metric."}, {"rule": "The narrowed note() in forum_r3.py (top 4 shops with 2+ settles, last 2 refs per shown shop) is not disproven. It may be retried if it is the only forum change in its window, and judged on the forum rating and on which posts draw dislike stances.", "evidence": ["F3"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Reading the revert (-20%) as proof the change was bad. That figure is a weak raw reading, so a good change may have been discarded."}, {"rule": "Treat the cap on our_deals posts (none if either of our last two posts was one, about 1 post in 3) as unproven. Do not tune the cap. Check whether our_deals posts are among those that draw dislike stances, since the forum rating is lost on dislikes.", "evidence": ["F4"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "It was kept with +15% expected against -9% measured, on a weak raw reading. \'Kept\' is not \'helped\', and 14/14 tests passing only shows the code runs."}, {"rule": "The posting cadence is fixed by code at 310 s, the market\'s limit (it was 600 s before 11/06 15:01), so it is not a lever for the team. Put forum effort into post quality, meaning the stances that draw dislikes, and never trade quality for count.", "evidence": ["F5"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Assuming more posts mean more votes or a higher rating. 11/06 15:01 has no verdict, and posts are only a small part of the buyer\'s score."}, {"rule": "Keep prices built by code from the ledger and forum kinds built by code from the ledger, weighted by votes. Neither has a verdict, so do not credit them with gains. Make each later shop change alone in its window so it gets its own verdict.", "evidence": ["F1", "F2"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Layering changes on these two foundations in the same hours gives MIXED windows, which are no verdict, so the lead cannot say which change moved board points."}]}'
