[11/10 00:19:42] HARNESS: try 1: 20.1 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Keep the heat-scaled depth for a 150-300k goods SKU at DEAR_HOT or more, capped at 2x dear_depth. It is the only depth change judged on the board\'s terms. Do not read its size as a forecast for the next depth change.","evidence":["F90"],"status":"verified","trap":"It measured shop_revenue_h +398% and shop points/h +613%, net of the market\'s own change (paid value x1.05, count x1.08), against +8% expected. F89 and F91 (clear_frac, dear_depth 4 -> 5) and the F88 restore fell in the same hours, so the size is not attributable to this change alone. Quoting +398% as the expected gain of the next depth change would be wrong."},{"rule":"The hot 300k+ heat cap (5x dear_depth, up to 20 units a line) is currently in force but undecided. Before stacking more depth on 300k+ lines, judge it alone on board_pts_h with the 2 h verdict and the fast guard.","evidence":["F84","F88","F90"],"status":"unverified","trap":"The 3x to 5x raise read shop_margin_h -20% on raw before/after, which reads the hour of day, and was reverted. The supervisor restored it at F88 without a verdict on the board\'s terms. Both the revert and the restore rest on weak or no evidence, so neither is proof that 5x helps or hurts."},{"rule":"Keep the limits on slow (sku_score under DEAR_HOT) 300k+ stock: 1-unit depth, the slow_held cap of 40, and slow units excluded from the stock_value cap and goods_frac room. Do not credit them with the gains read beside them.","evidence":["F38","F57","F66"],"status":"unverified","trap":"All three were judged on raw before/after (weak) with other changes nearby. F66 read shop_margin_h +252% against +5% expected, a size that shows the read followed the hour of day, not the change."},{"rule":"Do not treat a revert on raw before/after margin as proof that an idea is bad, and do not retry a reverted code change as written without a board-terms check. Several 300k+ restock code changes were reverted on that read alone.","evidence":["F42","F50","F53","F64","F80","F84"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Each revert rests on a raw before/after read (weak), e.g. F42 shop_margin_h -32% and F64 shop_deals_h -43%. Treating them as settled would bar changes that were never fairly judged. Treating them as safe to retry would repeat untested risks."},{"rule":"Do not size a stock cap from our own recent sales rate when that rate was depressed by a restock bug. Check whether the shop was buying the market\'s best sellers first.","evidence":["F26","F20","F24"],"status":"unverified","trap":"F26 capped 300k+ stock at 4 h of our own 300k+ sales (2.2 an hour). Those sales were low because restock did not buy the market\'s best sellers until the ranking and room fixes of 12:46-13:48, so the cap would have locked the bug in. It was reverted on a raw read (weak), but the reasoning stands."},{"rule":"Do not count on the food shelf-life change (selling food categories need min(min_shelf_hours, 48)) to cut refusals. Check shelf_refused_h on a closed window before building on it.","evidence":["F77"],"status":"contradicted","trap":"It was kept, but shelf_refused_h was expected -30% and measured +21%, the wrong way. The read was raw before/after (weak), so it is not proof of harm either. Building on it as a working fix would assume a gain the record does not show."}]}'
