ence": ["F42", "F50", "F53", "F64", "F80", "F84"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Each revert rests on a raw before/after read (weak), e.g. F42 shop_margin_h -32% and F64 shop_deals_h -43%. Treating them as settled would bar changes that were never judged fairly. Re-running one unchanged without a check repeats the same weak read."},\n  {"rule": "Do not size a stock cap from our own recent sales rate when that rate was depressed by a restock bug. Check first whether the shop was buying the market\'s best sellers.", "evidence": ["F26", "F20", "F24"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "F26 capped 300k+ stock at 4 h of our own 300k+ sales (2.2 an hour). Those sales were low because restock did not buy the market\'s best sellers until the ranking and room fixes of F20 and F24, so the cap locked in the bug. The supervisor reverted it; the reasoning is not a measured verdict."},\n  {"rule": "Do not count on the food shelf-life change (selling food categories need min(min_shelf_hours, 48)) to cut refusals. Check shelf_refused_h on a closed window before building on it.", "evidence": ["F77"], "status": "contradicted", "trap": "It was kept, but shelf_refused_h was expected -30% and measured +21%, the wrong way. The read was raw before/after (weak), so it is not proof of harm either, but building on it as a win would be wrong."}\n]}\n```'
