[11/10 05:37:10] HARNESS: try 1: 20.3 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Change one shop number at a time and let the 2 h verdict and the fast guard judge it alone. Do not bundle knobs, and do not touch stock or restock settings (stock_value, reserve_cash, dear_depth) in the same window. Only a number judged alone gives a usable reading.","evidence":["F70","F57","F60","F66"],"status":"verified","trap":"The 11/09 06:43 bundle moved seven knobs and had to be undone whole at 09:21. On 11/09 13:40 warranty_hours, final_frac and reserve_cash moved together, and the row is MIXED with no verdict. Only the single change at F70 produced a clean reading."},{"rule":"The one clean reading so far is a lower food floor: floor_frac_food 0.65 -> 0.62 raised shop points/h net of the market by 112% (178/6046 -> 218/6087 sales). Treat it as a lead for food only. Read the value now (0.62) before any next step, make a small step, and judge it alone. Do not carry it over to goods floors.","evidence":["F70","F57","F60","F69"],"status":"verified","trap":"Copying the food result to goods floors, or cutting floors in a bundle (floor_frac 0.67 -> 0.45 on 11/09 06:43), was undone at 09:21. The goods-floor row F69 is MIXED, so it is no evidence."},{"rule":"Do not flip a knob back and forth. Read its value now before moving it, never move it toward a value it already has, and leave it for its full window.","evidence":["F58","F59","F60","F63","F64","F65"],"status":"unverified","trap":"On 11/09 ask_frac went 0.85 -> 0.7 -> 0.85 -> 0.7 within about 2 h (07:02, 07:21, 09:21). ask_frac_food went 0.7 -> 0.75 at 12:06 and back to 0.7 at 12:07. Each flip left only MIXED or no-verdict rows. The facts are code rows with no verdicts, so this rests on the record of the churn, not on a measured gain."},{"rule":"Judge a playbook or a bundle by paid sales and board_pts_h, not by margin per talk or raw margin/h. Do not copy a rival\'s playbook whole; faster concessions, lower floors and fewer turns have cost deals.","evidence":["F6","F57","F60"],"status":"unverified","trap":"The IKEA playbook lost its A/B (13.7% margin over list a talk, 39 deals of 55, against 8.8%, 17 of 31) because fast concessions and fewer turns lost deals. The 11/09 costco bundle (max_turns 6 -> 4, step 0.4 -> 0.5) copied the same pattern and was undone at 09:21. F6 is old and its verdict read margin, so it is weak."},{"rule":"Treat every number verdict of 11/05-11/09 as no evidence either way. Do not hold or avoid a value because of one, and do not cite their percentages. Retest a number only when it can be judged alone.","evidence":["F7","F8","F9","F39","F40","F43","F67"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Each of these is MIXED or read raw margin/h, which reads the hour of day. Swings such as +401% (11/08 10:15) or -72% (11/08 05:35) came with several other changes in the same hours. Citing them as proof of a value is how churn started."},{"rule":"Count these code changes as unmeasured: food shelf-life shipping, the 6 s scout wait with the b-fast single-call haggle, the kit v4 checkout workaround, and the seller model haggling share. Do not credit or blame them for later swings in paid sales.","evidence":["F1","F2","F3","F4","F5"],"status":"unverified","trap":"They shipped with no verdict and many changes landed on top. A later gain or drop can neither be pinned on them nor ruled out, so do not rebuild on them or revert them on a hunch."}]}'
