[11/10 05:53:39] HARNESS: try 1: 26.6 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Treat CAP as a trade-off between saved/deal and close rate, and judge any move on board points/h and paid sales, never on saved/deal alone. Read the current value first, since the only recent keep is 0.8 -> 0.75 (F43). 0.7 has no verdict: F47 was undone by F48 within 17 minutes.","evidence":["F43","F38","F34","F32","F22","F47","F48"],"status":"verified","trap":"Lower CAP raises saved/deal but cuts close rate (F43: saved/deal 0.33 -> 0.3498, close rate 0.667 -> 0.618). The same direction gave mixed results: 0.85 -> 0.8 was kept in F38 but not taken in F22 and F32, and 0.85 -> 0.82 was not taken in F34. Citing one win as settled, or citing F47 as evidence, misleads.","status_note":""},{"rule":"Keep FIRM_GAP where it is after its two winning upward steps (0.03 -> 0.05 in F23, 0.05 -> 0.07 in F25). Do not step it down again, and do not push it up without a new reason. Read the value first.","evidence":["F23","F25","F31","F40","F50","F52"],"status":"verified","trap":"A step down looks harmless when saved/deal rises (F31: 0.2949 -> 0.2988) but close rate falls (0.698 -> 0.655). On the board\'s terms the latest step down was far worse (F52: buyer points/h 0.000582 -> 0.00038, -35%). 0.07 -> 0.09 gave only +2% points/h with saved difference -0.2 sd (F50), which is not a win.","status_note":""},{"rule":"Keep FOOD_MARGIN at the value that won (1.1 -> 1.15, F33). Do not retry 1.2 without a new reason, and read the value first.","evidence":["F33","F24","F45"],"status":"verified","trap":"1.1 -> 1.15 lost once (F24: saved/deal 0.2947 -> 0.2905) and won once (F33: 0.2981 -> 0.3195), so a single result on this number is weak. 1.15 -> 1.2 was not taken (F45: saved/deal 0.3619 -> 0.3536) even though close rate rose (0.617 -> 0.678).","status_note":""},{"rule":"MAX_RAISE: the only result judged on buyer points/h is the 0.4 -> 0.35 win (F46, +3%). Read the value now and leave it. 0.3 was not taken twice and 0.5 once, so do not retry those.","evidence":["F46","F29","F35","F27","F44","F21"],"status":"verified","trap":"0.4 -> 0.35 lost on F29 and F35, then won on F46, so it is hour-sensitive and one result is thin. 0.4 -> 0.3 had saved/deal up in F44 (0.3472 -> 0.3535) but close rate down (0.725 -> 0.71), and it was still not taken.","status_note":""},{"rule":"Leave C_CAP alone. 0.6 -> 0.55 was not taken five times and the supervisor stopped the third trial, so do not restart it. Since F30, grade C needs a warranty and the C_CAP price clause is dropped, so the number matters even less.","evidence":["F13","F17","F18","F28","F36","F20","F30"],"status":"verified","trap":"At 0.55 close rate rises (F17: 0.598 -> 0.683; F36: 0.613 -> 0.691), which looks good, but surplus/order or saved/deal fell (F17: 23094 -> 11281; F28: 0.2972 -> 0.2741).","status_note":""},{"rule":"Do not add more reweighting or penalty terms to candidates() ranking for the buyer without paid-sales evidence. The recent ones expected gains and measured losses on saved/deal or paid sales. Check which of them still run, and read what is live before touching ranking.","evidence":["F12","F26","F37","F39","F41","F42"],"status":"verified","trap":"A \'kept\' label is not a win. F39 was kept at -6% saved/deal (expected +1%) and the supervisor later reverted it (F41). F42 was reverted at -4%. F37 (-2%) and F26 (-2%) were also kept despite expecting +3% and +5%. F12 measured -10% on paid/h against +4% expected.","status_note":""},{"rule":"Keep the close_gap price-tier overrides (200k or more in F8, 300k or more in F19). Treat the global CLOSE_GAP as unsettled: read its value first and do not cite either global 0.11 -> 0.12 step as settled.","evidence":["F8","F19","F14","F11"],"status":"unverified","trap":"The tier overrides won big (F8 +243%, F19 +65%) but on the older surplus/order metric, not saved/deal or board points, so the evidence is weak. The global 0.11 -> 0.12 step lost in F11 (surplus/order 24947 -> 21630) and won in F14 (8615 -> 14245), so neither result settles it.","status_note":""}]}'
