[11/10 06:09:57] HARNESS: try 1: 7.9 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [{"rule": "Judge every forum change alone, on its own closed 2 h window, by the forum rating (0-1, not a percentile) and by which posts draw dislike stances. Never keep or revert a forum change on forum_votes_post read as the hour before against the hour after: that reading follows the hour of day and is weak. Make no other forum change in the same window.", "evidence": ["F3", "F4"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "11/05 09:22 was reverted on -20% and 11/05 10:57 was kept despite -9%. Both were raw before/after readings (UNVERIFIED), so neither call shows what the change did and both could be wrong."}, {"rule": "The narrowed note() in forum_r3.py (top 4 shops with 2+ settles, last 2 refs per shown shop) is not disproven. It may be retried as the only forum change in its window and judged on the forum rating and on which posts draw dislike stances.", "evidence": ["F3"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Treating the revert (forum_votes_post -20%) as proof the change was bad. That figure is a weak raw reading, so a good change may have been discarded."}, {"rule": "Treat the cap on our_deals posts (none if either of our last two posts was our_deals, about 1 post in 3) as unproven. Do not tune the cap on its raw reading; check whether our_deals posts are among those that draw dislike stances, and judge any change to the cap alone on the forum rating.", "evidence": ["F4"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "It was kept with +15% expected against -9% measured, on a weak raw reading. \'Kept\' is not \'helped\', and 14/14 tests passing only shows the code runs."}, {"rule": "The posting cadence is fixed by code at the market\'s limit of 310 s (it was 600 s before 11/06 15:01), so it is not a lever for the team. Put forum effort into post quality, meaning finding the stances that draw dislikes, and never trade quality for count.", "evidence": ["F5"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Assuming more posts mean more votes or a higher rating. The 11/06 15:01 change has no verdict, and posts are only a tenth of the buyer\'s ALL."}, {"rule": "Do not credit the code-built ledger prices or the code-built, vote-weighted forum kinds with any gain: neither has a verdict. Any later change should be made alone in its window so it gets its own verdict on board points per hour.", "evidence": ["F1", "F2"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Layering changes on these two foundations in the same hours gives MIXED windows, which are no verdict, so nobody can say which change moved board points."}]}'
