[11/10 06:10:22] HARNESS: try 1: 8.4 s, exit 0, answer '{"proposal": {}, "why": "The shop change slot is busy until 07:04 with the floor_frac 0.65 -> 0.63 verdict pending, and the supervisor\'s rule is one shop change at a time, so any shop number I proposed now would be held. I am holding every number at its current value, and I am queuing stuck_hours 5 for the next free slot, which is not in my key list.", "ideas": ["Our 300k+ share of paid sales is 22% in the last 6 h, against 56-84% for the top-revenue shops (inextro, seochanit, 25620027). Our 300k+ units are mostly slow stock held near cost, so no number can fix the mix quickly; the fix is to stop buying slow 300k+ SKUs (L3), not to add depth to them.", "Forum: all top posts carry +8, so our rating of 0.911 is lost on dislike stances. Reading which of our posts draw dislikes, and changing the stance rather than the post count, is a non-number lever that the supervisor\'s rule 6 already asks for."], "lessons_used": ["L2", "L3"]}'
[11/10 06:10:25] HARNESS: try 1: 11.5 s, exit 0, answer '{"proposal": {}, "recruit": null, "why": "All buyer numbers except CAP are already at the values their verdict ledgers support (FIRM_GAP 0.07 per L1, FOOD_MARGIN 1.15 per L2, MAX_RAISE 0.35 per L3), and MAX_TRIES, SCOUTS and CLOSE_GAP are at their bounds. The one CAP trial (0.75 -> 0.8) was followed by deals/h falling 184 -> 132 and settled/h 156 -> 108, and the recruit with FIRM_GAP 0.05 lost its A/B (saved/deal 0.3818 -> 0.3673), so no buyer change has new evidence behind it.", "ideas": ["Grade C is the weak goods line: 17.6% of C goods break within 24 h against 1.6% for A, and the policy refused 9 C purchases for grade. Buying C only with a warranty, or not at all, is a purchase-policy change rather than a number, and it should be judged on paid sales and the break rate.", "The shelf-life refusals (5 in the last 100 payments) show the buyer is buying goods that will not last long enough for the payment policy. Choosing SKUs with more shelf life left at purchase, instead of tuning haggling numbers, would target that loss directly."], "lessons_used": ["L1", "L2", "L3", "L5"]}'
