 a reverted code change as written. Re-test it alone and judge it on board_pts_h with the 2 h verdict and the fast guard.", "evidence": ["F42", "F50", "F53", "F64", "F80", "F84"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Each revert rests on a raw before/after read (weak), e.g. F42 shop_margin_h -32% and F64 shop_deals_h -43%. Treating them as settled would bar changes that were never fairly judged, and retrying them blindly would repeat a change that may have been harmful."},\n{"rule": "Do not read a number change\'s raw margin move as evidence when other changes fell in the same hours. Change one shop number at a time and wait for its closed window before the next.", "evidence": ["F92", "F94", "F95"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "stock_value 130M, reserve_cash, warranty_hours and final_frac moved within hours of each other, so the raw margin reads +578%, +717% and -48% belong to no single change. All of 11/5-11/9\'s shop number verdicts were MIXED, so they give no reason to hold or to try any number. This lesson rests on the record\'s MIXED labels and the supervisor\'s order, not on a measured effect."},\n{"rule": "Do not size a stock cap from our own recent sales rate when that rate was depressed by a restock bug. Check first whether the shop was buying the market\'s best sellers.", "evidence": ["F26", "F20", "F24"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "F26 capped 300k+ stock at 4 h of our own 300k+ sales (2.2 an hour). Those sales were low because restock did not buy the market\'s best sellers until the ranking and room fixes of 12:46-13:48, so the cap would have locked in the bug. The supervisor reverted it."},\n{"rule": "Do not count on the food shelf-life change (selling food categories need min(min_shelf_hours, 48)) to cut refusals. Check shelf_refused_h on a closed window before building on it.", "evidence": ["F77"], "status": "contradicted", "trap": "It was kept, but shelf_refused_h was expected -30% and measured +21%, the wrong way. The read was raw before/after 