[11/10 14:57:13] HARNESS: try 1: 12.5 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [{"rule": "Judge each shop number alone: change one number at a time and keep stock_value, restock, warranty and final_frac changes out of its window. Only single-change windows gave readable verdicts (F70, F71, F72); every earlier shop number verdict was MIXED and is no evidence.", "evidence": ["F70", "F71", "F72", "F73"], "status": "verified", "trap": "F73 (stuck_hours 5 -> 4) was MIXED because stock_value 130000000 -> 200000000.0 changed in the same hours, so it gave no verdict. Moving stock_value alongside a number wastes the window, as did the 96 mixed verdicts of 11/5-11/9."}, {"rule": "Lower floor_frac_food was the one floor move that paid when judged alone: floor_frac_food 0.65 -> 0.62 raised shop points/h net of the market by 112% (178/6046 -> 218/6087 sales), and the raw verdict agreed.", "evidence": ["F70"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Reading this as \'floors should go lower everywhere\' is not supported (see the goods floor lesson). It is one verified food reading, so check the value now before moving it again (order 5)."}, {"rule": "Do not expect gains from the goods floor: floor_frac 0.65 -> 0.63 made no difference beyond noise (value share -14%, raw margin -14%; 293/6225 -> 303/6331 sales). Spend windows on other levers.", "evidence": ["F71"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Copying the food floor result onto goods is not supported. Cutting floors inside a bundle (floor_frac 0.67 -> 0.45 on 11/09 06:43) was undone whole at 09:21 after it cut paid sales."}, {"rule": "Shortening stuck_hours to free stuck capital faster helped when judged alone: stuck_hours 6 -> 5 raised shop points/h net of the market by 63% (314/6377 -> 294/6145 sales), and the raw verdict agreed. This fits the top-10 aim of more paid sales from the same capital.", "evidence": ["F72"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The follow-up 5 -> 4 (F73) has no verdict because stock_value changed in the same hours. Do not read it as confirming or refuting the 5 -> 4 step; re-judge it alone."}, {"rule": "Never ship a multi-knob bundle: the 11/09 06:43 change moved ask_frac, floor_frac, min_margin, step, max_turns and the food asks together, and was undone at 09:21 after it cut paid sales.", "evidence": ["F57", "F58", "F59", "F60"], "status": "verified", "trap": "An A/B that wins on margin per talk can still lose on paid sales (the 06:43 playbook cut them 65% per the standing orders). Judge on board points per hour, not margin per talk. Undo steps were themselves partial and overlapping (F58, F59, F60), which made the window unreadable."}, {"rule": "Goods ask changes by themselves rarely drive results: the IKEA-style fast-concession playbook lost margin and deals against the strategy\'s own settings, so keep the slower, more-turns haggling settings.", "evidence": ["F6"], "status": "verified", "trap": "F6 was judged on margin per talk, which standing order 1 calls only a part of the aim, and it is from 11/05. Use it only as a warning against fast concessions and fewer turns, not as a value to set."}]}'
