[11/10 15:13:57] HARNESS: try 1: 34.4 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [\n{"rule": "FIRM_GAP: do not step it down from 0.07, and do not step it up to 0.09 without a new reason. Read its value first (standing order 5). Raising it won twice (0.03 -> 0.05, 0.05 -> 0.07). Lowering it from 0.07 was not taken three times, the last on points/h.", "evidence": ["F23", "F25", "F31", "F40", "F50", "F52"], "status": "verified", "trap": "A step down can look fine on one part and still lose. On 11/07 10:29 saved/deal rose 0.2949 -> 0.2988 while close rate fell 0.698 -> 0.655. On 11/09 23:48 saved/deal fell 0.3818 -> 0.3673 and points/h fell 35%. The 0.07 -> 0.09 step showed only +2% points/h with saved difference -0.2 sd, so it is noise, not a reason to try again."},\n{"rule": "CAP: read its value now. Do not raise it back to 0.8, since 0.8 -> 0.75 won (11/08 21:51) and 0.75 -> 0.8 was not taken on points/h. Treat 0.7 as untested, because the supervisor undid it within minutes with no verdict.", "evidence": ["F43", "F53", "F38", "F47", "F48"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Older CAP results flip with the hour: 0.85 -> 0.8 was not taken twice (F22, F32) and then won (F38). The latest evidence against going up is thin: points/h 0.000513 -> 0.000487 (-5%), saved difference +0.2 sd. Do not read it as proof that lower is always better, and do not treat 0.7 as ruled out."},\n{"rule": "MAX_RAISE: 0.4 -> 0.35 won once on points/h (+3%). Going lower to 0.3 was not taken three times, and raising to 0.5 was not taken. Do not go below 0.35 or above 0.4 without a new reason. Read its value now.", "evidence": ["F46", "F54", "F27", "F44", "F21"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Differences are tiny and the sign flips between windows. 0.4 -> 0.35 was not taken on 11/07 07:25 and 11/08 08:49 (saved/deal 0.3316 -> 0.3228) and then won on 11/09 10:35. On 11/10 08:39 0.35 -> 0.3 gave +1% points/h with close rate 0.775 -> 0.664 and was still not taken."},\n{"rule": "FOOD_MARGIN: leave it where it is and do not retry 1.2. The 1.1 -> 1.15 step won once (11/07 23:45), and 1.15 -> 1.2 was not taken.", "evidence": ["F33", "F24", "F45"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The evidence is thin and hour-sensitive. 1.1 -> 1.15 lost on 11/06 17:22 (saved/deal 0.2947 -> 0.2905) and won on 11/07 23:45 (0.2981 -> 0.3195). 1.15 -> 1.2 had saved/deal 0.3619 -> 0.3536 although close rate rose 0.617 -> 0.678."},\n{"rule": "Leave C_CAP alone. 0.6 -> 0.55 was not taken five times and the supervisor stopped the third trial, so do not restart it. Since 11/07 10:14 grade C needs a warranty and the C_CAP price clause is dropped, so the number matters even less.", "evidence": ["F13", "F17", "F18", "F28", "F36", "F20", "F30"], "status": "verified", "trap": "At 0.55 the close rate rises (11/05 19:30: 0.598 -> 0.683; 11/08 11:54: 0.613 -> 0.691), which looks good. But surplus/order fell on 11/05 19:30 (23094 -> 11281) and saved/deal fell on 11/07 05:02 (0.2972 -> 0.2741), so a higher close rate alone proves nothing."},\n{"rule": "Do not add more reweighting or penalty terms to the buyer candidates() ranking without paid-sales evidence. First check which earlier terms still run and read the current code. Most ranking terms measured at or below zero against their expected gain.", "evidence": ["F12", "F37", "F39", "F41", "F42", "F51", "F55"], "status": "verified", "trap": "A \'kept\' label is not a win. 11/08 16:36 was kept at -6% saved/deal (expected +1%) and the supervisor reverted it (11/08 19:53). 11/08 21:36 was reverted at -4%. 11/08 11:55 (-2%) and 11/10 09:28 (-2%, expected +3%) were kept with negative measures. 11/09 21:40 was kept at +1% against an expected +4%. 11/05 00:24 measured -10% on buyer_paid_h."},\n{"rule": "Judge buyer changes on buyer points/h (the board\'s terms) over closed windows, never on a part (seconds per order, close rate, saved/deal) alone. Do not expect early walk-away or early cancel rules to shorten talks. Treat points/h moves of 1-3% as noise. Do not hold or ask for an A/B where the standing orders no longer require one.", "evidence": ["F46", "F50", "F52", "F53", "F54", "F16", "F49"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Parts point the wrong way. On 11/10 08:39 close rate fell 0.775 -> 0.664 with points/h +1%. On 11/09 23:48 points/h fell 35% while close rate fell 0.631 -> 0.542. The two early-exit rules were kept but missed what they promised: 11/05 17:22 expected -8% secs/order and got +1%, and 11/09 16:37 expected -5% and got +13%."},\n{"rule": "Where a lever pays, look at price-tiered settings before touching global numbers. A wider close gap on high-priced SKUs gave the largest measured gains (+243% for 200k or more, +65% for 300k or more at a tighter gap). Treat this as a lead to re-check on points/h, not as proof.", "evidence": ["F8", "F19"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Both were measured on surplus/order, not on board points, and before 11/9 11:13. Close gap is not monotone either: 0.11 -> 0.12 was not taken on 11/05 00:07 (close rate 0.705 -> 0.652) and kept on 11/05 11:12, so a global move on it is a coin flip."}\n]}'
