[11/10 16:03:10] HARNESS: try 1: 19.7 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [{"rule": "Keep the heat-scaled depth for a 150-300k goods SKU at DEAR_HOT or more, capped at 2x dear_depth (5x stays for 300k+). It is the only depth change with a verdict on the board\'s terms.", "evidence": ["F90"], "status": "verified", "trap": "It measured shop_revenue_h +398% and shop points/h +613%, net of the market\'s own change (paid value x1.05, count x1.08), against +8% expected. Do not forecast gains of that size for the next depth change. Other numbers moved in nearby hours (F89, F91), so do not credit the whole gain to this one line either."}, {"rule": "The hot 300k+ heat cap (5x dear_depth, up to 20 units a line) is in force but has no verdict of its own. Before stacking more depth on 300k+ lines, change one shop number at a time and judge it alone on board_pts_h with the 2 h verdict and the fast guard. No A/B is needed.", "evidence": ["F84", "F88", "F90"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "The raise from 3x to 5x was reverted on raw before/after shop_margin_h (-20%, 11/09 08:06), which reads the hour of day and is weak. The supervisor restored it at 11:18 without a verdict. Reading either move as proof the cap is good or bad would be wrong, and F90\'s verdict covers the 150-300k band, not the 300k+ cap."}, {"rule": "Do not read a number change\'s raw margin move as evidence when other changes fell in the same hours. Change one shop number at a time, read its value now first, and judge it alone on board_pts_h on a closed window.", "evidence": ["F92", "F94", "F95", "F97", "F99", "F100"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "stock_value, reserve_cash, warranty_hours, final_frac and ask_frac_food moved within hours of each other (11/09 13:17-15:11), then stock_value moved three times on 11/10 (F97, F99, F100). Those rows are MIXED or have no verdict, so no single move can be credited or blamed. Bundling them leaves nothing to learn from."}, {"rule": "Do not treat a revert on raw before/after margin or deals as proof that an idea is bad, and do not retry a reverted code change as written. Re-test it alone and judge it on board_pts_h with the 2 h verdict and the fast guard.", "evidence": ["F42", "F50", "F53", "F64", "F80", "F84"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Each revert rests on a raw before/after read (weak), e.g. 11/07 06:54 shop_margin_h -32% and 11/08 05:01 shop_deals_h -43%. Treating them as settled would bar changes that were never fairly judged. Retrying one verbatim would repeat a change the team already withdrew."}, {"rule": "Keep the limits on slow (sku_score under DEAR_HOT) 300k+ stock: 1-unit depth, the slow_held cap of 40, and slow units excluded from the stock_value cap and goods_frac room. Do not credit them with the gains read beside them.", "evidence": ["F38", "F57", "F66"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "All three were judged on raw before/after (weak) with other changes nearby. On 11/08 08:33 F66 read shop_margin_h +252% against +5% expected, a size that shows the read came from the hour of day, not the rule. Weak evidence cuts both ways: it does not show these limits help, and it does not show they hurt."}, {"rule": "Do not size a stock cap from our own recent sales rate when that rate was depressed by a restock bug. Check first whether the shop was buying the market\'s best sellers.", "evidence": ["F26", "F24"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "On 11/06 14:35 a cap of 4 h of our own 300k+ sales (2.2 an hour) was reverted by the supervisor. Those sales were low because restock did not buy the market\'s best sellers until the ranking and room fixes of 12:46-13:48. The cap would have locked in the bug\'s effect. The revert read is raw before/after, so it is weak."}, {"rule": "Do not count on the food shelf-life change (selling food categories need min(min_shelf_hours, 48)) to cut refusals. Judge it on board_pts_h on a closed window, because shelf_refused_h is only a part.", "evidence": ["F77"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "It was kept, but shelf_refused_h was expected -30% and measured +21%, the wrong way. The read was raw before/after (weak), so it is not proof of harm either. Judging it on a part metric instead of board_pts_h would repeat the mistake the supervisor\'s aim rule warns against."}]}'
