[11/10 16:03:40] HARNESS: try 1: 10.6 s, exit 0, answer '{"proposal": {"FOOD_MARGIN": 1.10}, "recruit": null, "why": "The supervisor\'s shelf-life check found 119 of 1,000 unpaid talks were refused at 1.02x or more of use_within, and food deals save 0.31-0.44 of list against our 0.297 mean, so a 0.05 step to 1.10 (the largest allowed) should win some of those deals. CAP 0.70 stays off the table until 11/11 12:26 because the last trial lost, and the rival buyer teams\' rewards (0.036-0.042) are too close to justify a recruit style change.", "ideas": ["The hot high-value goods are capped by goods_room (stock_value vs goods held at cost), not by any buyer number. Only a shop-side judged change can lift it, and the shop change slot is busy until 16:24.", "Forum rating (0.912 vs the leader\'s 0.934) moves on which posts draw dislike stances, not on post count. Find the posts that draw dislikes and keep their quality, since the post rate is already capped by the 310 s limit."], "lessons_used": []}'
[11/10 16:03:41] HARNESS: try 1: 12.0 s, exit 0, answer '{"proposal": {}, "why": "No shop number changes now: the shop change slot is busy with stock_value 160M->130M until 16:24, and reserve_cash 10M->6M until 16:21, so any move would confound both verdicts (rule 3). The queued reserve_cash 10M->7M is stale because the value in force is now 6M (rule 5), and stock at cost (149.8M) already exceeds stock_value (130M), so restock is blocked by the goods room, not by any number I could move this cycle.", "ideas": ["Our mean paid sale is 98k against 853k at inextro and 209k at moss-and-oak, and only 12% of our sales are 300k+ against 36-84% for the top shops, so revenue per hour falls even when deals hold. No number makes a buyer pay more for cheap goods; only stocking dearer lines does, and the goods room currently blocks that. Once the verdict clears, the question is whether to free room by selling aged stock.", "475 of our 862 units are older than 24 h, and that aged stock is what fills the goods room. The demand table shows the top SKUs (G022ce883, Gef4d3036, G74e686be) well above the rest, but no number chooses which aged units sell first. Clearing those units at or above cost, under rule 7\'s stuck-capital exception, is the only lever that reopens room for the high-demand dear lines."], "lessons_used": []}'
[11/10 16:03:41] HARNESS: try 1: 12.1 s, exit 0, answer '{"proposal": {}, "ab": {"param": "floor_frac_food", "kind": "food", "value": 0.6}, "recruit": null, "playbook": "none", "why": "The shop slot is busy until 16:24 with stock_value and reserve_cash changes still unjudged, and the last several shop-number verdicts were MIXED, so I am not stacking another shop change on top. Food talks open at the floor 78% of the time, so floor_frac_food is the one number that reaches most food sales; L2 found a 0.65 to 0.62 cut paid when judged alone, and a 0.6 arm is a small single-number test, with L1 keeping it readable.", "ideas": ["Goods talks mostly open at the warranty floor or the market line (51% at floor, 47% on the market line), so no per-negotiation number reaches them. The goods gap to market (price_list 0.605 vs goods median 0.651) is a market-line and stock question, not a floor question, per L3.", "The board\'s SCAM review says our receipts were read as forged. Before the midterm, check that every receipt names the shop\'s real identity and that every grade and claim matches the certificate, since a single flagged receipt costs stars and the honesty rule."], "lessons_used": ["L1", "L2", "L3"]}'
