[11/10 18:28:30] HARNESS: try 1: 29.2 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [\n{"rule": "FIRM_GAP: do not lower it. 0.07 -> 0.05 cut buyer points/h from 0.000582 to 0.00038 (-35%, F52). Raising to 0.09 was not taken either (points/h +2%, saved difference -0.2 sd, F50), so there is no gain there. Earlier steps up (0.03 -> 0.05, 0.05 -> 0.07) won on saved/deal. Read the value now (standing order 5) and leave it unless you have a new reason, not a retest.", "evidence": ["F23", "F25", "F31", "F40", "F50", "F52"], "status": "verified", "trap": "A step down can look fine on a part and still lose. On 11/07 10:29 saved/deal rose 0.2949 -> 0.2988 while close rate fell 0.698 -> 0.655. On 11/09 23:48 points/h fell 35%. Judging on saved/deal alone would have kept it."},\n{"rule": "CAP: do not raise it. 0.8 -> 0.75 won (saved/deal 0.33 -> 0.3498, F43) and 0.75 -> 0.8 was not taken on points/h (-5%, F53). Going lower was tested too: 0.75 -> 0.7 was not taken (points/h +2%, saved difference +0.5 sd, F56), so it is no longer untested. The supervisor\'s 0.7 step was undone within minutes with no verdict (F47, F48). Read the value now and leave it.", "evidence": ["F43", "F53", "F56", "F38", "F47", "F48"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Older CAP results flip with the hour: 0.85 -> 0.8 was not taken twice (F22, F32) and then won (F38). A +2% points/h move at +0.5 sd looks like a win but was not taken, so treat it as noise and do not chase it."},\n{"rule": "MAX_RAISE: 0.4 -> 0.35 won once on points/h (+3%, F46). Going lower to 0.3 was not taken (F54, F44, F27) and raising to 0.5 was not taken (F21). Do not move it below 0.35 or above 0.4 without a new reason. Read its value now.", "evidence": ["F46", "F54", "F44", "F27", "F21"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Differences are tiny and the sign flips between windows. 0.4 -> 0.35 was not taken on 11/07 07:25 and 11/08 08:49 (F29, F35) and then won on 11/09 10:35. One window does not settle this number, and a +1% points/h move (F54) is noise."},\n{"rule": "FOOD_MARGIN: leave it alone and do not retry 1.2. The 1.1 -> 1.15 step won once (F33) and 1.15 -> 1.2 was not taken (F45).", "evidence": ["F33", "F24", "F45"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The evidence is thin and sits on saved/deal, not points/h. 1.1 -> 1.15 lost on 11/06 17:22 (0.2947 -> 0.2905, F24) and won on 11/07 23:45 (0.2981 -> 0.3195). Do not read a flip as a trend."},\n{"rule": "Leave C_CAP alone. 0.6 -> 0.55 was not taken five times (F13, F17, F18, F28, F36) and the supervisor stopped the third trial, so do not restart it (F20). Since 11/07 10:14 grade C needs a warranty and the C_CAP price clause is dropped, so the number matters even less (F30).", "evidence": ["F13", "F17", "F18", "F28", "F36", "F20", "F30"], "status": "verified", "trap": "At 0.55 the close rate rises (11/05 19:30: 0.598 -> 0.683; 11/08 11:54: 0.613 -> 0.691), which looks good. But surplus/order fell on 11/05 19:30 (23094 -> 11281), and saved/deal fell on 11/07 05:02 (0.2972 -> 0.2741). A higher close rate bought with lower value is a loss."},\n{"rule": "Do not add more reweighting or penalty terms to the buyer candidates() ranking without paid-sales evidence. Check which earlier terms still run and read the current code first. Nearly every ranking term measured at or below zero against its expectation: F12 -10% (expected +4%), F37 -2%, F39 -6%, F42 -4%, F55 -2%. F51 reached only +1% against +4% expected. F57 has no verdict yet.", "evidence": ["F12", "F37", "F39", "F41", "F42", "F51", "F55", "F57"], "status": "verified", "trap": "A \'kept\' label is not a win. F39 was kept at -6% saved/deal (expected +1%) and the supervisor reverted it (F41). F42 was reverted at -4%. Terms stack, so a new one can silently undo an old one."},\n{"rule": "Judge buyer changes on buyer points/h over closed windows, never on a part (seconds per order, close rate, saved/deal) alone. Early walk-away or early cancel rules did not shorten talks (F16: -8% expected, +1% measured; F49: -5% expected, +13% measured). Buyer number nudges near the current values moved points/h by 5% or less (F50, F53, F54, F56). Treat such moves as noise and spend effort on the shop\'s book and revenue (standing order 3). Do not demand an A/B for them.", "evidence": ["F46", "F50", "F52", "F53", "F54", "F56", "F16", "F49"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Parts point the wrong way. On 11/10 08:39 close rate fell 0.775 -> 0.664 with points/h +1%. On 11/09 23:48 points/h fell 35% while close rate fell 0.631 -> 0.542. Optimising a part, or fiddling with buyer numbers at a plateau, wastes cycles."}\n]}'
