e number."}, {"rule": "Do not treat a revert on raw before/after margin or deals as proof that an idea is bad, and do not retry a reverted code change as written. Re-test it alone and judge it on board_pts_h with the 2 h verdict and the fast guard.", "evidence": ["F42", "F50", "F53", "F64", "F80", "F84"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Each revert rests on a raw before/after read, which is weak. Examples: shop_margin_h -32% on 11/07 06:54 and shop_deals_h -43% on 11/08 05:01. Treating them as settled would bar changes that were never fairly judged, but retrying them unchanged repeats the same read."}, {"rule": "Do not size a stock cap from our own recent sales rate when that rate was depressed by a restock bug. Check first whether the shop was buying the market\'s best sellers.", "evidence": ["F26", "F24"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "On 11/06 14:35 a cap of 4 h of our own 300k+ sales (2.2 an hour) was reverted by the supervisor. Those sales were low because restock had not bought the market\'s best sellers until the ranking and room fix of 11/06 12:46-13:48, so the cap would have locked in the bug. The revert read was raw before/after, so this is weak."}, {"rule": "Do not count on the food shelf-life change (selling food categories need min(min_shelf_hours, 48)) to cut refusals. Judge it on board_pts_h on a closed window, because shelf_refused_h is only a part.", "evidence": ["F77"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "It was kept, but shelf_refused_h was expected -30% and measured +21%, the wrong way. The read was raw before/after (weak), so it is not proof of harm either. Judging it on a part rather than on board_pts_h would mislead."}]}'
