[11/10 21:43:18] HARNESS: try 1: 36.1 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [\n{"rule": "FIRM_GAP: do not lower it. 0.07 -> 0.05 cut buyer points/h from 0.000582 to 0.00038 (-35%, saved difference -1.1 sd, close rate 0.631 -> 0.542) on 11/09 23:48. Raising to 0.09 was not taken either (points/h +2%, saved difference -0.2 sd), so neither direction paid on points/h. Older steps up (0.03 -> 0.05, 0.05 -> 0.07) won on saved/deal only, so they are weak evidence.", "evidence": ["F52", "F50", "F23", "F25", "F31", "F40"], "status": "verified", "trap": "A step down can look fine on a part and still lose. On 11/07 10:29 saved/deal rose 0.2949 -> 0.2988 while close rate fell 0.698 -> 0.655, and the later points/h reading showed -35%. Do not judge it on saved/deal alone."},\n{"rule": "CAP: 0.8 -> 0.75 won (saved/deal 0.33 -> 0.3498, 11/08 21:51). Going back up, 0.75 -> 0.8, was not taken on points/h (-5%, 11/10 03:43). Going down, 0.75 -> 0.7, was not taken either (points/h +2%, saved difference +0.5 sd, 11/10 12:26), and the supervisor\'s 0.7 step was undone (F48). Do not recommend 0.7 or 0.8 without a new reason.", "evidence": ["F43", "F53", "F56", "F47", "F48", "F38"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Older CAP results flip with the hour: 0.85 -> 0.8 was not taken twice (11/06 12:28, 11/07 13:15) and then won on 11/08 14:39, so the same step gave both signs. A +2% points/h move at +0.5 sd looks like a win but was not taken."},\n{"rule": "MAX_RAISE: 0.4 -> 0.35 won once on points/h (+3%, 11/09 10:35). Going lower, 0.35 -> 0.3, was not taken (points/h +1%, 11/10 08:39), and 0.4 -> 0.3 was not taken twice (11/09 01:09, 11/07 02:12). Raising to 0.5 was not taken (11/06 09:13). Read its value now before touching it.", "evidence": ["F46", "F54", "F44", "F27", "F21"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Differences are tiny and the sign flips between windows: 0.4 -> 0.35 was not taken on 11/07 07:25 and 11/08 08:49 and then won on 11/09 10:35. One window\'s sign is not a trend."},\n{"rule": "FOOD_MARGIN: do not retry 1.2 (1.15 -> 1.2 not taken, 11/09 07:33). The evidence on 1.1 vs 1.15 conflicts: 1.1 -> 1.15 won on saved/deal (0.2981 -> 0.3195, 11/07 23:45) but lost on 11/06 17:22, and the newest row, 1.15 -> 1.1, read points/h +9% at +1.6 sd (saved/deal 0.3722 -> 0.3889) yet was labelled not taken (11/10 16:04). Treat 1.15 as unproven and do not restate it as a win.", "evidence": ["F33", "F24", "F45", "F57"], "status": "contradicted", "trap": "The old win rests on saved/deal, a part, and the newer row points the other way on points/h. Quoting \'raise it to 1.15\' as settled would repeat a conclusion newer facts undercut."},\n{"rule": "Leave C_CAP alone and do not restart the 0.6 -> 0.55 trial: it was not taken five times, and the supervisor stopped the third trial (11/06 05:36). Since 11/07 10:14 grade C needs a warranty and the C_CAP price clause is dropped, so the number matters less.", "evidence": ["F13", "F17", "F18", "F28", "F36", "F20", "F30"], "status": "verified", "trap": "At 0.55 the close rate rises (11/05 19:30: 0.598 -> 0.683; 11/08 11:54: 0.613 -> 0.691), which looks good. But surplus/order fell on 11/05 19:30 (23094 -> 11281) and saved/deal fell on 11/07 05:02 (0.2972 -> 0.2741), so the extra closes bought less."},\n{"rule": "Do not add reweighting or penalty terms to the buyer candidates() ranking without paid-sales evidence; read the current code to see which terms still run. Nearly every ranking term measured at or below its expectation: F12 -10% paid_h, F37 -2%, F39 -6% (reverted), F42 -4% (reverted), F55 -2%. The only matches were F58, lowering the short-shelf-life food penalty 0.3 -> 0.05 (+3% close rate), and F51 (+1% close rate). Removing a penalty has paid more than adding one.", "evidence": ["F12", "F37", "F39", "F41", "F42", "F51", "F55", "F58"], "status": "verified", "trap": "A \'kept\' label is not a win: F37, F39 and F30 were kept at -2%, -6% and -2% saved/deal against positive expectations, and F39 had to be reverted by the supervisor (F41). Terms stack, so a new one can cancel an older one."},\n{"rule": "Judge buyer changes on buyer points/h over closed windows, never on a part (seconds per order, close rate, saved/deal) alone. Early walk-away and early cancel rules did not shorten talks (F16: -8% expected, +1% measured; F49: -5% expected, +13% measured), so do not propose them for speed.", "evidence": ["F46", "F50", "F52", "F54", "F16", "F49"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Parts point the wrong way. On 11/10 08:39 close rate fell 0.775 -> 0.664 while points/h rose +1%. On 11/09 23:48 points/h fell 35% and close rate fell 0.631 -> 0.542. Choosing by close rate or saved/deal gives the wrong call in both directions."},\n{"rule": "Per-price-tier close_gap on dear SKUs is the buyer\'s largest code gain so far: close_gap 0.15 for list 200k or more gave surplus/order +243% (F8), and 0.06 for 300k or more gave +65% (F19). Look for similar tier-specific settings before touching global numbers; the global CLOSE_GAP 0.11 -> 0.12 gave opposite results (F11 not taken, F14 kept).", "evidence": ["F8", "F19", "F11", "F14"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "These rows are A/B in the same hours but measured on surplus/order, a part and not points/h, and they date from 11/04-11/06, before the board-point verdicts. Confirm on points/h before building more on them."}\n]}'
