[11/11 01:32:54] HARNESS: try 1: 10.4 s, exit 0, answer '{"proposal": {}, "ab": null, "recruit": null, "playbook": "none", "why": "The shop change slot is busy until 03:01 with the stock_value change, and L1 says one shop number per window is the only way to read a verdict, so any shop number I add now would confound it. The open_gap and market_ask tests are already decided or running (open_gap was reverted by the fast guard, and market_ask 0.9 vs 1.0 is still open), so a new A/B now would collide with them.", "ideas": ["Restock: stop buying 300k+ A lines whose median cost (0.678 of list) sits at or above the A market line (0.71 of list minus margin). Per the 11/10 22:00 audit, A goods earn 1.8% margin, so skipping or shallowing those lines should add more Book than any floor move. Judge it on margin per unit bought, not on count (L3: floors gave no gain on goods).", "Warranty-asking 300k+ talks close at 7.9% and 59% leave before an offer, versus 16% close and 29% leave for non-askers. The gap points to the first offer\'s timing and price for buyers who ask for a warranty, not to the warranty hours (which the supervisor has fixed at 72 h)."], "lessons_used": ["L1", "L3"]}'
