[11/11 03:40:33] HARNESS: try 1: 19.4 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [\n{"rule": "Judge each shop number alone: one change per window, with no stock_value, reserve_cash, restock-code or buyer-code change in its hours. Only the single-change windows of 11/10 (F70, F71, F72) gave readable verdicts. Every shop number verdict from 11/5 to 11/9 and the later rows F73-F75 are MIXED and prove nothing.", "evidence": ["F70", "F71", "F72", "F73", "F74", "F75"], "status": "verified", "trap": "F73 (stuck_hours 5 -> 4) shared its hours with stock_value 130000000 -> 200000000.0. F74 and F75 shared theirs with reserve_cash, stock_value and a buyer food-penalty change. Reading raw margin swings such as +497% or +717% as proof of a win is the mistake.", "status": "verified"},\n{"rule": "Lowering floor_frac_food paid once when judged alone: 0.65 -> 0.62 raised shop points/h net of the market by 112% (178/6046 -> 218/6087 sales), and the raw verdict agreed. Read the value now (order 5). Test any further food-floor move alone, and only when no other change is open.", "evidence": ["F70"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The later steps 0.62 -> 0.6 (F74) and 0.6 -> 0.58 (F75) are MIXED and unjudged. Counting them as a second or third win, or as proof that floors should keep falling, is unsupported."},\n{"rule": "The goods floor gave no gain: floor_frac 0.65 -> 0.63 made no difference beyond noise (value share -14%, raw margin -14%; 293/6225 -> 303/6331 sales). Look for board points on other levers, such as faster turns of capital, stuck stock or the edges table.", "evidence": ["F71"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Copying the food-floor win onto goods is not supported. The 11/09 06:43 floors bundle (F57, floor_frac 0.67 -> 0.45) was undone whole at 09:21 (F60)."},\n{"rule": "Releasing stuck stock sooner paid: stuck_hours 6 -> 5 raised shop points/h net of the market by 63% (314/6377 -> 294/6145 sales). The step 5 -> 4 is unjudged, so re-run it alone with stock_value held steady.", "evidence": ["F72", "F73"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Treating F73 as a verdict on 4 hours in either direction: it had stock_value 130000000 -> 200000000.0 in its hours and has none. Stuck goods now also follow the market line to 0.95 of cost (order 3), so any open window gains extra paid sales from that rule and the stuck_hours effect can be mis-credited."},\n{"rule": "Judge a playbook or bundle on board points per hour (paid sales, margin, revenue, buyer saved), never on margin per talk. The IKEA A/B (F6) was won by the strategy arm on margin per talk (13.7% against 8.8%), and the 06:43 floors/min_margin/max_turns bundle (F57) was undone whole (F60) for cutting paid sales.", "evidence": ["F6", "F57", "F60"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "F6 and the bundle rows predate the board-points judging and are weak evidence. Picking a winner on margin per talk can lose deals and board points."},\n{"rule": "Before moving a number, read its value now and move it in the direction you mean (order 5). Undo a bad move with a single, clearly labelled change.", "evidence": ["F8", "F9", "F10", "F58", "F59", "F63", "F64", "F65"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "On 11/05 ask_frac_food went 0.72 -> 0.75 -> 0.8 -> 0.72 in the same hours, and on 11/09 ask_frac_food went 0.7 -> 0.75 -> 0.7 within a minute (F63, F64, F65). The churn left every window MIXED and unreadable."}\n]}'
