\n{"rule": "MAX_RAISE: 0.35 won once on points/h (0.4 -> 0.35, +3%, 11/09 10:35). Going lower, 0.35 -> 0.3, was not taken (points/h +1%, close rate 0.775 -> 0.664, 11/10 08:39). 0.4 -> 0.3 was not taken twice (11/09 01:09, 11/07 02:12), and 0.4 -> 0.5 was not taken (11/06 09:13). Do not retry those steps; read the current value first.", "evidence": ["F46", "F54", "F44", "F27", "F21", "F29", "F35"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Differences are tiny and the sign flips between windows: 0.4 -> 0.35 was not taken on 11/07 07:25 and 11/08 08:49 and then won on 11/09 10:35. A single window\'s +1% or -1% is noise, so do not chase it.", "when": ["11/09 10:35", "11/10 08:39", "11/09 01:09", "11/07 02:12", "11/06 09:13", "11/07 07:25", "11/08 08:49"]},\n{"rule": "FOOD_MARGIN: do not retry 1.2 (1.15 -> 1.2 not taken, 11/09 07:33). 1.1 vs 1.15 is unresolved. 1.1 -> 1.15 won on saved/deal (0.2981 -> 0.3195, 11/07 23:45) but was not taken on 11/06 17:22. The newest row, 1.15 -> 1.1 (11/10 16:04), read points/h +9% (saved difference +1.6 sd) yet was still not taken, with close rate 0.851 -> 0.798. Read the current value before any move.", "evidence": ["F33", "F24", "F45", "F57"], "status": "contradicted", "trap": "The old win rests on saved/deal, a part, and the newest row points the other way on points/h. Quoting \'raise it to 1.15\' as settled would repeat a conclusion that newer evidence disputes; so would \'lower it to 1.1\' on one window.", "when": ["11/07 23:45", "11/06 17:22", "11/09 07:33", "11/10 16:04"]},\n{"rule": "CLOSE_GAP: the global 0.11 -> 0.12 step has no reliable verdict. It was not taken on 11/05 00:07 (close rate 0.705 -> 0.652) and kept on 11/05 11:12 (close rate 0.656 -> 0.723). Both rows judge parts (surplus/order, close rate) from before points/h was the metric. The only clear CLOSE_GAP wins are price-banded code changes: 0.15 for SKUs at 200k or more (surplus/order +243%) and 0.06 for 300k or more (+65%), both measured on surplus/order.", "evidence": ["F11", "F14", "F8", "F19"], "status": "contradicted", "trap": "Quoting either global CLOSE_GAP row alone as the answer: same step, same arms, opposite verdicts a few hours apart. The big wins were on surplus per order, not board points, so they do not prove a points/h gain.", "when": ["11/05 00:07", "11/05 11:12", "11/04 21:11", "11/06 02:41"]},\n{"rule": "C_CAP: leave it alone and do not restart the 0.6 -> 0.55 trial. It was not taken five times (11/05 02:44, 11/05 19:30, 11/06 02:24, 11/07 05:02, 11/08 11:54) and the supervisor stopped the third trial (11/06 05:36). Since 11/07 10:14 grade C is accepted only with a C_WARRANTY-hour warranty and the C_CAP price clause is dropped (behind a trial flag), so C_CAP matters less.", "evidence": ["F13", "F17", "F18", "F28", "F36", "F20", "F30"], "status": "verified", "trap": "At 0.55 the close rate rises (11/05 19:30: 0.598 -> 0.683; 11/08 11:54: 0.613 -> 0.691), which looks good. But surplus/order fell on 11/05 19:30 (23094 -> 11281) and on 11/05 02:44 (15836 -> 12680), and saved/deal fell on 11/07 05:02 (0.2972 -> 0.2741). A rising close rate alone is not a win.", "when": ["11/05 02:44", "11/05 19:30", "11/06 02:24", "11/07 05:02", "11/08 11:54", "11/06 05:36", "11/07 10:14"]},\n{"rule": "Do not add reweighting or penalty terms to the buyer candidates()/scout ranking without paid-sales evidence; read the current code to see which terms still run. Most ranking terms measured at or below expectation: 11/05 00:24 paid/h -10% (expected +4%), 11/08 11:55 saved/deal -2%, 11/08 16:36 -6% (reverted by the supervisor 11/08 19:53), 11/08 21:36 -4% (reverted), 11/10 09:28 -2%, 11/11 00:28 -5% (reverted). The only small gains were the paid-rate penalty change (close rate +1%, 11/09 21:40) and the lower short-shelf-life food penalty 0.3 -> 0.05 (close rate +3%, 11/10 17:41).", "evidence": ["F12", "F37", "F39", "F41", "F42", "F51", "F55", "F58", "F59"], "status": "verified", "trap": "A \'kept\' label is not a win: 11/08 11:55, 11/08 16:36