[11/11 03:58:04] HARNESS: try 1: 12.2 s, exit 0, answer '{"proposal": {}, "why": "The shop change slot is busy with market_ask 0.9 -> 0.95 under judgment until 05:09, and every number I own is a shop number, so any change now would be blocked and would confound that verdict. The last stock_value move (130M -> 140M, 11/11 01:01) re-judged MIXED, so it gives no evidence to move it back; with 138.3M at cost against the 140M cap and 496 units older than 24 h, I hold depth until the slot frees.", "ideas": ["Add a per-line cost gate in restock: skip or shallow any 300k+ A line whose unit cost is at or above that SKU\'s market settle. The supervisor\'s 11/10 22:0x audit found A goods earned 1.8% margin against 15.4% for B, with A bought at a median 0.678 of list and the A market paying 0.71. No single number expresses a per-SKU cost-versus-settle check, so this needs a code change.", "Add sell-through control per SKU: cut that SKU\'s depth when its units older than 24 h exceed its recent sales. Today sku_depth and depth are global, so 5-deep stock on slow lines ties up the cap while the top demand SKUs (Gef4d3036 at about 1596, G8ec51935 at about 1578) sell out. A global number cannot tell fast lines from slow ones."], "lessons_used": ["none"]}'
[11/11 03:58:05] HARNESS: try 1: 13.3 s, exit 0, answer '{"proposal": {}, "ab": null, "recruit": null, "playbook": "none", "why": "The shop change slot is busy until 05:09 with the market_ask 0.9 to 0.95 verdict still pending, and the open_gap 0.06 test was already judged and reverted, so no shop number should move now. The numbers in force already sit at the edges that the evidence supports (clear_hours 24, warranty_hours 72, endgame and final settings), so holding is the honest choice until the verdict lands.", "ideas": ["300k+ goods buyers who ask for a warranty close only 4.4% of the time, and 66% are gone before our offer arrives. The gap is response timing, not price, so offering the warranty in the first reply to a 300k+ ask (a code change to the reply flow) should be tested, since no number can speed up the offer.", "Food reviews show buyers rejecting units with too little shelf life left (11.2 h left against a 36 h need, 341.8 h against 360 h). Checking each buyer\'s stated shelf-life requirement before quoting a unit would stop those sales and protect stars (4.32 on the board), which a price number cannot do."], "lessons_used": ["none"]}'
[11/11 03:58:14] HARNESS: try 1: 22.3 s, exit 0, answer '```json\n{"proposal": {"forum_weights.pay_tips": 0.6}, "why": "Dislikes per post are close across kinds (pay_tips 0.33, fun and weather 0.27, freshness 0.26, best_value 0.25, our_deals 0.25, haggle 0.24, claims 0.21), so no kind clearly costs the rating; pay_tips has the highest rate, so I take one small step down (0.9 to 0.6) and judge it on the closed 2 h forum rating, not on mean votes. The claims and haggle \'one more dislike a post\' note does not show in this window, so I am not cutting those weights.", "ideas": ["Check our claims against the ledger refs before posting: our thisjonghoon claims average a 0.057 gap over 5 claims, against 0.002 to 0.02 for most authors, and a wrong claim is what draws stances. No weight can fix that.", "Dislike stances are one per voter account and apply to every post of ours, so one unhappy account lowers the whole rating. The only lever is posts that are accurate enough to draw no stance, not post count, and we must not ask for votes."], "lessons_used": ["L1", "L5"]}\n```'
