[11/11 06:54:39] HARNESS: try 1: 18.1 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Judge each shop number alone: one change per window, with no stock_value, reserve_cash, restock-code or buyer-code change in its hours. Only the single-change windows of 11/10 (F70, F71, F72) and the 11/11 03:09 one (F76) gave readable verdicts. Never read a raw margin swing as evidence, and keep one shop change open at a time.","evidence":["F70","F71","F72","F76","F73","F74","F75"],"status":"verified","trap":"11/10 11:36 (stuck_hours 5 -> 4) shared its hours with a stock_value rise 130000000 -> 200000000.0 (raw margin -67%). 11/10 17:23 and 19:35 shared theirs with reserve_cash, stock_value and buyer food-penalty changes. The 96 shop number verdicts of 11/5-11/9 were all MIXED, with raw margins from -72% to +717%. Treating any of these as a win or a loss misleads."},{"rule":"Lowering floor_frac_food paid once when judged alone: 0.65 -> 0.62 raised shop points/h net of the market by 112% (178/6046 -> 218/6087 sales), and the raw verdict agreed. Read the value now (order 5). Any further food-floor move must be tested alone before it counts.","evidence":["F70"],"status":"verified","trap":"The later steps 0.62 -> 0.6 (F74) and 0.6 -> 0.58 (F75) are MIXED and unjudged. Counting them as a second or third win, or as proof that floors should keep falling, is unsupported."},{"rule":"The goods floor gave no gain: floor_frac 0.65 -> 0.63 made no difference beyond noise (value share -14%, raw margin -14%; 293/6225 -> 303/6331 sales). Look for board points on other levers, such as faster turns of capital or stuck stock, not on this one.","evidence":["F71"],"status":"verified","trap":"Copying the food-floor win (F70) onto goods is not supported. The 11/09 06:43 bundle that dropped floor_frac 0.67 -> 0.45 was undone whole at 09:21 (F60)."},{"rule":"Releasing stuck stock sooner paid: stuck_hours 6 -> 5 raised shop points/h net of the market by 63% (314/6377 -> 294/6145 sales). The step 5 -> 4 is unjudged, so re-run it alone with stock_value held steady.","evidence":["F72","F73"],"status":"verified","trap":"Treating 11/10 11:36 as a verdict on 4 hours in either direction: it had stock_value 130000000 -> 200000000.0 in its hours and so has none."},{"rule":"market_ask is not a proven lever: 0.9 -> 0.95 made no difference beyond noise (value share +64%, raw margin +63%; 267/5711 -> 242/5675 sales). Do not spend a verdict window on it; put the slot on a lever with a plausible effect on paid sales.","evidence":["F76"],"status":"verified","trap":"market_ask was swung many times in MIXED windows (F53, F56, F67), each with a large raw margin move. Reading those as effects of market_ask is wrong."},{"rule":"Judge a change by board points per hour, not by margin per talk. A playbook that wins on margin per talk can still lose paid sales and board points.","evidence":["F6","F60"],"status":"unverified","trap":"The IKEA A/B (F6) won on margin per talk and deals, with fast concessions losing. Later, the 11/09 06:43 costco bundle, which lowered floors and raised min_margin, was undone whole at 09:21 (F60); standing order 1 records that it cut paid sales 65%. F6 is an old raw-before/after-style reading, so it is weak."},{"rule":"Before moving a number, read its value now and move it in the direction you mean (order 5). Undo a bad move with a single, clearly labelled change.","evidence":["F8","F9","F10","F58","F59","F63","F64","F65"],"status":"unverified","trap":"On 11/05 ask_frac_food went 0.72 -> 0.75 -> 0.8 -> 0.72 within the same hours (F9, F10, F12), and on 11/09 it went 0.7 -> 0.75 -> 0.7 within a minute (F63, F64, F65). These rows carry no verdict and only muddied later windows. They show why order 5 exists; they are not evidence about any value."}]}'
