[11/11 07:11:12] HARNESS: try 1: 34.7 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [{"rule": "Judge buyer changes on buyer points/h over closed windows, not on a part (close rate, saved/deal, seconds per order). Early walk-away and early cancel rules did not shorten talks, so do not rebuild them for speed.", "evidence": ["F52", "F54", "F46", "F57", "F16", "F49"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Parts point the wrong way. On 11/10 08:39 close rate fell 0.775 -> 0.664 while points/h rose +1%. On 11/09 23:48 points/h fell -35% and close rate fell 0.631 -> 0.542. Early-exit rules expected -8% and -5% seconds per order and measured +1% and +13% (11/05 17:22, 11/09 16:37).", "when": ["11/10 08:39", "11/09 23:48", "11/09 10:35", "11/10 16:04", "11/05 17:22", "11/09 16:37"]}, {"rule": "Do not re-rank candidates() or scout_wave by an \'expected saved rate\' or add break/spoil penalties. Every such code change measured worse on buyer_saved_deal than expected (F39 -6%, F42 -4% and F59 -5% reverted, F37 -2%, F55 -2%). The small wins came from removing a penalty (F58, short-shelf-life food penalty cut from 0.3 to 0.05, close rate +3%) or from softening a paid-rate penalty (F51).", "evidence": ["F39", "F42", "F59", "F37", "F55", "F58", "F51"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Each of these ranking ideas had a plausible argument and an expected gain of +1% to +4%, and each measured negative. \'Rank by what the board scores\' sounds right but lost twice (F42 and F59, both reverted).", "when": ["11/08 16:36", "11/08 21:36", "11/11 00:28", "11/08 11:55", "11/10 09:28", "11/10 17:41", "11/09 21:40"]}, {"rule": "Price-tiered close_gap is the only change with a large measured win: a wider close_gap for SKUs listed at 200k or more (F8) and a tighter one for 300k or more (F19). Look for more tier-specific closing rules. Do not use a global CLOSE_GAP step, which flipped sign (11/05 00:07 not taken, 11/05 11:12 kept).", "evidence": ["F8", "F19", "F11", "F14"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "These wins are