1/07 07:25 and 11/08 08:49 and then won on 11/09 10:35, so one window on saved/deal or close rate settles nothing.", "when": ["11/09 10:35", "11/10 08:39", "11/09 01:09", "11/07 02:12", "11/06 09:13", "11/07 07:25", "11/08 08:49"]}, {"rule": "FOOD_MARGIN: do not retry 1.2 (1.15 -> 1.2 not taken, 11/09 07:33). The choice between 1.1 and 1.15 is unresolved. The old win, 1.1 -> 1.15 on saved/deal (0.2981 -> 0.3195, 11/07 23:45), is contradicted by the newest row, 1.15 -> 1.1, where points/h rose +9% with saved difference +1.6 sd (11/10 16:04) but the step was not taken.", "evidence": ["F33", "F24", "F45", "F57"], "status": "contradicted", "trap": "Quoting \'raise it to 1.15\' as settled repeats a conclusion drawn from a part (saved/deal), while the newest points/h row points the other way and 1.1 -> 1.15 was not taken on 11/06 17:22.", "when": ["11/07 23:45", "11/06 17:22", "11/09 07:33", "11/10 16:04"]}, {"rule": "C_CAP: leave it alone and do not restart the 0.6 -> 0.55 trial. It was not taken five times (11/05 02:44, 11/05 19:30, 11/06 02:24, 11/07 05:02, 11/08 11:54), and the supervisor stopped the third trial (11/06 05:36). Grade C handling changed on 11/07 10:14 (F30).", "evidence": ["F13", "F17", "F18", "F28", "F36", "F20", "F30"], "status": "verified", "trap": "At 0.55 the close rate rises (11/05 19:30: 0.598 -> 0.683; 11/08 11:54: 0.613 -> 0.691), which looks good, but surplus/order fell on 11/05 19:30 (23094 -> 11281) and saved/deal fell on 11/07 05:02 (0.2972 -> 0.2741). A better close rate alone is not a win.", "when": ["11/05 02:44", "11/05 19:30", "11/06 02:24", "11/07 05:02", "11/08 11:54", "11/06 05:36", "11/07 10:14"]}]}'
