[11/11 07:27:50] HARNESS: try 1: 13.2 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [\n{"rule": "Judge each forum change on its own closed 2 h verdict, read on the forum rating (0-1, not a percentile) and on which of our posts draw dislike stances. Never keep or revert a forum change on forum_votes_post read as the hour before against the hour after.", "evidence": ["F3", "F4"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "F3 was reverted on -20% and F4 was kept despite -9%. Both were raw before/after readings that depend on the hour of day, so neither decision is evidence. Both rest only on weak UNVERIFIED readings."},\n{"rule": "The narrowed note() in forum_r3.py (top 4 shops with 2+ settles, last 2 refs per shown shop) is not disproven. It may be retried as the only forum change in its window, judged on the forum rating and on whether the posts carrying it draw dislikes.", "evidence": ["F3"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Treating the revert (-20%, raw before/after) as proof the change was bad. The reading is weak, so a good change may have been thrown away."},\n{"rule": "Treat the our_deals cap (a post goes to our_deals only when neither of our last two posts was our_deals) as unproven. Before tuning it, check whether our_deals posts are among those that draw dislikes.", "evidence": ["F4"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "F4 was kept with +15% expected against -9% measured on a weak raw reading. Passing its tests (14/14) shows the code runs, not that the forum rating improved."},\n{"rule": "Posting cadence is fixed by code at the market\'s limit of 310 s, so it is not a lever for the team. Put forum effort into post quality: find which stances and post kinds draw dislikes and cut those. Never trade quality for count.", "evidence": ["F5", "F6"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Assuming more posts mean a higher rating. F5 and F6 have no verdict, F6 (FORMAT_EVERY 360 -> 310) only aligned the code with the plan, and passing tests (16/16) says nothing about the rating. Posts are only a tenth of the buyer\'s ALL, so cadence cannot win the forum title."},\n{"rule": "Post kinds are built by code from the ledger and weighted by votes, and that mix has no verdict on the rating. Before changing the weighting, break dislikes down by kind to see which kinds cost the rating, then change one kind at a time.", "evidence": ["F1", "F2"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Assuming vote weighting is already optimal because it is vote-driven. F1 and F2 have no verdict, so nothing shows the mix avoids dislikes or protects the rating."}\n]}'
