[11/11 08:00:15] HARNESS: try 1: 17.9 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Put capital and depth behind the market\'s hot sellers: scale the planned depth and per-SKU cap by heat (sku_score at DEAR_HOT or more). For a 150-300k goods SKU the heat cap is 2x dear_depth; for 300k+ lines it stays at 5x dear_depth (20 units). Look for further changes of this kind.","evidence":["F90","F88","F84"],"status":"verified","trap":"F90 measured shop_revenue_h +398% and shop points/h +613% net of the market, against +8% expected, so do not forecast anything near that size. Raising the 300k+ heat cap from 3.0x to 5.0x (F84) was reverted on a raw before/after read (shop_margin_h -20%) and the supervisor restored it at F88, so that revert was not evidence against the idea."}, {"rule":"Change one shop number at a time and judge it alone on board_pts_h on a closed window. A raw margin move is no evidence when another change fell in the same hours, and a MIXED row is not a verdict.","evidence":["F104","F92","F94","F95","F97","F101","F102","F103"],"status":"verified","trap":"max_list 1200000 -> 900000 (F104, 11/10 21:44) is the only number judged alone and VERIFIED: points/h net of the market +50%, 356/5987 sales against 243/6015. Bundles such as F92, F94 and F97-F103 showed raw margins of +578%, +717% and +991% or -67% that cannot be credited to any one number, and the supervisor\'s own edits (F93, F98-F100, F103) carry no verdict."}, {"rule":"A code change reverted on a raw before/after read (which reads the hour of day) is not proof the idea is bad, and a keep on a raw read is not proof it is good. Re-test it on board_pts_h net of the market before dropping or building on it.","evidence":["F84","F88","F90","F28","F42","F50","F53","F64","F80"],"status":"verified","trap":"F84 was reverted on shop_margin_h -20% (raw) and then restored (F88), after which the heat-scaled change F90 measured shop points/h +613% net of the market. Raw verdicts such as the F66 keep (+252%) and the F64 revert (-43%) are equally weak, so do not treat them as settled either way."}, {"rule":"Do not size a stock cap from our own recent sales rate when a restock bug may have depressed it. First check that the shop was buying the market\'s best sellers.","evidence":["F26"],"status":"unverified","trap":"A cap of 4 h of our own 300k+ sales (2.2 an hour) was reverted at once. Those sales were low because restock had not bought the market\'s best sellers until 12:46 (a ranking and room bug), so the cap would have locked the shortfall in. This rests on a single raw read (weak)."}, {"rule":"Judge the food shelf-life change (selling food categories need min(min_shelf_hours, 48)) on board_pts_h on a closed window. Do not judge it on shelf_refused_h, which is only a part.","evidence":["F77"],"status":"unverified","trap":"It was kept although shelf_refused_h was expected -30% and measured +21%, the wrong way. The read was raw before/after (weak), so it is neither proof of harm nor of help, and a part metric moving either way settles nothing about points."}]}'
