[11/11 09:54:53] HARNESS: try 1: 16.7 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [\n{"rule": "Change one shop number per window and hold stock_value, reserve_cash, restock code and buyer code steady in its hours. Only the single-change windows 11/10 01:43, 11/10 05:04, 11/10 07:19 and 11/11 03:09 gave readable verdicts. Judge on shop points/h net of the market, not on raw margin.", "evidence": ["F70", "F71", "F72", "F76", "F73", "F74", "F75"], "status": "verified", "trap": "11/10 11:36 (stuck_hours 5 -> 4) shared its hours with stock_value 130000000 -> 200000000.0 (raw margin -67%). 11/10 17:23 and 19:35 also shared theirs with other changes. All three are MIXED and prove nothing. In F76 the raw margin read +63% but the verdict was noise, so raw margin misleads even in a clean window.", "when": ["11/10 01:43", "11/10 05:04", "11/10 07:19", "11/11 03:09", "11/10 11:36", "11/10 17:23", "11/10 19:35"]},\n{"rule": "Lowering floor_frac_food paid once when judged alone: 0.65 -> 0.62 raised shop points/h net of the market by 112% (178/6046 -> 218/6087 sales). Read the value now (order 5) before any further food-floor move, and test it alone.", "evidence": ["F70"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The later steps 0.62 -> 0.6 (F74) and 0.6 -> 0.58 (F75) are MIXED and unjudged. Counting them as a second or third win, or as proof that floors should keep falling, is unsupported.", "when": ["11/10 01:43", "11/10 17:23", "11/10 19:35"]},\n{"rule": "The goods floor gave no gain: floor_frac 0.65 -> 0.63 made no difference beyond noise (value share -14%, raw margin -14%; 293/6225 -> 303/6331 sales). Look for board points elsewhere, such as faster capital turns or stuck stock.", "evidence": ["F71"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Copying the food-floor win onto goods is not supported. The 11/09 06:43 bundle (floor_frac 0.67 -> 0.45, min_margin 0.02 -> 0.14, max_turns 6 -> 4 and more) was MIXED and was undone whole at 09:21.", "when": ["11/10 05:04", "11/09 06:43", "11/09 09:21"]},\n{"rule": "Releasing stuck stock sooner paid: stuck_hours 6 -> 5 raised shop points/h net of the market by 63% (314/6377 -> 294/6145 sales). Re-run 5 -> 4 alone, with stock_value held steady, after reading the value now.", "evidence": ["F72", "F73"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Treating 11/10 11:36 as a verdict on 4 hours in either direction: stock_value 130000000 -> 200000000.0 fell in its hours, so it has none.", "when": ["11/10 07:19", "11/10 11:36"]},\n{"rule": "market_ask 0.9 -> 0.95 made no difference beyond noise in its one clean window (value share +64%, raw margin +63%; 267/5711 -> 242/5675 sales). Put the next verdict slot on a lever with a plausible effect on paid sales and capital turns.", "evidence": ["F76"], "status": "verified", "trap": "market_ask was swung many times in MIXED windows (11/08 23:26, 11/09 06:26, 11/09 17:41), each with a large raw margin move. Reading those as effects of market_ask is wrong. It is also one window only, so it is not a proof of zero effect.", "when": ["11/11 03:09", "11/08 23:26", "11/09 06:26", "11/09 17:41"]},\n{"rule": "Never bundle shop changes. A multi-number change cannot be attributed and risks cutting paid sales. The 11/09 06:43 bundle was partly undone at 07:02 and 07:21 and wholly undone at 09:21.", "evidence": ["F57", "F58", "F59", "F60"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Reading the bundle\'s raw margin +30% as a gain: that window was MIXED, and the supervisor reversed the bundle anyway. Piecemeal undos (F58, then F59) also muddled which values were live.", "when": ["11/09 06:43", "11/09 07:02", "11/09 07:21", "11/09 09:21"]}\n]}'
