[11/11 09:55:30] HARNESS: try 1: 9.8 s, exit 0, answer '{"proposal": {}, "why": "The shop change slot is busy: stock_value 140M to 150M (set 09:39) is still being judged until 11:39, and shop numbers wait while it runs, so I am proposing no number changes now. Stock at cost is 143.6M against 25.7M cash and 509 of 1,724 units are older than 24 h, so the 150M cap is nearly binding and that is worth re-judging at the 11:39 verdict.", "ideas": ["Steer buying toward the demand leaders (Gef4d3036, G8ec51935, G5ec8117f, G022ce883) and the 300k+ furniture lines. Leading shops take 40-63% of revenue from 300k+ goods while ours is 3%, and our 31k mean sale is far below their 140k-577k. No cap sets what we buy, so this is a sourcing change, not a number.", "Age is not capped anywhere. 509 units older than 24 h hold capital that could turn faster, and that turn speed is what closes the 0.266 gap to #10. A rule that moves aged stock first, using the existing clear_frac and sell-down logic, would act on it without touching the shop slot."], "lessons_used": ["none"]}'
[11/11 09:55:31] HARNESS: try 1: 10.6 s, exit 0, answer '{"proposal": {"CAP": 0.7}, "recruit": null, "why": "Our buyer saved percentile is 0.3045 (weight 0.5) while deals sit at 0.812, so a lower CAP should buy bigger savings per deal, which is the weaker part of our buyer ALL. One 0.05 step is the largest allowed per cycle, and the 140 walks and 0.257 lost-talk gap show some deals will be lost, which the deals term can absorb.", "ideas": ["Forum rating is 0.913 against the leader\'s 0.934, and the notes say posts draw dislike stances. No number can fix that; reviewing which post types draw dislikes is the lever.", "113 talks ended with \'other shop none in stock\', so buyer scouts keep reaching shops that cannot supply. Reordering the scout target list toward shops with stock would cut wasted talks, but that is a scout-routing change, not a number."], "lessons_used": ["none"]}'
[11/11 09:55:33] HARNESS: try 1: 12.8 s, exit 0, answer '{"proposal": {}, "ab": {"param": "market_ask", "kind": "goods", "value": 1.0}, "recruit": null, "playbook": "none", "why": "The shop-change slot is busy until 11:39 and open_gap stays at 0 per the supervisor, so no shop number moves now. The goods A/B tests market_ask 1.0 against 0.95 because the supervisor\'s audit shows grade-A goods earning 1.8% against a market that pays about 4 points above their median cost, and I have not verified that the cap binds at 0.95.", "ideas": ["300k+ goods leave before the first offer 67% of the time when they ask for a warranty (close 3.1%), which matches the audit finding that buyers compare first asks across shops; quoting the market line on those goods before the first offer is a code change, not a number.", "Five of the low reviews cite too little shelf life left (28-216 h left against 42-540 h needed), so food should not be offered to buyers whose required shelf life exceeds what remains; that is a stock-filter rule, not a knob."], "lessons_used": ["L1", "L5"]}'
[11/11 09:55:36] HARNESS: try 1: 15.5 s, exit 0, answer '{"proposal": {"forum_weights": {"pay_tips": 1.2}}, "why": "pay_tips has the highest mean votes (6.56) but the lowest weight among the high-vote kinds (1.0), and its dislike rate (30 of 89 posts, about 0.34) is within noise of the other kinds (0.26 to 0.30), so one small step is supported. Per-kind dislike rates do not show any kind clearly costing the forum rating, so I am changing only this one kind (L5).", "ideas": ["Our forum rating (0.913) trails the leader (0.934) by 0.021, and the rating is lost through dislike stances, not post count, so the next check is which of our posts draw dislikes: the per-kind counts this hour do not separate the kinds, so I would tag dislikes per post by kind and author in the ledger before any further weight change.", "Claims and haggle name other shops, and the 11/9 note says they draw about one extra dislike per post, but this hour\'s per-post rates (claims 0.26, haggle 0.30) do not show that, so the claim should be re-measured on a larger sample before those kinds are cut."], "lessons_used": ["L4", "L5"]}'
