[11/11 10:11:46] HARNESS: try 1: 44.0 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Judge buyer changes on buyer points/h (board_pts_h) over closed same-hour windows, never on a part such as close rate, saved/deal or seconds per order. Early walk-away and early cancel rules did not make talks shorter, so do not rebuild them for speed.","evidence":["F52","F54","F46","F50","F57","F16","F49"],"status":"verified","trap":"Parts and points/h disagree. On 11/10 08:39 close rate fell 0.775 -> 0.664 while points/h rose +1%. On 11/10 16:04 close rate fell 0.851 -> 0.798 while points/h rose +9%. On 11/09 23:48 points/h fell -35% (0.000582 -> 0.00038) and close rate fell 0.631 -> 0.542. The speed rules measured worse than expected on seconds per order: 11/05 17:22 expected -8%, measured +1%; 11/09 16:37 expected -5%, measured +13% (+ is worse). Points/h gaps of 1-3% are small: on 11/09 18:04 +2% was still not taken.","note":""},{"rule":"Do not re-rank candidates() or scout_wave by an \'expected saved rate\', or add break/spoil penalties. Every such change measured worse on buyer_saved_deal than expected: 11/08 16:36 -6%, 11/08 21:36 -4% and 11/11 00:28 -5% (both reverted), 11/08 11:55 -2%, 11/10 09:28 -2%. Only small tweaks to an existing penalty held up: the food short-shelf-life penalty cut 0.3 -> 0.05 (close rate +3%) and the paid-rate penalty change (close rate +1%).","evidence":["F39","F42","F59","F37","F55","F58","F51"],"status":"verified","trap":"Each ranking idea had a plausible argument (\'rank by what the board scores\') and an expected gain of +1% to +4%, and each measured negative. Some were marked \'kept\' despite a negative measure (11/08 11:55, 11/10 09:28). The two small tweaks were judged on close rate, a part, not on points/h, so treat them as weak support.","note":""},{"rule":"FIRM_GAP: the value in the latest trials is 0.07; do not move it either way. 0.07 -> 0.05 cut points/h from 0.000582 to 0.00038 (-35%, 11/09 23:48) and 0.07 -> 0.09 was not taken (11/09 18:04). Read its value before touching it.","evidence":["F52","F50","F31","F40","F23","F25"],"status":"verified","trap":"The earlier wins (0.03 -> 0.05 kept 11/06 14:50, 0.05 -> 0.07 kept 11/06 20:57) were judged on saved/deal, a part. On 11/07 10:29 saved/deal rose 0.2949 -> 0.2988 while close rate fell 0.698 -> 0.655, and the step was not taken. The same 0.07 -> 0.05 step was not taken on 11/07 10:29, 11/08 17:55 and 11/09 23:48.","note":""},{"rule":"CAP: the latest trials started from 0.75, which won (0.8 -> 0.75, saved/deal 0.33 -> 0.3498, 11/08 21:51). Both neighbours were not taken on points/h: 0.75 -> 0.8 (0.000513 -> 0.000487, -5%, 11/10 03:43) and 0.75 -> 0.7 (+2%, close rate 0.86 -> 0.795, 11/10 12:26). The supervisor\'s 0.7 try was undone within 17 minutes (11/09 15:57, 16:14). Leave 0.75 unless paid-sales evidence is clear.","evidence":["F43","F53","F56","F47","F48","F38"],"status":"verified","trap":"Older CAP results flip with the hour: 0.85 -> 0.8 was not taken twice (11/06 12:28, 11/07 13:15) and then won on 11/08 14:39, so the same step gave both signs on saved/deal. 0.7 had +2% points/h on 11/10 12:26 and was still not taken, so do not read that as a win.","note":""},{"rule":"MAX_RAISE: the latest trials started from 0.35, which won on points/h (0.4 -> 0.35, +3%, 11/09 10:35). Do not go lower: 0.35 -> 0.3 was not taken (11/10 08:39), nor was 0.4 -> 0.3 twice (11/09 01:09, 11/07 02:12). Going up from 0.4 to 0.5 was not taken either (11/06 09:13).","evidence":["F46","F54","F44","F27","F21","F29","F35"],"status":"verified","trap":"The differences are tiny and the sign flips between windows. 0.4 -> 0.35 was not taken on 11/07 07:25 and 11/08 08:49 and then won on 11/09 10:35, so one window on saved/deal proves little. 0.4 -> 0.3 on 11/09 01:09 raised saved/deal (0.3472 -> 0.3535) and was still not taken.","note":""},{"rule":"FOOD_MARGIN: the latest trials started from 1.15. Do not retry 1.2 (1.15 -> 1.2 not taken, 11/09 07:33). 1.1 versus 1.15 is unresolved: the old win, 1.1 -> 1.15 on saved/deal (0.2981 -> 0.3195, 11/07 23:45), is contradicted by 1.15 -> 1.1 on 11/10 16:04, where points/h rose +9% and saved/deal 0.3722 -> 0.3889, yet it was recorded as not taken because close rate fell 0.851 -> 0.798.","evidence":["F33","F24","F45","F57"],"status":"contradicted","trap":"Quoting \'raise it to 1.15\' as settled repeats a conclusion drawn from a part (saved/deal), while the newest points/h row points the other way. The newest row\'s \'not taken\' tag also sits oddly with its +9% points/h, so do not cite either direction as proven. Read the current value first (standing order 5).","note":""},{"rule":"C_CAP: leave it alone and do not restart the 0.6 -> 0.55 trial. It was not taken five times (11/05 02:44, 11/05 19:30, 11/06 02:24, 11/07 05:02, 11/08 11:54), and the supervisor stopped the third trial (11/06 05:36) with the rule that a trial lost within a day is not restarted. Grade C handling was changed in code instead (11/07 10:14, C_WARRANTY hours required, C_CAP clause dropped).","evidence":["F13","F17","F18","F28","F36","F20","F30"],"status":"verified","trap":"At 0.55 the close rate rises (11/05 19:30: 0.598 -> 0.683; 11/08 11:54: 0.613 -> 0.691), which looks good, but surplus/order fell on 11/05 19:30 (23094 -> 11281) and saved/deal fell on 11/07 05:02 (0.2972 -> 0.2741). These trials all predate points/h verdicts.","note":""},{"rule":"Price-tier close_gap logic is where the large buyer wins came from: close_gap 0.15 for SKUs listed at 200k or more (surplus/order expected +8%, measured +243%, 11/04 21:11) and 0.06 for list prices of 300k or more (expected +4%, measured +65%, 11/06 02:41). Look for further tier-specific rules like these before nudging the global CLOSE_GAP.","evidence":["F8","F19","F11","F14","F26"],"status":"verified","trap":"These were judged on surplus/order, a part, before points/h existed, so the size of the gain may not carry to board points. The global CLOSE_GAP 0.11 -> 0.12 step flipped between windows (not taken 11/05 00:07, kept 11/05 11:12). A cap on the first offer at 88% of the first ask measured saved/deal -2% against an expected +5% (11/06 22:59).","note":""}]}'
