[11/11 10:12:23] HARNESS: try 1: 9.6 s, exit 0, answer '{"proposal": {}, "why": "No shop number change this cycle: the shop change slot is busy with stock_value (150M, judged at 11:39), and the supervisor\'s rule and code both hold any second shop change until that verdict reads out. The recent number changes are MIXED or PENDING with no clean verdict, so there is no evidence yet to move a value.", "ideas": ["Capital is the constraint: stock_at_cost is 144M against 25M cash, and 510 of 1795 units are older than 24 h. Faster turns need more buyers at the going medians (furniture/bedding ~0.69-0.71), which no number sets, so the next gain is in which grade and SKU lines the buyer restocks.", "The forum title gap is 0.913 against the leader\'s 0.934, and the API shows only about 100 recent posts, so 2-3 of ours are visible at a time. Post count cannot close it; what can is finding which of our posts draw dislike stances (the rating is lost there) and fixing those posts\' content."], "lessons_used": []}'
[11/11 10:12:29] HARNESS: try 1: 14.8 s, exit 0, answer '{"proposal": {}, "ab": {"param": "clear_frac", "kind": "food", "value": 0.5}, "recruit": null, "playbook": "none", "why": "The shop slot is busy with the stock_value change until 11:39, so I propose no shop number now. The A/B tests clear_frac for food alone, from 0.6 to 0.5 (the grocery_markdown value), to see whether earlier cuts turn food faster; food is 2808 of 3774 talks and the board\'s gap is book and revenue. Reading clear_frac\'s current value (0.6) before the move, as L1 and L2 require.", "ideas": ["Shelf-life complaints (2-star reviews: 28-70 h left against 42-126 h needed) point at which food lines the restock brings in, not at a price number; restock is closed until 1794360359, so favour longer-dated food lines when it reopens.", "The forum rating is 0.913 against the leader\'s 0.934, and our posts carry no dislike stances to fix; the gain is in post quality on the dislike-drawing topics, not in post count."], "lessons_used": ["L1", "L2", "L5"]}'
[11/11 10:12:29] HARNESS: try 1: 15.5 s, exit 0, answer '{"proposal": {}, "recruit": null, "why": "I would hold every buyer number. CAP 0.75, MAX_RAISE 0.35 and FIRM_GAP 0.07 are at the values lessons L2 to L4 say to keep, FOOD_MARGIN 1.15 is contradicted by judged rows in both directions (L5), and SCOUTS 5 and CLOSE_GAP 0.12 are already at their range limits with no judged evidence to move them. The buyer is converting well (440 deals from 485 orders, 96 of 100 paid), and the board says the rank gap is in the shop\'s book and revenue, not the buyer\'s terms.", "ideas": ["106 of 485 talks ended with \'other shop none in stock\', so scouts are spending quotes on shops that cannot sell. Having scouts check stock before asking for a quote would free talks for shops that can deal, and no buyer number can do that.", "The forum rating is 0.913 against the leader\'s 0.934 and every top post carries +8, so the loss comes from dislike stances. Finding which posts draw them, without trading post quality for count, is a forum change that no buyer number can make."], "lessons_used": ["L1", "L2", "L3", "L4", "L5"]}'
[11/11 10:12:32] HARNESS: try 1: 18.3 s, exit 0, answer '{"proposal": {"forum_weights": {"best_value": 3.0, "freshness": 2.2, "pay_tips": 0.9, "fun": 1.9, "claims": 1.0, "weather": 2.4, "haggle": 0.4}}, "why": "Dislikes per post are flat across kinds (0.27 to 0.34) and mean votes differ by under 0.6, so weights can only nudge the rating; pay_tips has the highest dislike rate (30/89 = 0.34) for a middling vote lift, so I cut only that kind, one kind at a time as L5 asks. Claims (0.27 dislikes per post) and haggle (0.30) are not above the other kinds here, which does not show the 11/9 note\'s claim of about one extra dislike per post, so I left them unchanged pending a per-kind check.", "ideas": ["Measure dislikes per post for claims and haggle on our own posts over a closed 2 h window before changing their weights, since the 11/9 note\'s +1 dislike is not visible in the per-kind counts (0.27 and 0.30 per post). No weight can tell whether the rating\'s dislike stances come from naming other shops or from something else in the same posts.", "Propose a new kind, a ledger-backed refund and break tally (\\"환불·고장 집계\\") built from the ledger refs, as dae-yangkim\'s 24 h 고장 기록 post shows such refunds exist; it would state only counts and refs, never a vote request, and would give readers a fact-based post that names no shop."], "lessons_used": ["L4", "L5"]}'
