[11/11 11:01:07] HARNESS: try 1: 28.4 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Change one shop number at a time. Read its value now (standing order 5) and judge it alone on board_pts_h over a closed window. A raw margin move is no evidence when another change fell in the same hours, and a MIXED row is not a verdict.","evidence":["F104","F92","F94","F95","F98","F100"],"status":"verified","trap":"F92, F94 and F95 moved stock_value, reserve_cash, warranty_hours and final_frac within hours of each other. Their raw margins (+578%, +717%, -48%) say nothing about any single number, and stock_value 200000000 (F98) was walked back to 130000000 (F100). The only number judged alone is max_list 1200000 -> 900000 (F104): points/h net of the market +50%, 356/5987 sales against 243/6015. That is one direction on one verdict, not a target value."},{"rule":"Do not revert a code change, or build on one, from a raw before/after read, because it reads the hour of day. Re-test on board_pts_h net of the market. A reverted idea can be restored and judged again.","evidence":["F84","F88","F90","F80","F64","F53","F50","F42","F28"],"status":"verified","trap":"F84 (heat cap 3.0x -> 5.0x of dear_depth) was reverted on shop_margin_h -20% (raw). It was restored in F88 (hot 300k+ lines up to 5x dear_depth, 20 units). F90 then measured shop points/h +613% net of the market. F28, F42, F50, F53, F64 and F80 were also reverted on raw reads, so their ideas were never fairly judged."},{"rule":"For faster turns from the same capital, scale depth and per-SKU cap with a SKU\'s heat (sku_score against DEAR_HOT) instead of using a flat depth. This is the one code change judged on board terms and kept.","evidence":["F90","F88"],"status":"verified","trap":"F90 (150-300k hot goods get dear_depth times a heat capped at 2x, 5x kept for 300k+) measured shop_revenue_h +398% and points/h +613%, net of the market\'s own change (paid value x1.05, count x1.08). It is a single verdict, so do not extend the heat cap further without a one-at-a-time board_pts_h judgement. The earlier cut to a flat depth for non-hot lines (F38, F57, F66) was kept only on raw reads."},{"rule":"Do not size a stock cap from our own recent sales rate when a restock bug may have depressed it. First check that the shop was buying the market\'s best sellers.","evidence":["F26"],"status":"unverified","trap":"A cap of 4 h of our own 300k+ sales (2.2 an hour) was reverted at once. Those sales were low only because restock had not bought the market\'s best sellers. This rests on one old fact judged on a raw read, so it is weak."},{"rule":"Judge the food shelf-life change (selling food categories need min(min_shelf_hours, 48)) on board_pts_h over a closed window. Do not judge it on shelf_refused_h, which is only a part of the aim.","evidence":["F77"],"status":"unverified","trap":"It was kept although shelf_refused_h was expected -30% and measured +21%, the wrong way. The read was raw before/after (weak), so it is neither proof of harm nor of benefit. Neither keeping nor reverting it on that part-metric is justified."}]}'
