[11/11 14:14:39] HARNESS: try 1: 23.8 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Judge a shop number on board_pts_h over a closed window, and count only a number changed alone. In play mode (standing order 3) several numbers may move per cycle, but a bundle earns no credit, so do not cite it. Read the number\'s value now before moving it (order 5).","evidence":["F104","F107","F92","F94","F95","F108","F109","F110"],"status":"verified","trap":"11/09 13:17, 13:40 and 15:11 moved stock_value, reserve_cash, warranty_hours and final_frac within hours of each other, and 11/11 11:44-13:42 moved a dozen numbers. The raw margins (+578%, +717%, -48%, +98%, +53%) say nothing about any one number. Supervisor rows (F93, F98, F99, F100, F103, F110) carry no verdict either."},{"rule":"Old MIXED and UNVERIFIED shop rows (F31-F103) are no reason to hold or to avoid a number. Do not use them to say a number was \'tried both ways\'. Only single-change VERIFIED rows count.","evidence":["F101","F102","F97","F92"],"status":"verified","trap":"Reading F97 (raw margin -67%) or F101/F102 (+991%) as proof for or against a stock_value or reserve_cash move. Each had other changes in the same hours."},{"rule":"Do not revert a code change, or build on one, from a raw before/after read, because it reads the hour of day. Re-test on board_pts_h net of the market. A reverted idea can be restored and judged again.","evidence":["F84","F88","F90","F80","F64","F53","F50","F42"],"status":"verified","trap":"The heat cap 3.0x -> 5.0x of dear_depth (F84) was reverted on a raw shop_margin_h of -20%. It was restored (F88), and the related 150-300k change (F90) measured shop_revenue_h +398% and points/h +613% net of the market. F80, F64, F53, F50 and F42 were reverted on raw reads and never re-tested."},{"rule":"For faster turns from the same capital, scale depth and per-SKU cap with a SKU\'s heat (sku_score against DEAR_HOT) instead of using a flat depth. This is the one code change judged on board terms and kept.","evidence":["F90","F88"],"status":"verified","trap":"Reading the +398% / +613% as a license for any heat cap. F90 is the 150-300k band capped at 2x, with 5x kept for 300k+. F88 is a supervisor restore with no verdict, so it adds no evidence."},{"rule":"Raising stock_value is not a proven lever for points. The one single-change verified read (140M to 150M) made no difference beyond noise. Look for turn-speeding changes first, and judge any capital change alone.","evidence":["F107","F105","F97"],"status":"verified","trap":"Raising stock_value again and again hoping for more paid sales. F107 showed value share +16% and raw margin +16% (278/5468 -> 245/5760 sales), which is noise. F105 and F97 are MIXED and prove nothing."},{"rule":"max_list has one verified read: lowering it from 1200000 to 900000 raised points/h net of the market by 50%. The later moves to 600000 and back to 1200000 (F108, F110) have no verdict. If it is moved again, move it alone and judge it on board_pts_h.","evidence":["F104","F108","F110"],"status":"verified","trap":"Treating F110\'s return to 1200000 as a finding. It is a supervisor bundle with no verdict and does not undo the verified F104 read."},{"rule":"Judge the food shelf-life change (selling food categories need min(min_shelf_hours, 48)) on board_pts_h over a closed window, not on shelf_refused_h, which is only a part of the aim.","evidence":["F77"],"status":"unverified","trap":"F77 was kept although shelf_refused_h was expected -30% and measured +21%. The read was raw before/after (weak), so it is neither proof of harm nor of benefit."}]}'
