[11/11 16:22:21] HARNESS: try 1: 21.7 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [{"rule": "Judge every buyer change on buyer points/h (board_pts_h) over closed same-hour windows, never on a part such as close rate, saved/deal or seconds per order. Code that cancels or walks away early did not shorten talks: F16 expected -8% secs/order and measured +1%; F49 expected -5% and measured +13%.", "evidence": ["F46", "F50", "F52", "F54", "F57", "F61", "F16", "F49"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Parts and points/h disagree. F54: close rate fell 0.775 -> 0.664 while points/h rose +1%. F57: close rate fell 0.851 -> 0.798 while points/h rose +9%. F61: close rate was flat (0.788 -> 0.79) while points/h fell -18%. Reading a close-rate or saved/deal gain as a win repeats these errors."}, {"rule": "FIRM_GAP: keep it at 0.07 (read its value in force before touching it). 0.07 -> 0.05 was not taken twice on points/h: 0.000582 -> 0.00038 (-35%, -1.1 sd, F52) and 0.000345 -> 0.000283 (-18%, -0.5 sd, F61). Raising it was no gain either: 0.07 -> 0.09 not taken (F50, +2% points/h, saved difference -0.2 sd). Stop trying lower values.", "evidence": ["F52", "F61", "F50", "F31", "F40", "F23", "F25"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The earlier wins (0.03 -> 0.05 F23, 0.05 -> 0.07 F25) were judged on saved/deal, a part. 0.07 -> 0.05 also looked fine on saved/deal in F31 and F40 (not taken) while points/h later fell sharply, so saved/deal alone misleads here."}, {"rule": "CAP: both neighbours of 0.75 were not taken on points/h: 0.75 -> 0.8 (0.000513 -> 0.000487, -5%, F53) and 0.75 -> 0.7 (+2%, saved difference +0.5 sd, F56). The gains are within noise, so look for levers elsewhere; read the value now before any move.", "evidence": ["F43", "F53", "F56", "F47", "F48", "F38"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Older CAP results flip with the hour: 0.85 -> 0.8 was not taken twice (F22, F32) and then won (F38). The 0.7 try of F47 was undone 17 minutes later (F48), so it is not a value to recommend."}, {"rule": "MAX_RAISE: 0.4 -> 0.35 won on points/h (+3%, F46). Going lower, 0.35 -> 0.3 (+1%, +0.2 sd, F54), was not taken; 0.4 -> 0.3 (F44, F27) and 0.4 -> 0.5 (F21) were not taken either. Differences are tiny, so do not spend changes here.", "evidence": ["F46", "F54", "F44", "F27", "F21", "F29", "F35"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The sign flips between windows: 0.4 -> 0.35 was not taken in F29 and F35 (saved/deal, a part) and then won in F46 on points/h. A single saved/deal window decides nothing."}, {"rule": "FOOD_MARGIN: do not retry 1.2 (1.15 -> 1.2 not taken, F45). 1.1 versus 1.15 is unresolved: the old win of 1.1 -> 1.15 (saved/deal 0.2981 -> 0.3195, F33) was judged on a part, while 1.15 -> 1.1 showed points/h +9% and +1.6 sd (F57) yet was logged not taken. Read the value in force before moving it.", "evidence": ["F33", "F24", "F45", "F57"], "status": "contradicted", "trap": "Quoting \'raise it to 1.15\' as settled repeats a conclusion drawn from saved/deal, a part, while the newest points/h row points the other way."}, {"rule": "C_CAP: leave it alone and do not restart the 0.6 -> 0.55 trial. It was not taken five times (F13, F17, F18, F28, F36), and the supervisor ruled that a trial lost within a day is not restarted (F20). Grade C is now handled by the warranty rule (F30).", "evidence": ["F13", "F17", "F18", "F28", "F36", "F20", "F30"], "status": "verified", "trap": "At 0.55 the close rate rises (F17: 0.598 -> 0.683; F36: 0.613 -> 0.691), which looks good, but surplus/order fell in F13 (15836 -> 12680) and F17 (23094 -> 11281). Close rate alone hides the loss."}, {"rule": "Candidate-ranking and weighting code: re-ranking offers by rate, ratio or break-rate penalties measured negative on saved/deal and was often reverted (F42 -4% reverted, F59 -5% reverted, F41 supervisor revert of F39 at -6%). Small trims of an existing penalty did better (F58 short-shelf-life penalty 0.3 -> 0.05, close rate +3%; F51 paid-rate penalty, +1%). Prefer small trims and test any new ranking against points/h.", "evidence": ["F37", "F39", "F41", "F42", "F55", "F58", "F59", "F51"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Each of these shipped with an expected gain of +1% to +4% and measured negative (F37 -2%, F39 -6%, F42 -4%, F55 -2%, F59 -5%). F37, F39 and F55 were kept despite that. A plausible-sounding ranking idea is not evidence, and a \'kept\' tag does not mean the measurement was positive."}]}'
