u_score against DEAR_HOT) instead of a flat depth. Keep the 150-300k band capped at 2x and 300k+ at 5x.", "evidence": ["F90", "F88"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Reading +398% revenue and +613% points/h as a licence for any heat cap. The 11/09 11:18 supervisor restore of 5x for 300k+ fell in the same hours as the 11/09 11:33 change, so the credit is not cleanly split between them."},\n{"rule": "Raising stock_value is not a proven lever for points. The one single-change verified read (140M to 150M) made no difference beyond noise. Look for turn-speeding changes first, and judge any capital change alone.", "evidence": ["F107", "F105", "F97"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Raising stock_value again and again hoping for more paid sales. 11/11 09:39 showed value share +16% and raw margin +16% (278/5468 -> 245/5760 sales), which is noise. The 11/10 12:31 and 11/11 01:01 raises were MIXED and prove nothing."},\n{"rule": "max_list has one verified read: lowering it from 1200000 to 900000 raised points/h net of the market by 50%. The later moves to 600000 and back to 1200000 (11/11 11:44, 11/11 13:42) were in bundles and have no verdict. Read the value in force before moving it, and note that a lone move is the only readable one.", "evidence": ["F104", "F108", "F117"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Treating the 11/11 13:42 return to 1200000 as a finding. It is a supervisor bundle with no verdict and does not undo the verified 11/10 21:44 read."},\n{"rule": "Judge the food shelf-life change (selling food categories need min(min_shelf_hours, 48)) on board_pts_h over a closed window, not on shelf_refused_h, which is only a part of the aim.", "evidence": ["F77"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "11/09 01:10 was kept although shelf_refused_h was expected -30% and measured +21%. The read was raw before/after (weak), so it is neither proof of harm nor of benefit."}\n]}'
