[11/11 23:34:08] HARNESS: try 1: 17.5 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Change one shop number per window and judge it on board_pts_h over a closed window, net of the market. Play mode (standing order 3) lets several numbers move per cycle, but a bundle earns no credit and must not be cited as a finding. Only single-change VERIFIED rows count: F104 (max_list 1200000 -> 900000, points/h +50% net of the market) and F107 (stock_value 140000000 -> 150000000, no difference beyond noise).","evidence":["F104","F107","F92","F94","F95","F108","F117"],"status":"verified","trap":"11/09 13:17-15:11 moved stock_value, reserve_cash, warranty_hours and final_frac together (raw margin +578%, +717%). 11/11 11:44-13:42 moved a dozen numbers (raw margin +98% to +12%). Those raw gains were read as wins, but no single number can be credited from them."},{"rule":"Old MIXED and UNVERIFIED shop rows (11/05 to 11/10 16:21) are no reason to hold or avoid a number. Do not say a number was \'tried both ways\' from them.","evidence":["F97","F101","F102","F92"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Reading 11/10 12:31 (raw margin -67%) or 11/10 16:20 and 16:21 (+991%) as proof for or against a stock_value or reserve_cash move. Each had other changes in the same hours."},{"rule":"Do not revert or build on a code change from a raw before/after read, because it reads the hour of day. Wait for a board_pts_h verdict net of the market. A reverted idea may be restored and judged again. F123 and F132 were kept, but both were MIXED, so they prove nothing either way. F134 has no verdict yet.","evidence":["F84","F88","F90","F80","F64","F123","F132","F134"],"status":"verified","trap":"The heat cap 3.0x -> 5.0x of dear_depth (F84) was reverted on a raw shop_margin_h of -20%. After it was restored (F88), the related F90 change measured shop_revenue_h +398% and points/h +613% net of the market. F64 and F80 were also reverted on raw reads (-43%, -36%)."},{"rule":"Raising stock_value is not a proven lever for points. The one single-change verified read (140M to 150M) made no difference beyond noise. Look for changes that speed up turns first, and judge any capital change alone.","evidence":["F107","F105","F97"],"status":"verified","trap":"Raising stock_value again and again to get more paid sales. F107 showed value share +16% and raw margin +16% (278/5468 -> 245/5760 sales), which is noise. F105 and F97 were mixed and prove nothing."},{"rule":"max_list has one verified read: 1200000 -> 900000 raised points/h net of the market by 50% (F104, 11/10 21:44). Every later move (600000 at F108, 1200000 at F117, 900000 at F128) was in a bundle or a mixed window. Judge any further max_list move alone, and read its value now first (standing order 5).","evidence":["F104","F108","F117","F128"],"status":"verified","trap":"Treating the 11/11 13:42 return to 1200000 or the 11/11 17:17 return to 900000 as a finding. Neither has a verdict, and neither undoes or confirms F104."},{"rule":"Judge the food shelf-life change (selling food categories need min(min_shelf_hours, 48)) on board_pts_h over a closed window, not on shelf_refused_h, which is only a part of the aim.","evidence":["F77"],"status":"unverified","trap":"F77 was kept although shelf_refused_h was expected -30% and measured +21%. The read was raw before/after (weak), so it is neither proof of harm nor of benefit."}]}'
