[11/12 02:50:57] HARNESS: try 1: 21.8 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [\n{"rule": "Play mode lets several shop numbers move per cycle, but a bundle earns no credit and must not be cited as a finding. Only a number changed alone gets a board_pts_h verdict net of the market. Before stepping a number again in the same direction, wait for its last change to have a closed 2 h verdict, and measure the next step at the value now in force.", "evidence": ["F104", "F107"], "status": "verified", "trap": "11/09 13:17 to 15:11 moved stock_value, reserve_cash, warranty_hours and final_frac together (raw margin +578%, +717%). 11/11 11:44 to 13:42 moved a dozen numbers (raw margin +98%, +53%, +37%). All of these were MIXED, so none says which number did what. The only clean reads are F104 (points/h +50% net) and F107 (no difference beyond noise)."},\n{"rule": "Raising stock_value is not a proven lever for points. The one single-change verified read (140000000 -> 150000000) made no difference beyond noise. Look first for changes that speed up turns, and judge any capital change alone.", "evidence": ["F107"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Raising stock_value again and again to get more paid sales. F107 showed value share +16% and raw margin +16% (278/5468 -> 245/5760 sales), which is noise. The later moves to 200000000 and 170000000 were all inside bundles, so they prove nothing either way."},\n{"rule": "max_list has one verified read: 1200000 -> 900000 raised points/h net of the market by 50% (value share +32%, 243/6015 -> 356/5987 sales). Treat any other value as untested, and judge a further move of max_list alone.", "evidence": ["F104"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Treating the later moves (600000 at 11/11 11:44, 1200000 at 11/11 13:42, 900000 at 11/11 17:17, 1200000 at 11/11 22:59) as findings. All were MIXED with no verdict. They neither confirm nor undo 11/10 21:44."},\n{"rule": "Do not revert or build on a code change from a raw before/after read, because it reads the hour