[11/12 05:54:12] HARNESS: try 1: 18.8 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [\n{"rule": "In play mode several shop numbers may move per cycle, but a bundle earns no credit and must not be cited as a finding. Only a number changed alone gets a board_pts_h verdict net of the market. Do not step a number a second time in the same direction until its last change has a closed 2 h verdict, and take evidence for the next step only from the value now in force.", "evidence": ["F104", "F107", "F140", "F141"], "status": "verified", "trap": "11/09 13:17 to 15:11 (F92, F94, F95) moved stock_value, reserve_cash, warranty_hours and final_frac together, and 11/11 11:44 to 13:42 (F108 to F117) moved a dozen numbers. Every row was MIXED with no verdict. On 11/12 the food floor (F140) and ask_frac (F141) were stepped again on audit data measured at the old values, and the supervisor reverted both."},\n{"rule": "Raising stock_value is not a proven lever for points. The one single-change verified read (140000000 -> 150000000) made no difference beyond noise. Look first for changes that speed up turns, and judge any capital change alone.", "evidence": ["F107"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Raising stock_value again and again to buy more paid sales. 11/11 09:39 showed value share +16% and raw margin +16% (278/5468 -> 245/5760 sales), which is noise. The later moves (F105, F109, F117, F142 era) were all MIXED and prove nothing."},\n{"rule": "max_list has one verified read: 1200000 -> 900000 raised points/h net of the market by 50% (value share +32%, 243/6015 -> 356/5987 sales). Treat any other value as untested, and judge a further move of max_list alone.", "evidence": ["F104"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Treating the later moves (600000 at F108, 1200000 at F117, 900000 at F128, 1200000 at F136, 900000 at F142) as findings. All were MIXED with no verdict, so none confirms or refutes F104."},\n{"rule": "Do not revert or build on a code change from a raw before/after read, because it reads the hour of day. Wait for a board_pts_h verdict net of the market. A reverted idea may be restored and judged again.", "evidence": ["F84", "F88", "F90", "F80"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The heat cap 3.0x -> 5.0x (F84) was reverted on a raw shop_margin_h of -20%. After it was restored (F88), the follow-up (F90, hot 150-300k lines capped at 2x heat) was kept with shop_revenue_h +398% and shop points/h +613% net of the market. F80 was also reverted on a raw -36%."},\n{"rule": "Code verdicts that name a MIXED confound (F123, F132, F135, F143) are not evidence for or against that code, even when marked kept or reverted. Judge such code again with a clean window before building on it or removing it.", "evidence": ["F123", "F132", "F135", "F143"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Reading F132 (points/h +810%) as proof the surge guard works, F123 (-167%) and F135 (-113%) as proof they hurt, or F143 (shop_revenue_h -63%) as proof the A-only veto skip is bad. Each shared its hours with other changes."},\n{"rule": "Old MIXED and UNVERIFIED shop rows (11/05 to 11/10 16:21) are no reason to hold or avoid a number. Do not say a number was \'tried both ways\' from them.", "evidence": ["F97", "F101", "F102"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Reading 11/10 12:31 (raw margin -67%) or 11/10 16:20 and 16:21 (raw margin +991%) as proof for or against a stock_value or reserve_cash move. Each had other changes in the same hours."},\n{"rule": "Judge the food shelf-life change (selling food categories need min(min_shelf_hours, 48)) on board_pts_h over a closed window, not on shelf_refused_h, which is only a part of the aim.", "evidence": ["F77"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "F77 was kept although shelf_refused_h was expected -30% and measured +21%. The read was a raw before/after (weak), so it is neither proof of harm nor of benefit."}\n]}'
