[11/12 08:09:45] HARNESS: try 1: 10.7 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Judge forum changes on the forum rating (0-1, not a percentile) and on which of our posts draw dislike stances. Do not judge them on forum_votes_post read as the hour before against the hour after. Never trade post quality for post count.","evidence":["F3","F4"],"status":"unverified","trap":"F3 was reverted on -20% and F4 was kept despite -9%. Both were raw before/after readings that depend on the hour of day, so neither verdict says anything about the change."},{"rule":"The narrowed note() in forum_r3.py (top 4 shops with 2+ settles, last 2 refs per shown shop) is not disproven. It may be retried without an A/B, since A/Bs are off in play mode. Judge it on the forum rating and on whether posts carrying it draw dislikes.","evidence":["F3"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Treating the -20% revert as proof the change was bad. That reading was raw before/after and weak, so a possibly good change was thrown away."},{"rule":"Treat the our_deals cap (a post goes to our_deals only when neither of our last two posts was our_deals) as unproven. Before tuning it, check whether our_deals posts are among those that draw dislikes.","evidence":["F4"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Keeping the cap because 14/14 tests passed. Passing tests show the code runs, not that the cap helps the rating, and the -9% reading was raw before/after and weak."},{"rule":"The post-kind mix (built by code from the ledger, weighted by votes) has no verdict on the rating. Before changing the weighting, break dislikes down by kind, then change the kind that costs the most rating.","evidence":["F1","F2"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Assuming vote weighting is already optimal because it is vote-driven. Neither change has a verdict, so nothing shows the mix avoids dislike stances."},{"rule":"The posting cadence (EVERY 600 -> 310 s, FORMAT_EVERY 360 -> 310) is now fixed by code at the market\'s limit. Do not claim it raised or lowered the rating, and do not tune count further. Spend effort on post quality, meaning which posts draw dislikes.","evidence":["F5","F6"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Citing F6 as proof the 310 s cadence helped. It was MIXED with other changes in the same hours and its forum_votes_post read None -> None, so it gives no verdict. The passing tests (16/16) only show the code runs."}]}'
