[11/12 08:59:09] HARNESS: try 1: 21.2 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Change shop numbers one at a time where you can. In play mode several may move per cycle, but a bundle earns no credit and must not be cited as a finding. Only a number changed alone gets a board_pts_h verdict net of the market. Never step a number a second time in the same direction before its last change has a closed 2 h verdict, and read its value now first. Evidence for a next step must be measured at the value now in force.","evidence":["F104","F107","F140","F141"],"status":"verified","trap":"11/12 00:59 (floor_frac_food 0.52 -> 0.5, dear_depth 5 -> 6) and 11/12 01:16 (ask_frac 0.8 -> 0.85, dear_first 2.75 -> 3.0) stepped again on top of unjudged moves. Both were MIXED with no verdict, so nothing was learned. Only F104 and F107 were clean single-change reads."},{"rule":"Raising stock_value is not a proven lever for points. The one single-change verified read (140000000 -> 150000000) made no difference beyond noise. Look first for changes that speed up turns, and judge any capital change alone.","evidence":["F107"],"status":"verified","trap":"Raising stock_value again and again to buy more paid sales. 11/11 09:39 showed value share +16% and raw margin +16% (278/5468 -> 245/5760 sales), which is noise."},{"rule":"max_list has one verified read: 1200000 -> 900000 raised points/h net of the market by 50% (value share +32%, 243/6015 -> 356/5987 sales). Treat every other value as untested, and judge any further move of max_list alone.","evidence":["F104"],"status":"verified","trap":"Treating the later moves (600000 at 11/11 11:44, 1200000 at 11/11 13:42, 900000 at 11/11 17:17, 1200000 at 11/11 22:59, 900000 at 11/12 01:27) as findings. All were MIXED with no verdict, so none confirms or undoes F104."},{"rule":"Do not revert or build on a code change from a raw before/after read, because it reads the hour of day. Wait for a board_pts_h verdict net of the market. A reverted idea may be restored and judged again.","evidence":["F80","F84","F88","F90"],"status":"verified","trap":"The heat cap 3.0x -> 5.0x (11/09 08:06) was reverted on a raw shop_margin_h of -20%, and 11/09 04:44 on -36%. After 4d10151 was restored (11/09 11:18), the follow-up that capped hot 150-300k lines at 2x heat (11/09 11:33) was kept, with shop_revenue_h +398% and shop points/h +613% net of the market. The raw reads pointed the wrong way."},{"rule":"Code verdicts that name a MIXED confound (11/11 15:35, 11/11 18:52, 11/11 22:27, 11/12 01:46) are not evidence for or against that code, even when marked kept or reverted. Judge such code again with a clean window before building on it or removing it.","evidence":["F123","F132","F135","F143"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Reading 11/11 18:52 (points/h +810%) as proof the surge guard works, 11/11 15:35 (-167%) and 11/11 22:27 (-113%) as proof they hurt, or 11/12 01:46 (shop_revenue_h -63%, reverted) as proof the A-only margin veto exemption is bad. Each had other changes in the same hours."},{"rule":"Old MIXED and UNVERIFIED shop rows (11/05 to 11/10 16:21) are no reason to hold or avoid a number. Do not say a number was \'tried both ways\' from them.","evidence":["F97","F101","F102"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Reading 11/10 12:31 (raw margin -67%) or 11/10 16:20 and 16:21 (raw margin +991%) as proof for or against a stock_value or reserve_cash move. Each had other changes in the same hours and the raw read depends on the hour of day."},{"rule":"Judge the food shelf-life change (selling food categories need min(min_shelf_hours, 48)) on board_pts_h over a closed window, not on shelf_refused_h, which is only a part of the aim.","evidence":["F77"],"status":"unverified","trap":"11/09 01:10 was kept although shelf_refused_h was expected -30% and measured +21%. The read was a raw before/after (weak), so it is neither proof of harm nor of benefit."}]}'
