[11/12 11:01:51] HARNESS: try 1: 35.2 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Judge every buyer change on buyer points/h over closed same-hour windows. Read the points/h and sd figures in the row, not the kept/not taken label. Close rate, saved/deal and seconds per order are parts, never the aim. Rows judged only on those parts, or on raw before/after, are weak.","evidence":["F46","F50","F54","F57","F61","F62","F64"],"status":"verified","trap":"Parts and points/h disagree. On 11/10 08:39 close rate fell 0.775 -> 0.664 while points/h rose +1%. On 11/10 16:04 close rate fell 0.851 -> 0.798 while points/h rose +9%. The kept/not taken label follows the part, so reading it alone gives the wrong call."},{"rule":"FIRM_GAP: read the value now before any move. Do not retry the downward step 0.07 -> 0.05. It lost on points/h twice (11/09 23:48: -35% at -1.1 sd; 11/11 11:18: -18% at -0.5 sd). The upward step 0.07 -> 0.09 gave +2% at -0.2 sd (11/09 18:04), which is noise, so there is no evidence for either direction beyond not going down.","evidence":["F52","F61","F50"],"status":"verified","trap":"The earlier FIRM_GAP wins (11/06 14:50, 11/06 20:57) were judged on saved/deal, a part. The same step 0.07 -> 0.05 then lost on points/h. A saved/deal win does not make a number safe."},{"rule":"CAP: read the value now first. Neither neighbour beat 0.75 on points/h: 0.75 -> 0.8 gave -5% (11/10 03:43); 0.75 -> 0.7 gave +2% at +0.5 sd (11/10 12:26) and +0% at +0.5 sd (11/12 05:22). The differences are noise, so spend no moves on CAP.","evidence":["F53","F56","F67"],"status":"verified","trap":"Older CAP verdicts (11/06 to 11/08) were saved/deal windows that flipped with the hour. The supervisor\'s 0.7 try and its undo (11/09 15:57, 16:14) carry no verdict. Citing them to justify a CAP move is citing noise."},{"rule":"FOOD_MARGIN: read the value now first. Both points/h windows for 1.15 -> 1.1 favour 1.1 (11/10 16:04: +9% at +1.6 sd; 11/11 22:09: +33% at +1.2 sd). Lowering to 1.1 is the one move the points/h evidence supports. Do not go up to 1.2. The 11/09 07:33 1.15 -> 1.2 trial was judged on saved/deal and was not taken.","evidence":["F57","F64","F45"],"status":"verified","trap":"Both 1.15 -> 1.1 rows are labelled not taken although points/h rose, so the label points the wrong way. The 1.1 -> 1.15 win on 11/07 23:45 was judged on saved/deal, a part, and 11/06 17:22 went the other way, so those are no basis. Also do not step the same direction again before the last change has a closed verdict."},{"rule":"Do not loosen the buyer\'s raise limits. MAX_RAISE 0.35 -> 0.3 lost -20% points/h on 11/11 14:49 and was flat at +1% on 11/10 08:39, so there is no gain in going lower. Raising RAISE_GOODS 0.8 -> 0.9 gave -3% at -1.4 sd and RAISE_FOOD 1.2 -> 1.3 gave -14% at -0.4 sd. The only win was MAX_RAISE 0.4 -> 0.35 (+3%, 11/09 10:35).","evidence":["F46","F54","F62","F63","F65"],"status":"verified","trap":"Close rate rose in some of these windows (RAISE_GOODS 0.695 -> 0.729) while points/h fell. Reading close rate would have kept a losing change."},{"rule":"Do not add more buyer ranking or penalty variants (expected-saved-rate sort, break-rate weighting, grade penalties, scout ranking, steeper over-cap exponent). Five tries lost on saved/deal (-2%, -6%, -4%, -2%, -5%), three were reverted, and the exponent 4 -> 8 try lost -9% close rate. The one win only lowered the short-shelf-life food penalty from 0.3 to 0.05 (+3% close rate).","evidence":["F37","F39","F42","F55","F59","F58","F41","F66"],"status":"verified","trap":"11/08 11:55, 11/08 16:36 and 11/10 09:28 were labelled kept although measured saved/deal was -2%, -6% and -2% against expected gains of +3%, +1% and +3%. Expected gains on ranking code have not been met."},{"rule":"Code meant to shorten talks (early cancel, earlier walk-away) must show that it shortens them before it stays, and must also be checked on points/h. Both tries missed their own target.","evidence":["F16","F49"],"status":"verified","t