 move."}, {"rule": "CAP: read the value now first. Neither neighbour clearly beat 0.75 on points/h: 0.75 -> 0.8 gave -5% (11/10 03:43); 0.75 -> 0.7 gave +2% at +0.5 sd (11/10 12:26) and +0% at +0.5 sd (11/12 05:22). The differences are noise, so spend no moves on CAP.", "evidence": ["F53", "F56", "F67"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Older CAP verdicts (11/06 to 11/08) were saved/deal windows that flipped with the hour. The supervisor\'s 0.7 try and its undo (11/09 15:57, 16:14) carry no verdict. Citing them as evidence for a CAP move is a mistake."}, {"rule": "Keep the raise limits where they are (read the values now first: MAX_RAISE 0.35, RAISE_GOODS 0.8, RAISE_FOOD 1.2). MAX_RAISE 0.35 -> 0.3 lost -20% points/h on 11/11 14:49 and was flat at +1% on 11/10 08:39, so going lower gains nothing. Raising RAISE_GOODS 0.8 -> 0.9 gave -3% at -1.4 sd and RAISE_FOOD 1.2 -> 1.3 gave -14% at -0.4 sd. MAX_RAISE 0.4 -> 0.35 gave +3% (11/09 10:35).", "evidence": ["F46", "F54", "F62", "F63", "F65"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Close rate rose in some of these windows (RAISE_GOODS 0.695 -> 0.729, MAX_RAISE 0.725 -> 0.71 aside) while points/h fell. Reading close rate would have kept a losing change."}, {"rule": "Code meant to shorten talks (early cancel, earlier walk-away) must show that it shortens them before it stays, and must also be checked on points/h. Both tries missed their own target.", "evidence": ["F16", "F49"], "status": "verified", "trap": "11/05 17:22 expected -8% seconds per order and measured +1%; 11/09 16:37 expected -5% and measured +13%. Both were marked kept, so the label hid that the change did the opposite of its aim."}, {"rule": "Do not expect gains from rewriting how offers or scouted shops are ranked or penalised. Six same-hours code A/Bs expected a gain and measured a loss: F37 -2%, F39 -6%, F42 -4% (reverted), F55 -2%, F59 -5% (reverted), F66 -9% on close rate (reverted). The only ones that held were small constant changes (F58 lower food shelf-life penalty +3%, matching the expected +3%; F51 paid-rate penalty +1% against +4% expected). Ship a ranking change only as a small constant tweak, and measure it on points/h.", "evidence": ["F37", "F39", "F42", "F55", "F59", "F66", "F58", "F51"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Several losing ranking changes (F37, F39, F55) were marked kept despite negative measured numbers, so the label hid the loss. Their expectations were all positive. Trusting the expected figure in the change note repeats the error."}\n]}'
