[11/12 17:03:28] HARNESS: try 1: 18.5 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Cutting the food floor paid once: floor_frac_food 0.65 -> 0.62 raised shop points/h net of the market by 112% (178/6046 -> 218/6087 sales). Every later food-floor move is MIXED, so none shows that going lower helps. Read the value in force, and do not step the same direction again before the last change has a closed 2 h verdict.","evidence":["F70","F74","F75","F88","F93","F110"],"status":"verified","trap":"Treating the one win as a trend and walking the food floor down (0.6, 0.58, 0.56, 0.53, 0.5), then back up (0.52, 0.53, 0.55). All of those steps shared their hours with other changes, so none can be credited or blamed."},{"rule":"The goods floor gave no gain: floor_frac 0.65 -> 0.63 made no difference beyond noise (value share -14%, raw margin -14%; 293/6225 -> 303/6331 sales). Put goods effort into capital turns, stuck stock and the warranty floor and market line, which set most goods asks.","evidence":["F71","F69","F101","F131"],"status":"verified","trap":"Copying the food-floor win onto goods. The later goods-floor moves (11/09 23:32, 11/11 20:11, 11/12 11:36) are MIXED, and floor_frac 0.66 <-> 0.68 flipped within minutes (11/12 14:51) without a verdict."},{"rule":"Releasing stuck stock sooner paid once: stuck_hours 6 -> 5 raised shop points/h net of the market by 63% (314/6377 -> 294/6145 sales). Faster capital turns are the gap to the top 10. Read the value in force before going lower, and keep stuck sales at or above cost.","evidence":["F72","F73","F79"],"status":"verified","trap":"5 -> 4 shared its hours with a stock_value rise (11/10 11:36), and 4 -> 2 with many other changes (11/11 11:44). Neither has a verdict, so neither shows that going lower works."},{"rule":"market_ask is not a proven lever: 0.9 -> 0.95 made no difference beyond noise (267/5711 -> 242/5675 sales). Do not spend cycles retuning it; put them on levers with a measured effect.","evidence":["F76","F91","F95","F103","F109","F121","F137"],"status":"verified","trap":"Raw margin moves after market_ask changes (11/11 21:06 +102%, 11/12 00:42 -56%) came with other changes in the same hours. Reading them as a market_ask effect is false attribution, and 0.9 -> 0.9 (11/11 13:57) changed nothing."},{"rule":"Only four shop changes have a one-at-a-time verdict: 11/10 01:43, 11/10 05:04, 11/10 07:19 and 11/11 03:09. A MIXED change, one that shares its hours with another, is no evidence whatever its raw margin says. In play mode, move different numbers each cycle so later changes can be judged.","evidence":["F70","F71","F72","F76","F66","F74","F101","F123"],"status":"verified","trap":"Raw margin swings such as +717% (11/09 13:40), +497% (11/10 17:23) and +125% (11/11 20:11) came with other changes in the same hours. Writing them up as wins, or building lessons on them, repeats the mistake."},{"rule":"Check the value in force before every number change (orders 5 and 9). Never move a number toward a value it already has, and never take a second step in the same direction before the last has a closed 2 h verdict. A different number or the opposite direction is free. This rests on the supervisor\'s orders, not on measured wins, so it is weak.","evidence":["F63","F64","F65","F90","F98","F99","F111","F112","F113","F114","F115"],"status":"unverified","trap":"ask_frac_food was raised 0.7 -> 0.75 and put back within a minute (11/09 12:06, 11/09 12:07). On 11/12 01:16 ask_frac stepped 0.8 -> 0.85 -> 0.8, citing data measured at old values; the supervisor reverted it. Such churn wastes cycles and blurs every later verdict."},{"rule":"Never recommend the 11/09 06:43 \'costco\' bundle values (floor_frac 0.45, floor_frac_food 0.45, min_margin 0.14, step 0.5, max_turns 4, ask_frac 0.85, ask_frac_food 0.85). The supervisor undid them (11/09 07:02, 07:21, 09:21). Never recommend any value a later row undid.","evidence":["F57","F58","F59","F60"],"status":"contradicted","trap":"The bundle looked good on raw margin (+30%) but cut paid sales over 06:43-09:21 per the orders. Reusing its values, or any value a later row undid, repeats that loss."}]}'
