[11/12 17:20:20] HARNESS: try 1: 22.6 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [\n{"rule": "Judge every buyer change on buyer points/h over closed same-hour windows. Read the points/h and sd figures in the row, not the kept/not taken label. Close rate, saved/deal and seconds per order are parts, never the aim. Never lean on a MIXED row such as F60.", "evidence": ["F46", "F50", "F54", "F57", "F61", "F62", "F64", "F68"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Parts and points/h disagree. On 11/10 08:39 close rate fell 0.775 -> 0.664 while points/h rose +1%. On 11/10 16:04 close rate fell 0.851 -> 0.798 while points/h rose +9%. On 11/12 11:03 close rate fell 0.855 -> 0.69 and points/h fell -42%, so the parts can also look fine while the aim is lost. Reading the label or a part gives the wrong call either way."},\n{"rule": "FOOD_MARGIN: read the value now first (it was 1.15 in both tests). Lowering 1.15 -> 1.1 won on points/h twice: +9% at +1.6 sd (11/10 16:04) and +33% at +1.2 sd (11/11 22:09). Both rows were labelled not taken, so the label hides a consistent gain. If the value is still 1.15, take the 1.1 step once. In play mode no A/B is needed, but check the 2 h verdict before stepping again in that direction.", "evidence": ["F57", "F64"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Skipping the move because the rows say not taken. The older rows (F45 1.15 -> 1.2 not taken, F33 keep of 1.15 on 11/07 23:45) were judged on saved/deal, a part, and do not outweigh two points/h gains. Also never move it toward a value it already has."},\n{"rule": "FIRM_GAP: leave it at 0.07 (read the value now first). Both directions lost on points/h: 0.07 -> 0.05 gave -35% at -1.1 sd (11/09 23:48) and -18% at -0.5 sd (11/11 11:18); 0.07 -> 0.09 gave -42% at -2.6 sd (11/12 11:03) and only +2% with saved -0.2 sd (11/09 18:04). Spend no more moves on it.", "evidence": ["F50", "F52", "F61", "F68"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Older rows kept 0.05 and 0.07 on saved/deal windows (F23, F25, F31, F40) that flipped with the hour. Citing them would restart a loop that points/h has already closed."},\n{"rule": "CAP: read the value now first. Neither neighbour clearly beat 0.75 on points/h: 0.75 -> 0.8 gave -5% (11/10 03:43); 0.75 -> 0.7 gave +2% at +0.5 sd (11/10 12:26) and +0% at +0.5 sd (11/12 05:22). The differences are noise, so spend no moves here.", "evidence": ["F53", "F56", "F67"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Older CAP verdicts (11/06 to 11/08) were saved/deal windows that flipped with the hour. The supervisor\'s 0.7 try and its undo (F47, F48) carry no verdict. Chasing saved/deal at 0.7 raised it (0.3993 -> 0.4044) while points/h stayed flat."},\n{"rule": "Keep the raise limits where they are (read the values now first: MAX_RAISE 0.35, RAISE_GOODS 0.8, RAISE_FOOD 1.2). MAX_RAISE 0.35 -> 0.3 lost -20% points/h on 11/11 14:49 and was flat at +1% on 11/10 08:39. RAISE_GOODS 0.8 -> 0.9 gave -3% at -1.4 sd and RAISE_FOOD 1.2 -> 1.3 gave -14%, so going higher loses too.", "evidence": ["F46", "F54", "F62", "F63", "F65"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Close rate rose in some of these windows (RAISE_GOODS 0.695 -> 0.729) while points/h fell. Reading close rate would have kept a losing change."},\n{"rule": "Code meant to shorten talks (early cancel, earlier walk-away) must show that it shortens them before it stays, and must also be checked on points/h. Both tries missed their own target.", "evidence": ["F16", "F49"], "status": "verified", "trap": "11/05 17:22 expected -8% seconds per order and measured +1%; 11/09 16:37 expected -5% and measured +13%. Both were marked kept, so the label hid that the change did not do what it promised."},\n{"rule": "Do not expect gains from rewriting how offers or scouted shops are ranked or penalised. Six same-hours code A/Bs expected a gain and measured a loss: F37 -2%, F39 -6%, F42 -4% (reverted), F55 -2%, F59 -5% (reverted), F66 -9% on close rate (reverted). Only two small penalty tweaks won, and only on close rate, a part: F58 +3% and F51 +1%. Treat a new ranking idea as a likely loss; if you try one, name the metric and watch points/h.", "evidence": ["F37", "F39", "F42", "F55", "F59", "F66", "F58", "F51"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Several losing ranking changes (F37, F39, F55) were marked kept despite negative measured numbers, so the label hid the loss. Every expectation was positive (+1% to +4%), so the confidence of the author predicts nothing."}\n]}'
