[11/12 17:20:48] HARNESS: try 1: 9.2 s, exit 0, answer '{"proposal": {"FOOD_MARGIN": 1.1}, "recruit": null, "why": "FOOD_MARGIN is in force at 1.15, and lowering it to 1.1 won on buyer points/h in both closed windows (+9% at +1.6 sd on 11/10 16:04, +33% at +1.2 sd on 11/11 22:09), so this is one step in the direction the evidence supports. CAP, FIRM_GAP and the raise limits stay where they are because their neighbours showed no clear points/h gain, and I see no buyer-team style that has been verified on points/h yet.", "ideas": ["Checkout refusals with \'unit ... is\' errors account for 5 of 100 recent payments and are a code path problem, not a price one: have the buyer re-check unit availability right before checkout and drop the order cleanly instead of failing it.", "The forum rating needs posts that draw no dislike stances, and no buyer number can change that; a code-side check on which post topics earn dislikes, run on the 100-post window, would show where to post."], "lessons_used": ["L1", "L2", "L3", "L4", "L5"]}'
[11/12 17:20:51] HARNESS: try 1: 12.1 s, exit 0, answer '{"proposal": {}, "why": "The two open changes (max_list 800000 -> 1100000 with its verdict due 17:41, and sku_depth 4 -> 3 at 17:04 with its verdict due 19:04) mean moving max_list up again or sku_depth down again would break order 9 and bundle a second change into the same hours as the pending verdicts, so I\'m holding them. Nothing else in the evidence supports a single-number change that would speed turns cleanly: 800 of 1441 units are older than 24 h, but the sales-to-stock link is confounded by the pending moves, and the lone clean window_depth read was too noisy to repeat.", "ideas": ["Clear the stale stock: 800 units older than 24 h at cost is capital that earns nothing, and the stuck-goods rule (sell down to cost, never under) is the direct fix for turn speed, not another depth or capital number."], "lessons_used": ["L1", "L5"]}'
