ce": ["F50", "F52", "F61", "F68"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Older rows kept 0.05 and 0.07 on saved/deal windows (11/06 14:50, 11/06 20:57, 11/07 10:29, 11/08 17:55) that flipped with the hour. Citing them restarts a loop that points/h has already closed. The 0.09 step looked free after +2% but lost -42% on the next try.", "when": ["11/09 18:04", "11/09 23:48", "11/11 11:18", "11/12 11:03"]}, {"rule": "CAP: read the value now first. Neither neighbour clearly beat 0.75 on points/h: 0.75 -> 0.8 gave -5% (11/10 03:43); 0.75 -> 0.7 gave +2% at +0.5 sd (11/10 12:26) and +0% at +0.5 sd (11/12 05:22). The differences are noise, so spend no more moves here until a new measurement says otherwise.", "evidence": ["F53", "F56", "F67"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Older CAP verdicts (11/06 to 11/08) were saved/deal windows that flipped with the hour, and the supervisor\'s 0.7 try and its undo (F47, F48) carry no verdict. Chasing the small saved/deal gain at 0.7 (0.3993 -> 0.4044) while points/h stayed at +0%.", "when": ["11/10 03:43", "11/10 12:26", "11/12 05:22"]}, {"rule": "Keep the raise limits where they are (read the values now first: MAX_RAISE 0.35, RAISE_GOODS 0.8, RAISE_FOOD 1.2). MAX_RAISE 0.35 -> 0.3 gave -20% points/h on 11/11 14:49 and +1% on 11/10 08:39; 0.35 -> 0.25 gave -2% on 11/12 14:51. RAISE_GOODS 0.8 -> 0.9 gave -3% at -1.4 sd. RAISE_FOOD 1.2 -> 1.3 gave -14%. Only 0.4 -> 0.35 helped (+3%).", "evidence": ["F46", "F54", "F62", "F63", "F65", "F69"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Close rate rose in some windows (RAISE_GOODS 0.695 -> 0.729) and saved/deal rose in others (MAX_RAISE 0.4053 -> 0.4097) while points/h fell. Reading those parts would have kept losing changes.", "when": ["11/09 10:35", "11/10 08:39", "11/11 14:49", "11/11 19:08", "11/12 01:27", "11/12 14:51"]}, {"rule": "Be doubtful of new ranking or scouting code that promises a gain: most of it measured at or below zero on its own metric. Reverted: scout_wave expected-saved-rate ranking (11/1