[11/12 23:23:44] HARNESS: try 1: 21.8 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [\n{"rule": "Judge every buyer change on buyer points/h over a closed same-hour A/B window, and read the points/h and sd figures in the row, not the kept/not taken label. Close rate, saved/deal and seconds per order are parts, never the aim. Read the number\'s value now before moving it, and never step it a second time in the same direction before its last change has a closed 2 h verdict.", "evidence": ["F46", "F54", "F57", "F61", "F62", "F64", "F68"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Parts and points/h disagree. On 11/10 08:39 close rate fell 0.775 -> 0.664 while points/h rose +1%. On 11/10 16:04 close rate fell 0.851 -> 0.798 while points/h rose +9%. On 11/12 11:03 close rate fell 0.855 -> 0.69 and points/h fell -42%. Deciding on the label or on a part gives the wrong call in either direction."},\n{"rule": "FOOD_MARGIN: read the value now first (it was 1.15 in both tests). Moving 1.15 -> 1.1 won on points/h twice: +9% at +1.6 sd (11/10 16:04) and +33% at +1.2 sd (11/11 22:09). Treat it as the best-supported move on this number and make it as a single step. Do not go back up: 1.15 -> 1.2 was not taken on 11/09 07:33.", "evidence": ["F57", "F64", "F45"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Both winning rows carry the label not taken, so skipping the move because of the label throws away the best evidence on this number. The older keep of 1.15 (11/07 23:45) was judged on saved/deal and is weak."},\n{"rule": "FIRM_GAP: leave it at 0.07 (read the value now first). Both directions lost on points/h: 0.07 -> 0.05 gave -35% at -1.1 sd (11/09 23:48) and -18% at -0.5 sd (11/11 11:18); 0.07 -> 0.09 gave -42% at -2.6 sd (11/12 11:03) and only +2% at -0.2 sd (11/09 18:04). Do not retest it without new evidence.", "evidence": ["F50", "F52", "F61", "F68"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Older rows kept 0.05 and 0.07 on saved/deal windows (11/06 14:50, 11/06 20:57, 11/07 10:29, 11/08 17:55) that flipped with the hour. Citing them restarts a loop that the points/h rows have already closed."},\n{"rule": "CAP: read the value now first. Neither neighbour clearly beat 0.75 on points/h: 0.75 -> 0.8 gave -5% (11/10 03:43); 0.75 -> 0.7 gave +2% at +0.5 sd (11/10 12:26) and +0% at +0.5 sd (11/12 05:22). The differences are noise, so spend no more trials on CAP and look at other numbers.", "evidence": ["F53", "F56", "F67"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Older CAP verdicts (11/06 to 11/08) were saved/deal windows that flipped with the hour, and the supervisor\'s 0.7 try and its undo (11/09 15:57, 11/09 16:14) carry no verdict. Citing them as proof for 0.7 or 0.8 is false. Small saved/deal gains (0.3709 -> 0.3739, 0.399 -> 0.4044) came with flat or lower points/h."},\n{"rule": "Keep the raise limits where they are (read the values now first: MAX_RAISE 0.35, RAISE_GOODS 0.8, RAISE_FOOD 1.2). MAX_RAISE 0.4 -> 0.35 won +3% (11/09 10:35), but going lower lost: 0.35 -> 0.3 gave -20% on 11/11 14:49 and +1% on 11/10 08:39, and 0.35 -> 0.25 gave -2% on 11/12 14:51. RAISE_GOODS 0.8 -> 0.9 gave -3% at -1.4 sd, and RAISE_FOOD 1.2 -> 1.3 gave -14%.", "evidence": ["F46", "F54", "F62", "F63", "F65", "F69"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Close rate rose in some windows (RAISE_GOODS 0.695 -> 0.729) and saved/deal rose in others (MAX_RAISE 0.4053 -> 0.4097) while points/h fell. Reading those parts as wins would loosen raises that cost points."},\n{"rule": "Be doubtful of new ranking, scouting or penalty code that promises a gain: most of it measured at or below zero on its own metric. Reverted: scout_wave expected-saved-rate ranking (11/11 00:28, -5%), over-cap exponent 8 (11/12 05:07, -9% close rate) and the grade-based ranking (11/08 21:36, -4%). Kept but measured negative or flat: break-rate weighting (-6%, 11/08 16:36), soft-breaks (-2%, 11/10 09:28), warranty-on-receipt (+0%, 11/12 16:48). Only the short-shelf-life food penalty cut (+3% close rate, 11/10 17:41) measured positive. Expect a gain only from a measured win, and check new code on points/h.", "evidence": ["F39", "F42", "F55", "F58", "F59", "F66", "F70"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The meta-agent\'s expected gains were +1% to +4% in every row, yet most measured negative. These rows were judged on saved/deal or close rate, which are parts, so even a kept label says nothing about points/h."},\n{"rule": "Code meant to shorten talks (early cancel, earlier walk-away) must show that it shortens them before it stays, and must also be checked on points/h. Both tries missed their own target.", "evidence": ["F16", "F49"], "status": "verified", "trap": "11/05 17:22 expected -8% seconds per order and measured +1%; 11/09 16:37 expected -5% and measured +13%. Both were marked kept, so the label hid that the change did the opposite of its aim."}\n]}'
