[11/13 00:30:45] HARNESS: try 1: 20.4 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Only a change shipped alone earns a board_pts_h verdict net of the market. In the whole record only F104 and F107 are such reads. Play mode lets several numbers and code changes ship per cycle, but a bundle earns no credit. Never cite a MIXED row, its raw margin, or a MIXED code verdict as proof for or against a value. When you pick the next step, read the value now in force and the supervisor\'s orders on repeat steps, and do not lean on MIXED history.","evidence":["F104","F107","F132","F143","F123"],"status":"verified","trap":"Reading MIXED rows as findings. Raw margin swung from -70% (F141) to +222% (F148) with other changes in the same hours. MIXED code verdicts disagree in sign: F132 measured +151% margin, F143 -63% revenue and was reverted, F123 -37%. They are noise, not rules. Window_depth went 2.8 -> 2.5 and back 2.5 -> 2.8 in the same minute (F174, F175), a reversal that no read supported."},{"rule":"max_list has one verified read: 1200000 -> 900000 raised shop points/h net of the market by 50% (value share +32%, 243/6015 -> 356/5987 sales), judged on 11/10 21:44. Every later move was in a bundle and is untested. Read the value in force before touching it. Do not step it again in the same direction before its last change has a closed 2 h verdict.","evidence":["F104","F128","F136","F142","F155","F170","F177"],"status":"verified","trap":"Treating the later moves as findings. They went 900000 -> 600000 -> 1200000 -> 900000 -> 1200000 -> 900000 -> 800000 -> 1100000 -> 900000, all MIXED, and they largely undid each other. The one verified read says nothing about 800000 or 1100000."},{"rule":"Raising stock_value is not a proven lever for points. The only verified single-change read (140000000 -> 150000000) made no difference beyond noise (value share +16%, 278/5468 -> 245/5760 sales). Look first for changes that speed up turns, and judge capital changes alone when you can.","evidence":["F107"],"status":"verified","trap":"Stepping stock_value up and down to buy more paid sales (F105, F109, F112, F115, F117, F156). All of those rows are MIXED, so none shows what capital does for points."},{"rule":"Do not recommend values from the 11/11 11:44-13:33 sweep, which changed up to six numbers per cycle (goods_frac 0.45, food_first 1.0, clear_age_hours 6, min_margin 0.02, dear_depth 2, surge_max 1). Cycle 11/11 13:42 reversed much of it (stock_value to 170000000, max_list to 1200000, goods_frac to 0.7), and later cycles moved the same numbers again.","evidence":["F108","F113","F114","F117","F118"],"status":"contradicted","trap":"Citing the raw margin gains beside the sweep rows (+98%, +53%, +49%, +32%) as support for those values. Every row carries the same other changes, so none can be credited, and the cycle that followed undid most of the sweep."}]}'
