[11/13 05:29:18] HARNESS: try 1: 31.4 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [{"rule": "Judge every buyer change on buyer points/h over a closed same-hour A/B window. Read the points/h and sd figures in the row, not the kept/not taken label. Close rate, saved/deal and seconds per order are parts, never the aim. Read the number\'s value now before any move. In the latest windows (11/12 19:00 to 11/13 02:10) points/h is negative in both arms, so a percentage there is a change in a negative base. Compare the absolute values and the sd before calling it a win.", "evidence": ["F46", "F54", "F57", "F61", "F62", "F64", "F68", "F71", "F73", "F74"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Parts and points/h disagree. On 11/10 08:39 close rate fell 0.775 -> 0.664 while points/h rose +1%. On 11/11 22:09 FOOD_MARGIN lost the \'not taken\' label while points/h rose +33%. On 11/12 22:18 points/h went -0.000773 -> -0.000958 (-24%) while saved/deal rose, so the sign of the percent and the direction of the change are easy to misread. Rows before 11/9 11:13 rest on windows that flipped with the hour; do not cite them."}, {"rule": "FOOD_MARGIN: read the value now first (it was 1.15 in all three 1.1 tests). Moving 1.15 -> 1.1 beat 1.15 on points/h twice, +9% at +1.6 sd (11/10 16:04) and +33% at +1.2 sd (11/11 22:09). The third try (11/12 22:18) went the other way on points/h, -0.000773 -> -0.000958 (-24%), although saved difference was +1.4 sd. The evidence leans to 1.1 but is split 2 to 1. Do not move it again until a clean closed same-hour window is read at the value now in force. 1.15 -> 1.2 was not taken (11/09 07:33).", "evidence": ["F57", "F64", "F73", "F45"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The 1.1 rows carry the label \'not taken\'. Skipping the move because of the label throws away the best evidence on this number. Equally, citing only the two wins ignores the 11/12 22:18 loss on points/h. That loss came on saved/deal +1.4 sd, which shows saved/deal alone does not decide."}, {"rule": "FIRM_GAP: