se a limit that the points/h record does not support."}, {"rule": "Be doubtful of new ranking, scouting or penalty code that promises a gain. Most of it measured at or below zero on its own metric. Reverted: the break-rate weighting (11/08 16:36, -6%, undone by 11/08 19:53), grade-based ranking (11/08 21:36, -4%), scout_wave expected-saved-rate ranking (11/11 00:28, -5%) and the over-cap exponent 8 (11/12 05:07, -9% close rate). Others measured at or near zero on their own targets: 11/10 09:28 -2%, 11/12 16:48 +0%, 11/09 21:40 +1%. Only the 11/10 17:41 food-penalty cut measured +3%, on close rate. Ship such code only behind a flag with a closed same-hour window, and expect no gain.", "evidence": ["F39", "F41", "F42", "F55", "F58", "F59", "F66", "F70"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The meta-agent\'s expected gains were +1% to +4% in every row, yet most measured negative. The positive ones were only on parts (close rate, seconds per order), not on points/h. The \'kept\' label on a +0% or -2% row hides that it added nothing."}, {"rule": "Code meant to shorten talks (early cancel, earlier walk-away) must show that it shortens them before it stays, and must also be checked on points/h. Two tries missed their own target. The scouting drop of over-cap shops (11/12 21:47) did shorten orders (+22% against an expected +10%, on the seconds-per-order metric). Its effect on points/h is not shown in the row, so check it there before building on it.", "evidence": ["F16", "F49", "F72"], "status": "verified", "trap": "11/05 17:22 expected -8% seconds per order and measured +1%. 11/09 16:37 expected -5% and measured +13%. Both were marked kept, so the label hid that the change did not do what it was built for."}, {"rule": "MAX_TRIES 6 -> 5 has one points/h read: +14% at +0.5 sd on 11/12 19:00 (close rate 0.866 -> 0.8, both windows with negative points/h). It is a single weak result, so repeat it on a closed same-hour window, read the value now first, and do not adopt it from this row alone.", "evidence": ["F71"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The row is labelled not taken and the close rate fell, so it is easy to dismiss. The earlier 11/05 try (11/05 16:16) was a surplus/close-rate window that read the hour of day, so it is no evidence either way. A +14% on a negative base is not proof of a win."}]}'
