[11/13 05:45:59] HARNESS: try 1: 10.5 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [{"rule": "Judge forum changes on the forum rating (0-1, counted as itself) and on which of our posts draw dislike stances, broken down by post kind. Do not judge them on forum_votes_post read as the hour before against the hour after.", "evidence": ["F3", "F4"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "F3 was reverted on -20% and F4 was kept despite -9%. Both were raw before/after readings that depend on the hour of day, so neither verdict shows whether the change helped. These facts are weak."}, {"rule": "The narrowed note() in forum_r3.py (top 4 shops with 2+ settles, last 2 refs per shown shop) is not disproven. It can be retried in play mode without an A/B. Judge it on the forum rating and on whether posts carrying it draw dislike stances.", "evidence": ["F3"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Treating the -20% revert as proof the change was bad. The reading was raw before/after and weak, so a possibly good change may have been thrown away."}, {"rule": "Treat the our_deals cap (a post goes to our_deals only when neither of our last two posts was our_deals, about 1 post in 3) as unproven. Before tuning it, check whether our_deals posts are among those that draw dislikes.", "evidence": ["F4"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Keeping the cap because the tests passed (14/14). Passing tests show the code runs, not that the cap helps the rating. The -9% reading was raw before/after and weak."}, {"rule": "The post-kind mix (built by code from the ledger, weighted by votes) has no verdict on the rating. Do not assume vote weighting is optimal. Check dislike stances by kind and change the mix where a kind draws them.", "evidence": ["F1", "F2"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Assuming the mix is fine because it is vote-driven. F1 and F2 have no verdict, so nothing shows the mix avoids dislike stances."}, {"rule": "Posting cadence is fixed by code at the market\'s 310 s limit. Do not tune count further and do