[11/13 08:30:26] HARNESS: try 1: 23.0 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Judge every buyer change on buyer points/h and its sd in the row, not on the kept/not taken label. Close rate, saved/deal and seconds per order are parts, never the aim. Read the value now before moving a number. Shop A/Bs are off in play mode, so use an A/B for a buyer number only when it is cheap. Never cite a MIXED row (F60) or a no-verdict row (F75) as evidence.","evidence":["F46","F54","F57","F61","F62","F64","F68","F71","F73","F74"],"status":"verified","trap":"Parts and points/h disagree. In F54 close rate fell 0.775 -> 0.664 while points/h rose +1%. In F71 and F74 both windows had negative points/h, so a percent change there is easy to misread. In F64 the \'not taken\' label hid +33% points/h."},{"rule":"FOOD_MARGIN: read the value now first. In F57 and F64, lowering it from 1.15 to 1.1 beat 1.15 on points/h, +9% at +1.6 sd and +33% at +1.2 sd. F73 went the other way: points/h -0.000773 -> -0.000958 (-24%) although saved difference was +1.4 sd. The evidence is two wins and one loss, so a move to 1.1 is allowed, but judge it on points/h and do not repeat it from the label alone.","evidence":["F57","F64","F73"],"status":"verified","trap":"All three 1.1 rows carry \'not taken\'. Skipping the move for that label throws away the best evidence on this number. Citing only the two wins hides F73, and F73\'s negative base makes -24% hard to read."},{"rule":"FIRM_GAP: leave it at 0.07 (read the value now first). Both directions lost on points/h. 0.07 -> 0.05 gave -35% at -1.1 sd (F52) and -18% at -0.5 sd (F61). 0.07 -> 0.09 gave -42% at -2.6 sd (F68) and only +2% at -0.2 sd (F50). Do not retry either step without a new reason.","evidence":["F50","F52","F61","F68"],"status":"verified","trap":"Older FIRM_GAP rows (F23, F25, F31, F40) were saved/deal windows that flipped with the hour. Citing them restarts a loop that points/h already closed."},{"rule":"CAP: no neighbour clearly beat the value now (read it first). 0.75 -> 0.8 gave -5% points/h (F53). 0.75 -> 0.7 gave +2% at +0.5 sd (F56) and +0% at +0.5 sd (F67). These differences are noise, so spend no more cycles on CAP unless the evidence is new.","evidence":["F53","F56","F67"],"status":"verified","trap":"Older CAP rows (F22, F32, F34, F38, F43) were saved/deal windows that flipped with the hour. F47 and F48 are supervisor moves with no verdict, so they prove nothing."},{"rule":"Raise limits: leave MAX_RAISE, RAISE_GOODS and RAISE_FOOD alone (read the values now first). MAX_RAISE 0.4 -> 0.35 won +3% (F46). Going lower gave +1% (F54), -20% (F62) and -2% (F69). RAISE_GOODS 0.8 -> 0.9 gave -3% (F63) and +15% at -0.1 sd (F74), with both F74 windows negative. RAISE_FOOD 1.2 -> 1.3 gave -14% (F65).","evidence":["F46","F54","F62","F63","F65","F69","F74"],"status":"verified","trap":"Close rate rose in some windows (F63: 0.695 -> 0.729) and saved/deal rose in others (F69: 0.4053 -> 0.4097) while points/h fell. F74\'s +15% is a weak read on negative bases, so do not build a raise from it."},{"rule":"Be doubtful of new ranking, scouting or penalty code that promises +1% to +4%. Most of it measured at or below zero on its own metric. Reverted: F39 (-6%), F42 (-4%), F59 (-5%), F66 (-9%). Others measured -2% (F55) or +0% (F70). F58 (+3% close rate) is the one clear positive. Ship such code only if it can be judged, and revert it on a negative window.","evidence":["F39","F41","F42","F55","F58","F59","F66","F70"],"status":"verified","trap":"The meta-agent\'s expected gains were +1% to +5% in nearly every row, yet most measured negative. A \'kept\' label with a measured -2% (F55) is not a win."},{"rule":"Code meant to shorten talks (early cancel, earlier walk-away, scout drops) must show that it shortens them, and must also be checked on points/h. F16 expected -8% seconds per order and measured +1%. F49 expected -5% and measured +13%. Only F72 (expected +10%, measured +22%, + is better) hit its target.","evidence":["F16","F49","F72"],"status":"verified","trap":"F16 and F49 were marked kept although they missed their target, so the label hid that the change did nothing or made talks longer. F72\'s win was on seconds per order only, with no points/h read in the row."},{"rule":"MAX_TRIES 6 -> 5 has one points/h read: +14% at +0.5 sd (F71), with close rate 0.866 -> 0.8 and both windows negative in points/h. It is a single weak result, so repeat it before relying on it (read the value now first), and judge on points/h, not close rate.","evidence":["F71"],"status":"verified","trap":"The row says \'not taken\' and close rate fell, so it is easy to dismiss. The older F15 was a surplus/close-rate window with a different read, so do not use it as a verdict on points/h."}]}'
