[11/13 11:13:54] HARNESS: try 1: 21.0 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Do not submit a change and its reversal within minutes of each other. The net effect is zero, and each row adds a confound to every other change in those hours. If the evidence does not settle a direction, leave the number alone this cycle. Also do not log a no-op row such as 0.9 -> 0.9.","evidence":["F90","F91","F110","F111","F113","F114","F130","F131","F139","F140","F149","F150","F154","F155","F157","F158","F160","F161"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Stepping a number up and straight back down, as with floor_frac_food at 11/12 00:59, 20:23 and 22:18/22:19, ask_frac at 01:16, floor_frac at 11:36 and 14:51, and market_ask at 11/13 00:48. All of these rows are MIXED, so the pair proves nothing, and the supervisor reverted several of the steps (F112, F115, F132, F141, F151, F156). This rests on process, not on a measured effect.","when":["11/12 00:59","11/12 01:16","11/12 11:36","11/12 14:51","11/12 20:23","11/12 22:19","11/13 00:48"]},{"rule":"Before the next step on a number, measure the evidence at the value now in force. Do not step it again in the same direction before its last change has a closed 2 h verdict. Do not return to a value whose own row closed negative without a new measurement taken after it.","evidence":["F110","F111","F113","F114","F129","F130","F139","F141","F149","F154","F156"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Raising floor_frac_food again (11/12 11:19, 20:23, 22:18) and returning floor_frac to 0.68 (11/12 14:51), each time citing audit data from an older value. The returns after the negative-looking rows F129 and F130 were reverted by the supervisor. The raw reads on those rows are MIXED, so the rule rests on standing order 9, not on a verdict.","when":["11/12 11:19","11/12 14:51","11/12 20:23","11/12 22:18"]},{"rule":"Do not cite a raw margin swing on a MIXED row as evidence for or against a number. No shop number row from F85 to F164 is a verdict. Argue from board points per hour, the rivals and edges tables, or a change made alone in its hours.","evidence":["F90","F91","F109","F121","F131","F152","F153","F160"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Reading a raw margin figure such as -56% (11/12 00:42), +63% (11/12 06:57) or +83% (11/12 21:12) as the effect of one number, when other numbers or code changes moved in the same hours. Raw margin also reads the hour of day. This is a rule about method, not a measured effect.","when":["11/12 00:42","11/12 06:57","11/12 21:12","11/13 00:48"]},{"rule":"To clear grade-A units priced above the market, use a clearance rule (clear_floor or the stuck rule), not a lower market_ask. Their floor is cost/(1-WARRANTY_Q), and the market cap never goes under cost plus margin, so a lower market_ask only cuts the price of units that already sell.","evidence":["F160","F161","F163","F164"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Lowering market_ask 1.0 -> 0.95 to move the unsold pile (11/13 00:48, 06:03). It was reverted by the supervisor each time, and the rows are MIXED, so no verdict. The code-floor reasoning comes from standing order 11, not from a measured effect.","when":["11/13 00:48","11/13 06:03"]},{"rule":"Several shop numbers and code changes landing in the same hours make every row MIXED. In play mode, still log which changes shared the hours, and do not read any one row as proof for its own number.","evidence":["F85","F86","F95","F101","F105","F145","F153","F163"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Treating the +125% (F101) or +83% (F152) raw margin rows as proof of one number when code changes and other numbers moved in the same hours. This is a caution about how to read the record, not a measured effect.","when":["11/11 20:11","11/12 21:12"]}]}'
