[11/13 14:16:26] HARNESS: try 1: 17.0 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Do not submit a change and its reversal in the same few minutes. The pair nets to zero and adds a confound to every other change in those hours. If the evidence does not settle a direction, leave the number alone this cycle.","evidence":["F90","F91","F113","F114","F130","F131","F139","F140","F149","F150","F154","F155","F157","F158","F160","F161"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Stepping a number up and straight back down, e.g. floor_frac at 11/12 11:36 and 14:51, floor_frac_food at 20:23 and 22:18/22:19, fresh_premium at 23:41/23:42, market_ask at 00:48. Each pair changed nothing and made the neighbouring rows MIXED. This rests on MIXED rows, so it is a record-keeping caution, not a measured effect."},{"rule":"Before moving a number again, measure the evidence at the value now in force. Do not step it a second time in the same direction before its last change has a closed 2 h verdict. Do not return to a value whose own row closed negative without a new measurement taken after it. Check the supervisor\'s standing orders for holds on that number first.","evidence":["F99","F112","F115","F117","F129","F130","F132","F139","F141","F149","F151","F154","F156"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Raising floor_frac_food (11/12 11:19, 20:23, 22:18) and returning floor_frac to the older value (11/12 14:51), each time citing audit data from the old value. The supervisor reverted these, as the [supervisor] code rows show (F99, F112, F132, F141, F151, F156). The raw figures are on MIXED rows, so they are not verdicts."},{"rule":"Do not lower market_ask to clear grade-A units priced above the market. Their floor is set by cost and warranty, so a lower market_ask only cuts the price of units that already sell. Use a clearance rule for that pile, and keep market_ask where the standing orders hold it.","evidence":["F148","F160","F161","F163","F164"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Lowering market_ask to 0.95 on 11/13 00:48 and 06:03 and raising it back within the same hours each time. Both moves landed with other changes, so neither has a verdict. The repeated lowering was reverted and gave no evidence."},{"rule":"Do not cite a raw margin swing on a MIXED row as evidence for or against a number. No shop number row from 11/11 13:21 to 11/13 10:09 is a verdict. Argue from board points per hour, the rivals and edges tables, or a change made alone in its hours. When several numbers or code changes land in the same hours, log which ones shared them and do not treat any one row as proof of its own number.","evidence":["F101","F105","F109","F121","F145","F152","F153","F163","F165","F166"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Reading +125% (11/11 20:11), -56% (11/12 00:42), +83% (11/12 21:12) or +163% (11/13 09:37) as the effect of one number when other numbers and code changes moved in the same hours. The raw margin also reads the hour of day."}]}'
