[11/13 14:33:39] HARNESS: try 1: 26.8 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [\n{"rule": "Judge every buyer change on buyer points/h and its sd, never on the kept/not taken label or on close rate, saved/deal or seconds per order, which are only parts. Read the number\'s value now before moving it. Do not move it a second time in the same direction before the last change has a closed 2 h verdict. Do not return to a value whose own verdict was negative without a new measurement taken after it.", "evidence": ["F54", "F57", "F61", "F62", "F64", "F68", "F71", "F73", "F74", "F75"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The parts and points/h disagree. 11/10 08:39: close rate 0.775 -> 0.664 while points/h was +1%. 11/12 22:18: saved difference +1.4 sd but points/h -24%. 11/11 22:09: points/h +33% sat beside a loss on the same number the next day. A \'kept\' or \'not taken\' label can contradict the points/h read.", "when": ["11/10 08:39", "11/10 16:04", "11/11 11:18", "11/11 14:49", "11/11 22:09", "11/12 11:03", "11/12 19:00", "11/12 22:18", "11/13 02:10", "11/13 07:58"]},\n{"rule": "FOOD_MARGIN 1.15 -> 1.1 has been judged in both directions on points/h: +9% at +1.6 sd (11/10 16:04), +33% at +1.2 sd (11/11 22:09) and -24% (11/12 22:18). It is not clearly better, so do not repeat it as a test. If it is moved in play mode, read the value now first and treat the result as a single noisy read.", "evidence": ["F57", "F64", "F73"], "status": "verified", "trap": "All three rows say \'not taken\'. Skipping the number for that label discards two wins, while citing only the wins hides the 11/12 22:18 loss. Going the other way is also not a free pass: 1.15 -> 1.2 (11/09 07:33) was judged only on saved/deal, so it is no evidence.", "when": ["11/10 16:04", "11/11 22:09", "11/12 22:18"]},\n{"rule": "CAP: no neighbour clearly beat the value now (read it first). 0.75 -> 0.8 gave -5% (11/10 03:43). 0.75 -> 0.7 gave +2% at +0.5 sd (11/10 12:26) and +0% at +0.5 sd (11/12 05:22). These are noise, so spend no cycles on CAP without new evidence.", "evidence": ["F53", "F56", "F67"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Older CAP rows were judged on saved/deal and flipped with the hour. The 11/09 supervisor moves had no verdict, so none of them is evidence. Close rate rose 0.733 -> 0.787 on 11/12 05:22 while points/h stayed flat.", "when": ["11/10 03:43", "11/10 12:26", "11/12 05:22"]},\n{"rule": "Raise limits: leave MAX_RAISE, RAISE_GOODS and RAISE_FOOD alone (read the values now first). MAX_RAISE 0.4 -> 0.35 won +3% (11/09 10:35). Going lower gave +1% (11/10 08:39), -20% (11/11 14:49) and -2% (11/12 14:51). RAISE_GOODS 0.8 -> 0.9 gave -3% (11/11 19:08) and +15% on 11/13 02:10 with both arms negative. RAISE_FOOD 1.2 -> 1.3 gave -14%.", "evidence": ["F46", "F54", "F62", "F63", "F65", "F69", "F74"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Close rate or saved/deal rose in some windows (11/11 19:08 close rate 0.695 -> 0.729) while points/h fell. 11/13 02:10 showed +15% but with both arms negative and saved difference -0.1 sd, so it is not a clear win; do not build on it.", "when": ["11/09 10:35", "11/10 08:39", "11/11 14:49", "11/11 19:08", "11/12 01:27", "11/12 14:51", "11/13 02:10"]},\n{"rule": "FIRM_GAP: keep the value now (read it first). 0.07 -> 0.05 lost on points/h three times: -35% (11/09 23:48), -18% (11/11 11:18). 0.07 -> 0.09 gave +2% at -0.2 sd (11/09 18:04) and -42% at -2.6 sd (11/12 11:03). Neither direction has won, so do not retest without a new measurement.", "evidence": ["F50", "F52", "F61", "F68"], "status": "verified", "trap": "11/12 11:03 close rate fell 0.855 -> 0.69 and points/h -42%, but 11/11 11:18 close rate was flat (0.788 -> 0.79) while points/h still fell -18%. Close rate does not predict the sign. The +2% on 11/09 18:04 is noise at -0.2 sd, not a reason to go up.", "when": ["11/09 18:04", "11/09 23:48", "11/11 11:18", "11/12 11:03"]},\n{"rule": "Treat new ranking, scouting or penalty code that promises +1% to +4% with doubt. Most of it measured at or below zero on its own metric. Reverted: 11/08 21:36 (-4%), 11/11 00:28 (-5%), 11/12 05:07 (-9%). Others measured -6% (11/08 16:36), -2% (11/10 09:28) and -3% (11/13 07:58). Require a clear win on points/h before keeping code of this kind.", "evidence": ["F39", "F42", "F55", "F58", "F59", "F66", "F70", "F75"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The meta-agent expected +1% to +10% nearly every time. \'Kept\' with a measured -2% (11/10 09:28) or -3% (11/13 07:58) is not a win. 11/10 17:41 (+3% close rate) and 11/12 16:48 (+0%) were judged on parts, so they are not points/h wins either.", "when": ["11/08 16:36", "11/08 21:36", "11/10 09:28", "11/10 17:41", "11/11 00:28", "11/12 05:07", "11/12 16:48", "11/13 07:58"]},\n{"rule": "Code meant to shorten talks (early cancel, earlier walk-away, scout drops) must show that it shortens them and must also be checked on points/h. Only the scout drop of 11/12 21:47 shortened talks, with seconds per order +22% against +10% expected. Even that row has no points/h read yet.", "evidence": ["F16", "F49", "F72"], "status": "verified", "trap": "11/05 17:22 (expected -8%, measured +1%) and 11/09 16:37 (expected -5%, measured +13%) were marked kept although they missed. 11/12 21:47 was judged on seconds per order only, so faster talks may not mean more points.", "when": ["11/05 17:22", "11/09 16:37", "11/12 21:47"]},\n{"rule": "MAX_TRIES 6 -> 5 has one points/h read: +14% at +0.5 sd (11/12 19:00), with close rate 0.866 -> 0.8 and both arms negative. It is a single weak result, so confirm it before relying on it. Read the value now first and judge on points/h.", "evidence": ["F71"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The row says \'not taken\' and close rate fell, so it is easy to dismiss. The 11/05 16:16 row was judged on surplus and close rate, so it does not count against it. Equally, +14% with both arms negative is not proof it is better.", "when": ["11/12 19:00"]}\n]}'
