9","F121","F145","F152","F153","F163","F165","F166"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Reading +125% (11/11 20:11), -56% (11/12 00:42), +83% (11/12 21:12) or +163% (11/13 09:37) as the effect of one number when several numbers and code changes moved in the same hours.","when":["11/11 20:11","11/11 21:51","11/12 00:42","11/12 06:57","11/12 17:21","11/12 21:12","11/12 21:46","11/13 06:03","11/13 09:37","11/13 10:09"]},{"rule":"When a code change to restock_r3.py, buyer_r3.py or the seller lands, hold the shop numbers for its 2 h window so the code change can get a verdict of its own. Change numbers in the other area, or wait.","evidence":["F95","F101","F105","F114","F153","F163","F165","F167","F168"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Moving several numbers beside a code change, such as the heat or plan-mode changes, so that code and numbers both read MIXED and the code\'s effect on board points cannot be separated.","when":["11/11 15:59","11/11 20:11","11/12 01:16","11/12 21:46","11/13 06:03","11/13 09:37","11/13 12:22"]},{"rule":"Do not lower market_ask to clear grade-A units priced above the market. Their price rests on a cost-based floor, so the cut only lowers the price of units that already sell. Clear that pile with a clearance rule (clear_floor or the stuck rule) instead.","evidence":["F160","F161","F163","F164"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Lowering market_ask to 0.95 at 11/13 00:48 and 06:03 on a pile it cannot reach. Each time it was undone within minutes (F161, F164), which left only noise.","when":["11/13 00:48","11/13 06:03"]}]}'
