[11/13 17:35:23] HARNESS: try 1: 22.1 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [\n{"rule": "Judge every buyer change on buyer points/h and its sd, not on the kept/not taken label, close rate, saved/deal or seconds per order, which are only parts. Read the number\'s value now before moving it. Do not move it a second time in the same direction until the last change has a closed 2 h verdict.", "evidence": ["F54", "F57", "F61", "F62", "F64", "F68", "F71", "F73", "F74", "F75"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The parts and points/h disagree. 11/10 08:39: close rate 0.775 -> 0.664 while points/h was +1%. 11/12 22:18: saved difference +1.4 sd but points/h -24%. 11/11 14:49: saved difference -0.1 sd and close rate flat, yet points/h -20%. A \'kept\' label can also hide a miss: 11/13 07:58 was kept at -3% points/h."},\n{"rule": "FOOD_MARGIN 1.15 -> 1.1 is a mixed result on points/h: +9% at +1.6 sd (11/10 16:04), +33% at +1.2 sd (11/11 22:09) and -24% (11/12 22:18). It is not clearly better, so do not count on it. If it is moved, read the value now first and judge on points/h.", "evidence": ["F57", "F64", "F73"], "status": "verified", "trap": "All three rows say \'not taken\'. Skipping the number for that label discards two wins, while citing only the wins hides the 11/12 22:18 loss. Citing the +33% alone would overstate it."},\n{"rule": "CAP: no neighbour clearly beat the value now (read it first). 0.75 -> 0.8 gave -5% (11/10 03:43). 0.75 -> 0.7 gave +2% at +0.5 sd (11/10 12:26) and +0% at +0.5 sd (11/12 05:22). These are noise, so spend no cycles on CAP without new evidence.", "evidence": ["F53", "F56", "F67"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Older CAP rows were judged on saved/deal and flipped with the hour. The 11/09 supervisor moves (F47, F48) had no verdict, so they are not evidence. In F67 saved/deal and close rate rose (0.733 -> 0.787) while points/h stayed at +0%."},\n{"rule": "FIRM_GAP: from 0.07 (read the value now) both neighbours lost on points/h. 0.07 -> 0.05 gave -35% (11/09 23:48) and -18% (11/11 11:18). 0.07 -> 0.09 gave +2% (11/09 18:04) and -42% at -2.6 sd (11/12 11:03). Leave it alone unless there is a new reason.", "evidence": ["F50", "F52", "F61", "F68"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The +2% at 0.09 (11/09 18:04) was small and came with saved difference -0.2 sd and close rate 0.68 -> 0.612. It is no case for 0.09. The earlier 0.05 and 0.07 rows were judged on saved/deal and went both ways, so they say nothing."},\n{"rule": "Raise limits: leave MAX_RAISE, RAISE_GOODS and RAISE_FOOD alone (read the values now first). MAX_RAISE 0.4 -> 0.35 won +3% (11/09 10:35). Going lower gave +1% (11/10 08:39), -20% (11/11 14:49) and -2% (11/12 14:51). Going back up to 0.4 gave -5% (11/13 11:32). RAISE_GOODS 0.8 -> 0.9 gave -3% (11/11 19:08) and +15% (11/13 02:10), RAISE_FOOD 1.2 -> 1.3 gave -14% (11/12 01:27).", "evidence": ["F46", "F54", "F62", "F63", "F65", "F69", "F74", "F76"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Close rate or saved/deal rose in some windows (11/11 19:08 close rate 0.695 -> 0.729; 11/13 11:32 saved difference +2.1 sd) while points/h fell. 11/13 02:10 showed +15% but both arms were negative, so it is not a reliable win."},\n{"rule": "Treat new ranking, scouting or penalty code that promises +1% to +4% with doubt. Most of it measured at or below zero on its own metric. Reverted: 11/08 21:36 (-4%), 11/11 00:28 (-5%), 11/12 05:07 (-9%). Others measured -6% (11/08 16:36), -2% (11/10 09:28), +0% (11/12 16:48) and -1% (11/13 13:13). Only the 11/10 17:41 food-penalty cut (+3% close rate, as expected) delivered what it promised.", "evidence": ["F39", "F42", "F55", "F58", "F59", "F66", "F70", "F75", "F77"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The meta-agent expected +1% to +10% nearly every time. \'Kept\' with a measured -2% (11/10 09:28) or -3% (11/13 07:58) is not a win. The 11/10 17:41 row was judged on close rate, not points/h, so it is not proof of a board gain."},\n{"rule": "Code meant to shorten talks (early cancel, earlier walk-away, scout drops) must show that it shortens them and must also be checked on points/h. Only the scout drop of 11/12 21:47 shortened talks, with seconds per order +22% against +10% expected.", "evidence": ["F16", "F49", "F72"], "status": "verified", "trap": "11/05 17:22 (expected -8%, measured +1%) and 11/09 16:37 (expected -5%, measured +13%) were marked kept although they missed. 11/12 21:47 was judged on seconds per order, not points/h, so its board effect is unknown."},\n{"rule": "MAX_TRIES 6 -> 5 has one points/h read: +14% at +0.5 sd (11/12 19:00), with close rate 0.866 -> 0.8 and both arms negative. It is a single weak result, so confirm it before relying on it. Read the value now first and judge on points/h.", "evidence": ["F71"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The row says \'not taken\' and close rate fell, so it is easy to dismiss. The 11/05 16:16 row (F15) was judged on surplus and close rate, so it does not count against it."}\n]}'
