[11/13 21:42:26] HARNESS: try 1: 20.6 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Treat every shop number row from F140 to F219 as no verdict. Each one is MIXED with other changes in its hours, so the raw margin figure beside it is not the effect of that number. Pick the next number from the rivals and edges tables (order 4) and from its value now (order 5), not from these raw margin readings.","evidence":["F141","F148","F185","F204","F209","F219"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Raw margin swings of +222% (F148), -70% (F141), +136% (F204) and -72% (F209) were read as the effect of the one number moved, although each row lists several other changes in the same hours."},{"rule":"Judge a code change on shop points/h, the supervisor\'s aim, not on revenue or margin. When they disagree, points/h decides. Every code verdict so far was MIXED with number changes, so each is weak evidence and none is proof.","evidence":["F143","F187","F195","F214"],"status":"unverified","trap":"F143 was reverted on shop_revenue_h -63% while points/h read +182%. F195 read shop_margin_h -142% with points/h -2%, and F214 read revenue +64% with points/h -24%. Following the revenue or margin figure alone points the wrong way."},{"rule":"\'Kept\' is not proof that a code change helped. Read the points/h figure beside it before building on the change.","evidence":["F158","F164","F195","F214"],"status":"unverified","trap":"F158, F164, F195 and F214 were all kept while points/h read -64%, -57%, -2% and -24%. Treating kept as a win left those throttles standing."},{"rule":"Do not add another stale-unit or hot-line throttle to restock_r3.py. F214 (the hot cheap goods cap) now has its verdict: revenue +64% but points/h -24%, the third such guard with negative points/h. Order 3 wants faster turns and more paid sales from the same capital. Make a new guard only if it shows points/h at or above zero, or loosen an existing one.","evidence":["F158","F164","F214"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Each guard cuts restocking and looked reasonable alone. F158, F164 and F214 each read negative on points/h, so stacking another repeats the pattern."},{"rule":"Do not repeat a move the supervisor reverted, such as lowering market_ask or raising floor_frac_food, unless a measurement taken after the revert supports it (order 9 return clause). The review times of orders 10 and 11 have passed, but that does not count as new evidence; a food-floor raise now needs a one-step A/B.","evidence":["F160","F178","F181","F186","F198"],"status":"unverified","trap":"market_ask was lowered at F186 and F198, and the food floor was raised at F160, F178 and F181. Each was justified by a MIXED raw margin reading and then reverted."},{"rule":"Never move a number and move it back in the same cycle, and never step it again in the same direction before its last change has a closed 2 h verdict (order 9). Read the value now and its recent rows first (order 5).","evidence":["F174","F175","F182","F183","F204","F205","F206","F207"],"status":"unverified","trap":"F204 and F205 moved max_list 600000 and back to 900000.0 in the same minute. F182 and F183 moved fresh_premium and dear_depth and reverted them a minute later (the supervisor logged F184). F174 and F175 moved window_depth both ways in the same minute. These produce no verdict and only churn."}]}'
