> 12 in 9 steps, each with other numbers or code changing in the same hours (all MIXED). No row says which value is better, and the swings in raw margin (+14% to +83% and -20%) say nothing about it."}, {"rule": "Do not cite a raw margin swing on a MIXED row as evidence for or against a number. Argue from board points per hour and the rivals and edges tables, and only from rows judged one number at a time.", "evidence": ["F101", "F105", "F109", "F121", "F145", "F152", "F153", "F163", "F165", "F166", "F170"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Reading +125% (11/11 20:11), -56% (11/12 00:42), +83% (11/12 21:12), +163% (11/13 09:37) or +290% (11/13 18:09) as the effect of one number, when several numbers or code rules changed in the same hours. Raw margin also reads the hour of day."}, {"rule": "To clear grade-A units priced above the market, do not lower market_ask. Their floor is cost/(1-WARRANTY_Q) and the market cap never takes a floor under cost plus margin, so a lower market_ask only cuts the price of units that already sell. Use a clearance rule (clear_floor, the stuck rule) instead.", "evidence": ["F160", "F161", "F163", "F164"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "market_ask was lowered 1.0 -> 0.95 twice (11/13 00:48 and 06:03) to clear the pile, and each was reverted within minutes. The rows are MIXED, so this rests on the supervisor\'s reasoning about the floor, not on a verdict."}]}'
