[11/13 23:39:32] HARNESS: try 1: 20.9 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Judge every buyer number change on buyer points/h and its sd, never on the kept/not taken label, close rate, saved/deal or seconds per order. Read the number\'s value now before moving it, and do not move it a second time in the same direction before the last change has a closed 2 h verdict.","evidence":["F54","F57","F61","F68","F73","F75","F76"],"status":"verified","trap":"The parts and points/h disagree. 11/10 08:39: close rate 0.775 -> 0.664 while points/h was +1%. 11/12 22:18: saved difference +1.4 sd but points/h -24%. 11/13 11:32: saved difference +2.1 sd and close rate 0.789 -> 0.842 but points/h -5%. Acting on a part would have picked the wrong arm."},{"rule":"FOOD_MARGIN 1.15 -> 1.1 is a mixed result on points/h, so do not count on it either way. Read the value now first, and if it is tried again judge it on points/h and sd.","evidence":["F57","F64","F73"],"status":"verified","trap":"All three rows say \'not taken\'. Skipping the number for that label discards two wins (+9% at +1.6 sd, +33% at +1.2 sd), while quoting only those hides the -24% at +1.4 sd. Any single row can be quoted to support either direction."},{"rule":"CAP: no neighbour clearly beat the value now (read it first). 0.75 -> 0.8 gave -5% points/h, and 0.75 -> 0.7 gave +2% at +0.5 sd and +0% at +0.5 sd. These are noise, so spend no cycles on CAP without new evidence measured at the value in force.","evidence":["F53","F56","F67"],"status":"verified","trap":"In F67 saved/deal (0.3993 -> 0.4044) and close rate (0.733 -> 0.787) rose while points/h was flat at +0%. Reading the parts would make 0.7 look like a win. Older CAP rows judged on saved/deal flipped with the hour and are not evidence."},{"rule":"FIRM_GAP: both neighbours of 0.07 have lost on points/h (read the value now). 0.07 -> 0.05 gave -35%, -18% and a weak +6% at -0.4 sd. 0.07 -> 0.09 gave +2% at -0.2 sd and -42% at -2.6 sd. It has been judged in both directions, so do not repeat either move.","evidence":["F50","F52","F61","F68","F78"],"status":"verified","trap":"The latest 0.05 row (F78, +6%) has both arms negative and saved difference -0.4 sd, and the +2% at 0.09 (F50) came with close rate 0.68 -> 0.612. Either can be quoted as a win, but neither is one against -35%, -18% and -42%."},{"rule":"Raise limits (MAX_RAISE, RAISE_GOODS, RAISE_FOOD): no direction has a clear points/h win, so leave them alone. Read the values now first. MAX_RAISE gave +3%, +1%, -20% and -2% going down and -5% going up. RAISE_FOOD 1.2 -> 1.3 gave -14%. RAISE_GOODS 0.8 -> 0.9 gave -3% and +15%.","evidence":["F46","F54","F62","F63","F65","F69","F74","F76"],"status":"verified","trap":"Close rate or saved/deal rose in some windows (F63 close rate 0.695 -> 0.729; F76 saved difference +2.1 sd) while points/h fell. The +15% of F74 has saved difference -0.1 sd and is the only RAISE_GOODS gain, against -3% in F63, so it is not enough on its own."},{"rule":"Treat new ranking, scouting, penalty or plan-mode code that promises +1% to +10% with doubt. Most of it measured at or below zero on its own metric. Reverted: -4% (F42), -5% (F59), -9% (F66). Others measured -6% (F39), -2% (F55), +0% (F70), -3% (F75), -1% (F77). Only F58 (+3% expected, +3% measured) delivered.","evidence":["F39","F42","F55","F58","F59","F66","F70","F75","F77"],"status":"verified","trap":"The meta-agent expected +1% to +10% nearly every time. \'Kept\' with a measured -2% (F55) or -3% (F75) is not a win, only a failure to reach the revert threshold. Do not cite these rows as support for similar code."},{"rule":"Code meant to shorten talks (early cancel, earlier walk-away, scout drops) must show that it shortens them and must also be checked on points/h. Only the scout drop of F72 shortened talks (seconds per order +22% against +10% expected).","evidence":["F16","F49","F72"],"status":"verified","trap":"F16 (expected -8%, measured +1%) and F49 (expected -5%, measured +13%) were marked kept although seconds per order got no better or got worse. F72 is judged on seconds per order, not on points/h, so it does not show that talks shorter in time earn more."},{"rule":"MAX_TRIES 6 -> 5 has one points/h read: +14% at +0.5 sd (F71), with close rate 0.866 -> 0.8 and both arms negative. It is a single weak result, so do not rely on it without a new measurement. Read the value now first and judge on points/h.","evidence":["F71"],"status":"verified","trap":"The row says \'not taken\' and close rate fell, so it is easy to dismiss. It is also easy to overrate: +14% from a negative base (-0.001089 -> -0.000936) at +0.5 sd is weak. The earlier 11/05 read (F15) is before the points/h basis and does not count."}]}'
