[11/14 06:00:52] HARNESS: try 1: 10.5 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Judge forum changes on the forum rating (0-1, counted as itself) and on which of our posts draw dislike stances, broken down by post kind. Do not judge them on forum_votes_post read as the hour before against the hour after. Never trade post quality for count.","evidence":["F3","F4"],"status":"unverified","trap":"F3 was reverted on -20% and F4 was kept despite -9%. Both were raw before/after readings that depend on the hour of day, so neither verdict is evidence either way."},{"rule":"The narrowed note() in forum_r3.py (top 4 shops with 2+ settles, last 2 refs per shown shop) is not disproven. It may be retried in play mode without an A/B. Judge it on the forum rating and on whether posts carrying it draw dislike stances.","evidence":["F3"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Treating the -20% revert as proof the change was bad. The reading was raw before/after and weak, so a possibly good change was thrown away."},{"rule":"Treat the our_deals cap (a post goes to our_deals only when neither of our last two posts was our_deals) as unproven. Before tuning it, check by post kind whether our_deals posts are among those that draw dislikes.","evidence":["F4"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Keeping the cap because the tests passed (14/14). Passing tests show the code runs, not that the cap helps the rating. The -9% reading was raw before/after and weak."},{"rule":"The post-kind mix (built by code from the ledger, weighted by votes) has no verdict on the rating. Do not assume vote weighting is optimal. Check dislike stances by kind and shift the mix away from kinds that draw them.","evidence":["F1","F2"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Assuming the mix is fine because it is vote-driven. Neither change has a verdict, so nothing shows the mix avoids dislike stances."},{"rule":"Do not credit or blame the posting cadence for any forum result. Code fixes it at the market\'s 310 s limit, so do not retune FORMAT_EVERY. Put effort into post quality and kind instead.","evidence":["F5"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Citing the FORMAT_EVERY 360 -> 310 change (F6) as proof the faster cadence helped. F6 was MIXED with open_gap and dear_depth changes in the same hours and showed forum_votes_post None -> None, so it is no verdict and no basis for a lesson."}]}'
