[11/14 06:51:07] HARNESS: try 1: 21.7 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Treat every shop number row from 11/12 13:27 to 11/14 04:39 as no verdict. Each one is MIXED with other changes in the same hours, so the raw margin figure beside it is not that number\'s effect. Pick the next number from the standing orders, the rivals table and the edges table, not from these rows.","evidence":["F185","F204","F209","F217","F227","F241"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Raw margin swings of +84% (F185), +136% (F204), -72% (F209) and +204% (F217) were read as the effect of the one number moved, but each row lists other changes in the same hours."},{"rule":"Judge a code change on shop points/h, the aim. When revenue or margin disagree with points/h, points/h decides. Every code verdict so far is MIXED with number changes, so it is weak evidence, not proof.","evidence":["F164","F187","F195","F214","F226","F238"],"status":"unverified","trap":"F195 showed margin -142% while points/h was -2%. F214 showed revenue +64% while points/h was -24%. F226 showed revenue +46% while points/h was -11%. Reading the part instead of the aim misjudges the change."},{"rule":"Do not add more stale-unit clamps (heat 1.0, mult 1, half-cost room) to restock. All three stale changes closed negative on points/h: -57%, -24% and -11%. They are mixed, so this is weak, but there is no evidence they help the board. Free stuck capital with the seller\'s stuck/clearance rule instead.","evidence":["F164","F214","F226"],"status":"unverified","trap":"F214 and F226 were kept on revenue gains (+64%, +46%) while points/h fell. F164 also read revenue -17% against its expected +3%."},{"rule":"Do not cap dear (150k+) line depth by market-sales or sellable-share signals. The share-scaled depth (F195) gave points/h -2%. The 6 h market-settle cap (F238) gave points/h -32%, margin -69%, and the guard said revert it. If that cap is still in code, remove it.","evidence":["F195","F238"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Both changes sounded like risk control and were kept on expected +5%, but measured margin was -142% and -69%. Capping depth cut paid sales, which are the shop\'s gap to the top 10."},{"rule":"Keep the grade-A expected_margin valuation (sell only draws at or under the market median, charge A_HOLD for the rest). It is the only code change with a large positive points/h (+335%). It is mixed with number changes, so treat it as promising but not proven, and do not stack more tweaks on it without a new reading.","evidence":["F187"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Its own follow-on (F195) extended the same idea to depth scaling and went flat or negative (points/h -2%). A good change does not prove its extension."},{"rule":"Do not reverse a number you moved a cycle or two ago, and do not return to values already refused. dear_depth 5->4 was reverted every time (F230, F240), and sku_depth 3->2 (F235) was reverted by the supervisor, so keep dear_depth 5 and sku_depth at 3 or more. A different number is free in play mode.","evidence":["F230","F231","F235","F236","F240","F241"],"status":"unverified","trap":"dear_depth 4 (F230, F240) and sku_depth 2 (F235) were proposed as a different number from past moves. The supervisor reverted them (F232, F237, F242) because their own verdicts had closed negative."},{"rule":"Do not make a move and its undo in the same hours. Such pairs leave both rows MIXED and the cycle with no information. Make one clear move per number, then read it.","evidence":["F204","F205","F223","F224","F230","F231"],"status":"unverified","trap":"max_list 900000->600000 and back (F204, F205), window_depth 2.0->1.5 and back (F223, F224), and dear_depth 5->4->5.0 (F230, F231) each ended at the starting value after a wasted cycle."}]}'
