 first step has a closed 2 h verdict. Measure the next step at the value now in force.", "evidence": ["F106", "F107", "F111", "F113", "F114", "F115"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "ask_frac went 0.72 -> 0.77 (11/11 22:09), 0.77 -> 0.8 (11/11 23:18) and then 0.8 -> 0.85 with dear_first 2.75 -> 3.0 (11/12 01:16). That is three same-direction steps in about three hours, each with other numbers moving. The 0.85 step was undone to 0.8 by the supervisor (F115), and no step had a clean verdict."},\n{"rule": "Do not cite a raw margin swing from a MIXED row as the effect of one number. In play mode almost every row is MIXED, so argue from board_pts_h, the rivals table and the edges table. Treat a swing as a lead to measure, never as a result.", "evidence": ["F101", "F109", "F152", "F165", "F170", "F175"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Reading +125% (11/11 20:11), -56% (11/12 00:42), +83% (11/12 21:12), +163% (11/13 09:37), +290% (11/13 18:09) or +21% (11/14 06:02) as the effect of one number, when 3-5 other numbers or code changes fell in the same hours. Raw margin also reads the hour of day, so a number chosen on such a swing may be pure noise."}\n]}'
