[11/14 08:49:12] HARNESS: try 1: 12.4 s, exit 0, answer '{"proposal": {}, "recruit": {"MAX_RAISE": 0.3, "FIRM_GAP": 0.05, "OPEN": "p25"}, "why": "All four buyer team styles and their rewards are negative (-0.108 to -0.124) and all open low, so the buyer team\'s haggling approach is the weak part, while every numeric lever in our lessons is either judged mixed (CAP, FOOD_MARGIN, FIRM_GAP, raise limits) or has no closed verdict in its favour, so no number should move this cycle. A recruit with a different opening (p25) and mid-range raise and gap values tests the one variable the team has not varied, and it is not a repeat of any judged number move.", "ideas": ["tool: a per-grade break-adjusted saved figure in the buyer ledger, so the saved term counts refunds on C (18.8% break rate in 24 h) and A at their true cost, not only at the list-price gap.", "Read the forum\'s dislike stances on our posts (rating 0.917, top posts all +8) and tune post wording on the posts that draw dislikes, since the rating counts as itself and is the 0.3 part of our buyer ALL, which the number tuning cannot reach."], "lessons_used": ["L1", "L2", "L3", "L4", "L5"]}'
