[11/14 09:05:52] HARNESS: try 1: 12.3 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [\n{"rule": "Judge forum changes on the forum rating (0-1, counted as itself) and on which of our posts draw dislike stances, broken down by post kind. Do not use forum_votes_post read as the hour before against the hour after. Never trade post quality for post count.", "evidence": ["F3", "F4"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "F3 (11/05 09:22) was reverted on -20% and F4 (11/05 10:57) was kept despite -9%. Both were raw before/after readings that depend on the hour of day, so neither outcome is evidence. Both are weak, unverified facts."},\n{"rule": "Neither forum code change of 11/05 is proven good or bad. The narrowed note() (top 4 shops with 2+ settles, last 2 refs per shown shop) and the our_deals cap (no our_deals post when either of our last two posts was one) can be retried or tuned in play mode without an A/B. First check by post kind whether the posts they shape draw dislike stances, then decide.", "evidence": ["F3", "F4"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Reading the F3 revert as proof the change was bad, or keeping the F4 cap because 14/14 tests passed. Passing tests only show the code runs, not that the rating improves. Both readings were weak raw before/after."},\n{"rule": "The post-kind mix (built by code from the ledger, weighted by votes) has no verdict on the rating. Do not assume vote weighting is optimal. Count dislike stances per kind and shift the mix away from the kinds that draw them.", "evidence": ["F1", "F2"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Assuming the mix is fine because it is vote-driven. Neither F1 nor F2 has a verdict, so nothing shows the mix avoids dislike stances."},\n{"rule": "Do not credit or blame posting cadence for any forum result. Code fixes it at the market\'s 310 s limit, so do not retune FORMAT_EVERY. Put the effort into post quality and kind.", "evidence": ["F5"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Citing the FORMAT_EVERY 360 -> 310 change (F6, 11/11 07:13) as proof the faster cadence helped. F6 was MIXED with open_gap and dear_depth changes in the same hours, so it gives no verdict. F5 has no verdict either."}\n]}'
