[11/14 11:52:23] HARNESS: try 1: 25.8 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Judge every buyer number change on buyer points/h and its sd, never on the kept/not taken label, close rate, saved/deal or seconds per order. Read the number\'s value now before moving it (order 5). Never step it a second time in the same direction before the last change has a closed 2 h verdict (order 9).","evidence":["F46","F54","F57","F61","F64","F68","F73","F76","F79","F80"],"status":"verified","trap":"The parts and points/h disagree. 11/10 08:39: close rate 0.775 -> 0.664 while points/h was +1%. 11/12 22:18: saved difference +1.4 sd but points/h -24%. 11/13 11:32: saved difference +2.1 sd but points/h -5%. 11/11 22:09: points/h +33% with close rate 0.75 -> 0.776. Reading only the parts, or the \'not taken\' label, picks the wrong number.","when":["11/09 10:35","11/10 08:39","11/11 22:09","11/12 22:18","11/13 11:32","11/13 23:57","11/14 04:38"]},{"rule":"FOOD_MARGIN 1.15 -> 1.1 has been judged in both directions on points/h: +9% (+1.6 sd), +33% (+1.2 sd) and -24% (+1.4 sd). The result is mixed, so do not repeat the step (order 2). Read the value now first. Only a new measurement taken at the value in force justifies moving it.","evidence":["F57","F64","F73"],"status":"verified","trap":"All three rows say \'not taken\'. Skipping the number on that label discards two wins. Quoting only the wins hides the -24% of 11/12 22:18. The saved difference was positive (+1.4 sd) in that losing window too, so it does not predict points/h.","when":["11/10 16:04","11/11 22:09","11/12 22:18"]},{"rule":"CAP: no neighbour of the value now clearly beat it (read it first). 0.75 -> 0.8 gave -5% points/h. 0.75 -> 0.7 gave +2% at +0.5 sd, +0% at +0.5 sd and -11% at -0.0 sd. Treat this as noise leaning negative, and spend no cycles on CAP without a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F53","F56","F67","F80"],"status":"verified","trap":"On 11/12 05:22 saved/deal (0.3993 -> 0.4044) and close rate (0.733 -> 0.787) rose while points/h was flat at +0%. On 11/14 04:38 saved/deal was flat (0.4157 -> 0.4156) while points/h was -11%. A move sold on the parts buys nothing on the board.","when":["11/10 03:43","11/10 12:26","11/12 05:22","11/14 04:38"]},{"rule":"Raise limits (MAX_RAISE, RAISE_GOODS, RAISE_FOOD): no direction has a clear points/h win, so leave them alone unless a new measurement says otherwise. Read the values now first. MAX_RAISE going down gave +3% (0.4 -> 0.35), +1%, -20%, -2% and -17%; 0.35 -> 0.3 was judged +1%, -20% and -17%, so do not repeat it. MAX_RAISE 0.35 -> 0.4 gave -5%. RAISE_GOODS 0.8 -> 0.9 gave -3% and +15%. RAISE_FOOD 1.2 -> 1.3 gave -14%.","evidence":["F46","F54","F62","F63","F65","F69","F74","F76","F79"],"status":"verified","trap":"Close rate or saved/deal rose in some windows (11/11 19:08 close rate 0.695 -> 0.729, 11/13 11:32 saved difference +2.1 sd) while points/h fell. The +15% of 11/13 02:10 came with a saved difference of -0.1 sd and the -3% of 11/11 19:08 is the same number, so one window cannot be trusted over the other.","when":["11/09 10:35","11/10 08:39","11/11 14:49","11/11 19:08","11/12 01:27","11/12 14:51","11/13 02:10","11/13 11:32","11/13 23:57"]},{"rule":"FIRM_GAP: 0.07 held against every tried move on points/h. 0.07 -> 0.05 gave -35%, -18% and +6% (at -0.4 sd). 0.07 -> 0.09 gave +2% (-0.2 sd) and -42% (-2.6 sd). Do not move it without a new measurement taken at the value in force.","evidence":["F50","F52","F61","F68","F78"],"status":"verified","trap":"The +6% (11/13 14:35) and +2% (11/09 18:04) are small and sit with negative saved differences, so they are not wins. Citing them would hide the -35% and -42% results. Close rate 0.788 -> 0.79 on 11/11 11:18 also hid -18% points/h.","when":["11/09 18:04","11/09 23:48","11/11 11:18","11/12 11:03","11/13 14:35"]},{"rule":"Treat new ranking, scouting, penalty or plan-mode code that promises +1% to +10% with doubt. Most of it measured at or below zero on its own metric. Reverted: -4% (11/08 21:36), -5% (11/11 00:28), -9% (11/12 05:07). Others measured -6% (11/08 16:36), -2% (11/10 09:28), -3% (11/13 07:58) and -1% (11/13 13:13). Ask for a test of the claim and the points/h read before building on it.","evidence":["F39","F42","F55","F59","F66","F75","F77"],"status":"verified","trap":"The meta-agent expected +1% to +10% nearly every time. \'Kept\' with a measured -2% (11/10 09:28) or -3% (11/13 07:58) is not a win, only a failure to reach the revert line. Building the next change on a kept row with a negative measurement stacks losses.","when":["11/08 16:36","11/08 21:36","11/10 09:28","11/11 00:28","11/12 05:07","11/13 07:58","11/13 13:13"]},{"rule":"Code meant to shorten talks (early cancel, earlier walk-away, scout drops) must show that it shortens them, and must also be checked on points/h. Only the scout drop of 11/12 21:47 shortened talks (seconds per order +22% against +10% expected, + is better). The early cancel and the earlier walk-away did not.","evidence":["F16","F49","F72"],"status":"verified","trap":"11/05 17:22 (expected -8%, measured +1%) and 11/09 16:37 (expected -5%, measured +13%) were marked kept although seconds per order got no better or got worse. A shorter talk that loses closes is no gain, and the F72 row says nothing about points/h either.","when":["11/05 17:22","11/09 16:37","11/12 21:47"]},{"rule":"MAX_TRIES 6 -> 5 has one points/h read: +14% at +0.5 sd (11/12 19:00), with close rate 0.866 -> 0.8 and both arms negative. It is a single weak result, so do not rely on it without a new measurement. Read the value now first and judge on points/h.","evidence":["F71"],"status":"verified","trap":"The row says \'not taken\' and close rate fell, so it is easy to dismiss. It is also easy to overrate: +14% from a negative base (-0.001089 -> -0.000936) at +0.5 sd is thin. The older 11/05 16:16 read (not taken, close rate 0.526 -> 0.553) was on a different metric and gives no support.","when":["11/12 19:00"]}]}'
