[11/14 13:00:05] HARNESS: try 1: 18.5 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Treat every shop number row from 11/12 13:27 to 11/14 04:39 as no verdict. Each is MIXED with other changes in the same hours, so the raw margin beside it is not that number\'s effect. Choose the next number from the standing orders (orders 9, 12, 13 and 14), not from these rows.","evidence":["F185","F204","F209","F217","F227","F241"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Raw margin swings of +84% (F185), +136% (F204), -72% (F209) and +204% (F217) were read as the effect of the one number moved, but each row lists other changes in the same hours. Raw margin also reads the hour of day. A lesson built on these would be noise."},{"rule":"Judge a code change on shop points/h, the aim. When revenue or margin disagree with points/h, points/h decides. Every code verdict so far is MIXED with number changes, so it is weak evidence, not proof. Do not call a code change a win because revenue rose.","evidence":["F195","F214","F226","F238","F253"],"status":"verified","trap":"F195 showed margin -142% while points/h was -2%. F214 showed revenue +64% while points/h was -24%. F226 showed revenue +46% while points/h was -11%. F253 showed revenue +133% while points/h was -28%. Each was marked kept on its revenue or margin figure, while points/h, the aim, fell."},{"rule":"Do not re-add the cap on a dear line\'s depth by the market\'s settles over the last 6 h. Its code verdict was margin -69% and points/h -32%, and the guard asked for a revert (shop_revenue_h 7191536 -> 3340211). Any retry needs a points/h reading taken after it and must not stack with other dear_depth or max_list moves.","evidence":["F238"],"status":"unverified","trap":"The verdict is MIXED with number changes (dear_depth, sku_depth, max_list), so the -32% is not cleanly the cap\'s own effect. Reading it as proof the idea is dead is as wrong as ignoring it. The revert was left for the supervisor while lines had changed, so the evidence is muddy."},{"rule":"Make one clear move per number and read it. Do not move a number and undo it in the same hours, and do not repeat a change the supervisor reverted. Before proposing a value, check orders 12-14: window_depth stays at 2.0 or more, sku_depth stays at 3 or more, and the negative-value list.","evidence":["F204","F205","F223","F224","F230","F231","F235","F236","F240","F241","F248","F249"],"status":"unverified","trap":"These moves and undos filled the record: max_list 900000->600000 and back (F204, F205), window_depth 2.0->1.5 and back (F223, F224), dear_depth 5->4->5.0 (F230, F231, F240, F241), sku_depth 3->2 and back (F235, F236), and sku_depth 4->3.0 (F248, F249). Their windows overlap, so none can be judged, and the supervisor reverted several."},{"rule":"Treat the grade-A sellable-share logic in restock_r3 as unproven beyond its first step. The first step valued grade A over cost draws and sold only draws at or below the market median (F187, points/h +335%, MIXED). The follow-up that scaled dear-line depth by that share (F195) showed points/h -2%. Do not extend it further without a points/h reading of its own.","evidence":["F187","F195"],"status":"unverified","trap":"F187\'s measured +92% margin and +335% points/h were MIXED with number changes, and F195 kept the idea while margin fell -142%. Assuming the idea works because F187 looked good, then stacking more depth scaling on it, is what F195 did, and its points/h did not improve."}]}'
