[11/14 15:01:28] HARNESS: try 1: 21.8 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Judge every buyer number change on buyer points/h and its sd (board_pts_h, standing order 1). The kept/not taken label, close rate, saved/deal and seconds per order are parts, never the aim. Read the number\'s value now before moving it (order 5), and never step it a second time in the same direction before the last change has a closed 2 h verdict (order 9).","evidence":["F46","F54","F57","F61","F64","F68","F73","F76","F79","F80"],"status":"verified","trap":"The parts and points/h disagree. On 11/10 08:39 close rate fell 0.775 -> 0.664 while points/h was +1%. On 11/12 22:18 saved difference was +1.4 sd but points/h was -24%. On 11/13 11:32 saved difference was +2.1 sd but points/h was -5%. Reading the parts picks the wrong winner."},{"rule":"FOOD_MARGIN 1.15 -> 1.1 has been judged in both directions on points/h: +9% (+1.6 sd), +33% (+1.2 sd) and -24% (+1.4 sd). The result is mixed, so do not repeat the step (order 2). Read the value now first. Move it only on a new measurement taken at the value in force.","evidence":["F57","F64","F73"],"status":"verified","trap":"All three rows say \'not taken\'. Skipping the number on that label throws away two wins. Quoting only the wins hides the -24% of 11/12 22:18, whose saved difference was positive."},{"rule":"CAP: no neighbour of the value now has clearly beaten it (read it first). 0.75 -> 0.8 gave -5% points/h. 0.75 -> 0.7 gave +2% (+0.5 sd), +0% (+0.5 sd) and -11% (-0.0 sd). Treat this as noise leaning negative and spend no cycles on CAP without a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F53","F56","F67","F80"],"status":"verified","trap":"On 11/12 05:22 saved/deal (0.3993 -> 0.4044) and close rate (0.733 -> 0.787) rose while points/h was flat at +0%. On 11/14 04:38 saved/deal was flat (0.4157 -> 0.4156) and points/h was -11%. Neither part predicts points/h."},{"rule":"Raise limits (MAX_RAISE, RAISE_GOODS, RAISE_FOOD): no direction has a clear points/h win, so leave them alone unless a new measurement at the value in force says otherwise. MAX_RAISE downward gave +3% (0.4 -> 0.35) and +1% (0.35 -> 0.3), but also -20%, -2% and -17%. Upward steps gave -14% (RAISE_FOOD 1.2 -> 1.3), -3% and +15% (RAISE_GOODS 0.8 -> 0.9), and -5% (MAX_RAISE 0.35 -> 0.4).","evidence":["F46","F54","F62","F63","F65","F69","F74","F76","F79"],"status":"verified","trap":"The +15% of 11/13 02:10 came from a negative base with saved difference -0.1 sd, so it is not a win. Close rate or saved/deal rose in other windows (11/11 19:08, 11/13 11:32) while points/h fell."},{"rule":"FIRM_GAP: 0.07 has held against every tried move on points/h. 0.07 -> 0.05 gave -35%, -18% and +6% (at -0.4 sd). 0.07 -> 0.09 gave +2% (-0.2 sd) and -42% (-2.6 sd). Do not move it without a new measurement taken at the value in force.","evidence":["F50","F52","F61","F68","F78"],"status":"verified","trap":"The +6% (11/13 14:35) and +2% (11/09 18:04) are small and sit with negative saved differences, so they are not wins. Citing them would hide the -35% and -42% results."},{"rule":"Treat new ranking, scouting, penalty or plan-mode code that promises +1% to +10% with doubt. Most of it measured at or below zero on its own metric. Reverted: -4% (11/08 21:36), -5% (11/11 00:28), -9% (11/12 05:07). Kept but negative: -6% (11/08 16:36), -2% (11/10 09:28), -3% points/h (11/13 07:58), -1% (11/13 13:13). Ship such code only with a clear mechanism, and judge it on points/h, not on its own part metric.","evidence":["F39","F42","F55","F59","F66","F75","F77"],"status":"verified","trap":"The meta-agent expected gains nearly every time. \'Kept\' with a negative measurement is not a win, only a failure to cross the revert bar. F70 (+0%) and F51 (+1%) were also kept with next to no gain."},{"rule":"Code meant to shorten talks (early cancel, earlier walk-away, scout drops) must show that it shortens them. Seconds per order is a part, not the aim (order 1), so also check points/h before counting it a win. Only the scout drop of 11/12 21:47 shortened talks (seconds per order +22% against +10% expected). No points/h verdict is recorded for it.","evidence":["F16","F49","F72"],"status":"verified","trap":"11/05 17:22 (expected -8%, measured +1%) and 11/09 16:37 (expected -5%, measured +13%) were marked kept although seconds per order got no better or got worse. A label of kept says nothing about speed."},{"rule":"MAX_TRIES 6 -> 5 has one points/h read: +14% at +0.5 sd (11/12 19:00), with close rate 0.866 -> 0.8 and both arms negative. This is a single weak result, so do not rely on it without a new measurement. Read the value now first and judge on points/h.","evidence":["F71"],"status":"verified","trap":"The row says \'not taken\' and close rate fell, so it is easy to dismiss. It is also easy to overrate: +14% from a negative base (-0.001089 -> -0.000936) at +0.5 sd is within noise."}]}'
