[11/14 18:04:46] HARNESS: try 1: 22.7 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Judge every buyer number change on buyer points/h and its sd (board_pts_h, standing order 1). Close rate, saved/deal, saved difference and the kept/not taken label are parts, never the aim. Read the number\'s value now before moving it (order 5), and do not step it again in the same direction before the last change has a closed 2 h verdict (order 9).","evidence":["F54","F57","F64","F68","F73","F80","F65"],"status":"verified","trap":"The parts and points/h disagree. On 11/10 08:39 close rate fell 0.775 -> 0.664 while points/h was +1%. On 11/12 22:18 saved difference was +1.4 sd but points/h was -24%. On 11/14 04:38 saved/deal was flat (0.4157 -> 0.4156) while points/h was -11%. Picking a number on a part would have chosen wrongly in each case."},{"rule":"FOOD_MARGIN 1.15 -> 1.1 has been judged in both directions on points/h: +9% (+1.6 sd), +33% (+1.2 sd) and -24% (+1.4 sd). The result is mixed, so do not repeat the step (order 2). Read the value now first, and move it only on a new measurement taken at the value in force.","evidence":["F57","F64","F73"],"status":"verified","trap":"All three rows say \'not taken\'. Dismissing the number on that label throws away two wins. Quoting only the wins hides the -24% of 11/12 22:18, whose saved difference was +1.4 sd, so saved/deal looked good while points/h fell."},{"rule":"CAP: no neighbour of the value now has clearly beaten it (read it first). 0.75 -> 0.8 gave -5% points/h. 0.75 -> 0.7 gave +2% (+0.5 sd), +0% (+0.5 sd) and -11% (-0.0 sd). Treat it as noise leaning negative and spend no cycles on CAP without a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F53","F56","F67","F80"],"status":"verified","trap":"On 11/12 05:22 saved/deal (0.3993 -> 0.4044) and close rate (0.733 -> 0.787) rose while points/h was flat at +0%. Reading those parts as a win would have kept a change that earned nothing. The older CAP wins (F43) were on saved/deal alone