way, scout drops) must show that it shortens them. Seconds per order is a part, not the aim (order 1), so also check points/h before counting it a win. Only the scout drop of 11/12 21:47 shortened talks (+22% against +10% expected).","evidence":["F16","F49","F72"],"status":"verified","trap":"11/05 17:22 (expected -8%, measured +1%) and 11/09 16:37 (expected -5%, measured +13%) were marked kept although seconds per order got no better or got worse. A \'kept\' label does not mean the goal was reached."},{"rule":"MAX_TRIES 6 -> 5 has one points/h read: +14% at +0.5 sd (11/12 19:00), with close rate 0.866 -> 0.8 and both arms negative. This is a single weak result, so do not rely on it without a new measurement. Read the value now first and judge on points/h.","evidence":["F71"],"status":"verified","trap":"The row says \'not taken\' and close rate fell, so it is easy to dismiss. It is also easy to overrate: +14% from a negative base (-0.001089 -> -0.000936) at +0.5 sd is within noise, and the earlier 11/05 16:16 trial was judged on surplus, not points/h."}]}'
