de rows F232, F237, F242 and F250 show these were corrected."},{"rule":"Move food_first in one direction and let it close before the next step. On 11/14 it was stepped up and down within hours with no verdict to read.","evidence":["F233","F244","F245","F246","F266","F268","F269"],"status":"unverified","trap":"food_first went 0.0 -> 0.1, 0.1 -> 0.25, 0.25 -> 0.5, 0.5 -> 0.25, 0.25 -> 0.5, 0.5 -> 0.75 and 0.75 -> 0.5. Each row is MIXED, and the sequence left no readable effect."},{"rule":"Read the points/h verdict of F274 (the cap of depth 2 on 300k+ goods SKUs holding a unit unsold over 24 h) before extending it, and before adding any other stuck-stock depth cap. Earlier stale-stock changes raised revenue but not points/h.","evidence":["F214","F226","F238","F274"],"status":"unverified","trap":"F214 and F226 freed room and cash for hot SKUs and showed revenue +64% and +46%, but points/h fell -24% and -11%. F238\'s depth cap on dear lines was marked should-be-reverted by its guard (shop_revenue_h 7191536 -> 3340211.3004918206), with points/h -32%. All three are MIXED. A stuck-stock cap that cuts depth can be read as a win on revenue while points/h falls."},{"rule":"Do not ship code that puts food SKU lines ahead of the category entries without a points/h gain to show for it. F264 did that and was reverted.","evidence":["F264"],"status":"unverified","trap":"F264 expected deals +4% but measured -12%, with points/h -0%, and its revenue guard reverted it (shop_revenue_h 14530921 -> 8196697.338845459). It was MIXED with number changes, so this is weak evidence against it, not proof."},{"rule":"Treat the grade-A sellable-share depth scaling (F195) as unproven. It was kept, but nothing in the record shows a points/h gain.","evidence":["F195"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Expected margin was +5% and measured -142%, with points/h -2%, MIXED with stock_value, sku_depth and clear_hours changes. \'It was kept\' reads as \'it works\', and \'margin fell\' reads as \'it failed\'; neither follows from this row."}]}'
