nt at the value in force says otherwise. MAX_RAISE 0.35 -> 0.3 gave +1%, -20% and -17%. 0.35 -> 0.25 gave -2%. 0.35 -> 0.4 gave -5%. RAISE_FOOD 1.2 -> 1.3 gave -14% and -4%.","evidence":["F54","F62","F65","F69","F76","F79","F81","F63","F74"],"status":"verified","trap":"RAISE_GOODS 0.8 -> 0.9 gave -3%, then +15% on 11/13 02:10, but that +15% came from a negative base (-0.001027 -> -0.000873) at -0.1 sd, so it is not a win. MAX_RAISE 0.35 -> 0.4 had +2.1 sd on saved difference yet points/h fell. MAX_RAISE 0.35 -> 0.3 at +1% looked like a small win and then lost -20% and -17%."},{"rule":"FIRM_GAP: 0.07 has held against every tried move on points/h. 0.07 -> 0.05 gave -35%, -18% and +6% (at -0.4 sd). 0.07 -> 0.09 gave +2% (-0.2 sd) and -42% (-2.6 sd). Do not move it without a new measurement taken at the value in force.","evidence":["F50","F52","F61","F68","F78"],"status":"verified","trap":"The +6% (11/13 14:35) and +2% (11/09 18:04) are small and sit with negative saved differences, so they are not wins. Citing them alone would hide the -35% and -42% rows."},{"rule":"Treat new ranking, penalty, scouting or plan-mode code that promises a gain with doubt, and prefer a small, targeted rule over a re-ranking. Re-rankings and penalties measured at or below zero on their own metric: reverted -4% (F42), -5% (F59), -9% (F66); kept but negative -6% (F39), -2% (F55), -3% (F75), -1% (F77). Require the claimed gain to show on the metric that matters before counting it a win.","evidence":["F39","F42","F55","F59","F66","F75","F77"],"status":"verified","trap":"The meta-agent expected gains nearly every time (F75 expected +10%, measured -3%). \'Kept\' with a negative measurement is not a win, only a failure to cross the revert bar. F70 (+0% against expected +3%) was also kept with no gain."},{"rule":"Code meant to shorten talks (early cancel, earlier walk-away, scout drops) must show that it shortens them. Seconds per order is a part, not the aim (order 1), so also check points/h before counting it a win. Only the scout drop of 11/12 21:47 delivered (expected +10%, measured +22% on buyer_secs_order).","evidence":["F16","F49","F72"],"status":"verified","trap":"F16 (expected -8%, measured +1%) and F49 (expected -5%, measured +13%) were marked kept although seconds per order got no better or got worse. A faster talk can also cost closes, so a good seconds figure alone does not make the change good."},{"rule":"MAX_TRIES 6 -> 5 has one points/h read: +14% at +0.5 sd (11/12 19:00), with close rate 0.866 -> 0.8 and both arms negative. This is a single weak result, so do not rely on it without a new measurement. Read the value now first and judge on points/h.","evidence":["F71"],"status":"verified","trap":"The row says \'not taken\' and close rate fell, so it is easy to dismiss. It is also easy to overrate: +14% from a negative base (-0.001089 -> -0.000936) at +0.5 sd is not a win."}]}'
