[11/15 00:09:23] HARNESS: try 1: 24.0 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Judge every buyer change on buyer points/h and its sd (board_pts_h, standing order 1). Close rate, saved/deal, the saved difference and the kept/not taken label are parts, never the aim. Read the number\'s value now before moving it (order 5). Do not step a number again in the same direction before the last change has a closed 2 h verdict (order 9).","evidence":["F54","F57","F64","F65","F68","F73","F80","F82"],"status":"verified","trap":"The parts and points/h disagree. On 11/10 08:39 close rate fell 0.775 -> 0.664 while points/h was +1%. On 11/12 22:18 the saved difference was +1.4 sd and saved/deal rose 0.3836 -> 0.3967, but points/h was -24%. On 11/12 05:22 saved/deal and close rate rose while points/h was +0%. Reading the parts would have kept losing changes.","when":["11/10 08:39","11/11 22:09","11/12 01:27","11/12 05:22","11/12 11:03","11/12 22:18","11/14 04:38","11/14 18:55"]},{"rule":"FOOD_MARGIN 1.15 -> 1.1 has been judged in both directions on points/h (+9%, +33%, -24%), so do not repeat the step (order 2). A new try needs a fresh measurement taken at the value in force, with the value read first.","evidence":["F57","F64","F73"],"status":"verified","trap":"All three rows say \'not taken\'. Dismissing the number on that label throws away two wins (+9% at +1.6 sd, +33% at +1.2 sd). Quoting only the wins hides the -24% on 11/12 22:18, where saved difference was +1.4 sd but points/h fell.","when":["11/10 16:04","11/11 22:09","11/12 22:18"]},{"rule":"CAP: no neighbour of the value now has clearly beaten it. Read the value first and spend no cycle on CAP without a new measurement. 0.75 -> 0.8 gave -5% points/h. 0.75 -> 0.7 gave +2% (+0.5 sd), +0% (+0.5 sd) and -11% (-0.0 sd).","evidence":["F53","F56","F67","F80"],"status":"verified","trap":"On 11/12 05:22 saved/deal (0.3993 -> 0.4044) and close rate (0.733 -> 0.787) rose while points/h was flat at +0%. Reading those parts as a win would have kept a move that earned nothing. Two of the three 0.7 reads are within noise.","when":["11/10 03:43","11/10 12:26","11/12 05:22","11/14 04:38"]},{"rule":"Raise limits (MAX_RAISE, RAISE_GOODS, RAISE_FOOD): no direction has a clear points/h win, so leave them alone unless a new measurement at the value in force says otherwise. MAX_RAISE 0.35 -> 0.3 gave +1%, -20% and -17%. 0.35 -> 0.25 gave -2% and 0.35 -> 0.4 gave -5%. RAISE_FOOD 1.2 -> 1.3 gave -14% and -4%. The only win is MAX_RAISE 0.4 -> 0.35 at +3% (F46).","evidence":["F46","F54","F62","F65","F69","F76","F79","F81","F63","F74"],"status":"verified","trap":"RAISE_GOODS 0.8 -> 0.9 gave -3%, then +15% on 11/13 02:10. That +15% came from a negative base (-0.001027 -> -0.000873) at -0.1 sd, so it is not a win. The MAX_RAISE +1% on 11/10 08:39 came with close rate falling 0.775 -> 0.664. A positive percentage on a negative base is a smaller loss, not a gain.","when":["11/09 10:35","11/10 08:39","11/11 14:49","11/12 01:27","11/12 14:51","11/13 11:32","11/13 23:57","11/14 12:10","11/11 19:08","11/13 02:10"]},{"rule":"FIRM_GAP: 0.07 has held against every tried move on points/h. 0.07 -> 0.05 gave -35%, -18%, +6% (-0.4 sd) and +6% (+0.5 sd). 0.07 -> 0.09 gave +2% (-0.2 sd) and -42% (-2.6 sd). Do not move it without a new measurement taken at the value in force.","evidence":["F50","F52","F61","F68","F78","F82"],"status":"verified","trap":"The two +6% reads (11/13 14:35 and 11/14 18:55) and the +2% (11/09 18:04) are small, come from negative bases or negative saved differences, and sit against -35% and -18% on the same step. Citing them alone would hide the losses and invite another repeat of a step already judged both ways.","when":["11/09 18:04","11/09 23:48","11/11 11:18","11/12 11:03","11/13 14:35","11/14 18:55"]},{"rule":"Treat new ranking, penalty, scouting or plan-mode code that promises a gain with doubt, and prefer a small, targeted rule over a re-ranking. Re-rankings and penalties measured at or below zero on their own metric: F39 -6%, F42 -4% (reverted), F55 -2%, F59 -5% (reverted), F66 -9% (reverted), F75 -3% points/h, F77 -1%, F37 -2%.","evidence":["F37","F39","F42","F55","F59","F66","F75","F77"],"status":"verified","trap":"The meta-agent expected gains nearly every time (11/13 07:58 expected +10%, measured -3%). \'Kept\' with a negative measurement is not a win, only a failure to cross the revert line. The ranking rules that stayed at or above zero (F51 +1%, F58 +3%, F70 +0%) were small, targeted changes.","when":["11/08 11:55","11/08 16:36","11/08 21:36","11/10 09:28","11/11 00:28","11/12 05:07","11/13 07:58","11/13 13:13"]},{"rule":"Code meant to shorten talks (early cancel, earlier walk-away, scout drops) must show that it shortens them. Seconds per order is a part, not the aim (order 1), so also check points/h before counting it a win. Only the scout drop of 11/12 21:47 measured a real gain in seconds per order (+22%, expected +10%).","evidence":["F16","F49","F72"],"status":"verified","trap":"11/05 17:22 (expected -8%, measured +1%) and 11/09 16:37 (expected -5%, measured +13%) were marked kept although seconds per order got no better or got worse. A faster talk can still lose points if it walks away from deals.","when":["11/05 17:22","11/09 16:37","11/12 21:47"]},{"rule":"MAX_TRIES 6 -> 5 has one points/h read: +14% at +0.5 sd (11/12 19:00), with close rate 0.866 -> 0.8 and both arms negative. This is a single weak result, so do not rely on it without a new measurement. Read the value now first and judge on points/h.","evidence":["F71"],"status":"verified","trap":"The row says \'not taken\' and close rate fell, so it is easy to dismiss. It is also easy to overrate: +14% from a negative base (-0.001089 -> -0.000936) at +0.5 sd is a smaller loss, not a proven gain.","when":["11/12 19:00"]}]}'
