as a win would have been a mistake. MAX_RAISE 0.35 -> 0.3 looked good on saved/deal (+1.3 sd on 11/13 23:57) while points/h fell 17%."},{"rule":"FIRM_GAP: the value now (0.07 was the one tested from) has no winning neighbour. Cutting 0.07 -> 0.05 gave -35%, -18%, +6% and +6% points/h. Raising 0.07 -> 0.09 gave +2% and -42%. Do not move it without a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F50","F52","F61","F68","F78","F82"],"status":"verified","trap":"The two +6% reads (11/13 14:35 at -0.4 sd, 11/14 18:55 at +0.5 sd) are small and sit on negative bases, while the 11/9 23:48 read was -35% at -1.1 sd. Calling the cut \'recent and positive\' would ignore the -18% on 11/11 11:18."},{"rule":"FOOD_MARGIN 1.15 -> 1.1 has conflicting points/h reads: +9% (+1.6 sd), +33% (+1.2 sd) and -24% (+1.4 sd, negative base). It is unsettled, so read the value now and re-test only as a new measurement. 1.15 -> 1.2 was not taken.","evidence":["F45","F57","F64","F73"],"status":"verified","trap":"Saved/deal rose in all three 1.1 trials (0.3722 -> 0.3889, 0.3877 -> 0.3996, 0.3836 -> 0.3967) and the saved difference was positive each time, yet points/h went +9%, +33%, -24%. The sd belongs to the saved difference, not to points/h, so it does not settle the question."},{"rule":"Treat new ranking, penalty, scouting or plan-mode code that promises a gain with doubt, and prefer a small, targeted rule over a re-ranking. Re-rankings and penalties measured at or below zero on their own metric: 11/08 16:36 -6%, 11/08 21:36 -4% (reverted), 11/10 09:28 -2%, 11/11 00:28 -5% (reverted), 11/12 05:07 -9% (reverted), 11/13 07:58 -3%, 11/13 13:13 -1%. Small targeted rules fared better (11/10 17:41 +3%).","evidence":["F37","F39","F42","F55","F58","F59","F66","F75","F77"],"status":"verified","trap":"The meta-agent expected gains nearly every time (11/13 07:58 expected +10%, measured -3%). \'Kept\' with a negative measurement is not a win, only a failure to cross the revert line, so do not cite a kept row of -2% or -3% as support."},{"rule":"Code meant to shorten talks (early cancel, earlier walk-away, scout drops) must show that it shortens them. Seconds per order is a part, not the aim (order 1), so also check points/h before counting it a win. Only the scout drop of 11/12 21:47 showed a real gain on seconds per order (expected +10%, measured +22%).","evidence":["F16","F49","F72"],"status":"verified","trap":"11/05 17:22 (expected -8%, measured +1%) and 11/09 16:37 (expected -5%, measured +13%) were marked kept although seconds per order got no better or got worse. A kept label says nothing about whether the stated gain happened."},{"rule":"MAX_TRIES 6 -> 5 has one points/h read: +14% at +0.5 sd (11/12 19:00), with close rate 0.866 -> 0.8 and both arms negative. This is a single weak result, so do not rely on it without a new measurement. Read the value now first and judge on points/h.","evidence":["F71"],"status":"verified","trap":"The row says \'not taken\' and close rate fell, so it is easy to dismiss. It is also easy to overrate: +14% from a negative base (-0.001089 -> -0.000936) at +0.5 sd is not a clear win."}]}'
