[11/15 03:42:28] HARNESS: try 1: 11.5 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Judge a forum change on the forum rating (0-1, counted as itself) and on which of our posts draw dislike stances, broken down by post kind, as order 6 requires. Do not judge it on forum_votes_post read as the hour before against the hour after.","evidence":["F3","F4","F6"],"status":"unverified","trap":"F3 was reverted on -20% and F4 was kept despite -9%. Both are raw before/after readings that depend on the hour of day, so they are weak. F6 read forum_votes_post None -> None, which measures nothing."},{"rule":"Treat the narrowed note() in F3 (top 4 shops with 2+ settles, last 2 refs per shop) and the our_deals cap of about 1 post in 3 in F4 as open questions, neither proven good nor bad. Retry or tune either only if it is judged on the forum rating and on dislike stances per post kind.","evidence":["F3","F4"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Reading the F3 revert as proof the change was bad, or keeping the F4 cap because its tests passed (14/14). Passing tests show the code runs, not that the rating improved."},{"rule":"The post-kind mix (built by code from the ledger, weighted by votes) has no verdict on the rating. Do not assume vote weighting is optimal. Count dislike stances per kind and shift the mix away from the kinds that draw them.","evidence":["F1","F2"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Assuming the mix is fine because it is vote-driven. F1 and F2 have no verdict, so nothing shows the mix avoids dislike stances."},{"rule":"Do not credit or blame posting cadence for any forum result. Code fixes the cadence at the market\'s 310 s limit (order 6), so do not retune FORMAT_EVERY or the forum interval. Put the effort into post quality and kind.","evidence":["F5","F6"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Citing F6 (FORMAT_EVERY 360 -> 310) as proof the faster cadence helped. F6 was MIXED with open_gap and dear_depth changes in the same hours, so it is no verdict. F5 has no verdict either."}]}'
