[11/15 06:27:55] HARNESS: try 1: 22.7 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [\n{"rule": "Judge every buyer change on buyer points/h and its sd (board_pts_h, standing order 1). Close rate, saved/deal, the saved difference and the kept/not taken label are parts, never the aim. Read the number\'s value now before moving it (order 5). A positive saved difference with flat or negative points/h is not a win.", "evidence": ["F54", "F57", "F64", "F68", "F73", "F76", "F79", "F80", "F83"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The parts and points/h keep disagreeing. 11/10 08:39: close rate fell 0.775 -> 0.664 while points/h was +1%. 11/12 22:18: the saved difference was +1.4 sd and saved/deal rose 0.3836 -> 0.3967, but points/h was -24%. 11/15 02:53: the saved difference was +2.6 sd and saved/deal 0.3942 -> 0.4259, but points/h was +0% (-0.000761 -> -0.000758)."},\n{"rule": "CAP: no neighbour of the value now has clearly beaten it. Read the value first and spend no cycle on CAP without a new measurement. 0.75 -> 0.8 gave -5% points/h. 0.75 -> 0.7 gave +2% (+0.5 sd), +0% (+0.5 sd) and -11% (-0.0 sd).", "evidence": ["F53", "F56", "F67", "F80"], "status": "verified", "trap": "On 11/12 05:22 saved/deal (0.3993 -> 0.4044) and close rate (0.733 -> 0.787) rose while points/h was flat at +0%. Reading those parts as a win would have kept a change that added nothing. The +2% on 11/10 12:26 was followed by -11% on 11/14 04:38."},\n{"rule": "Raise limits (MAX_RAISE, RAISE_GOODS, RAISE_FOOD) have no clear points/h winner in any direction, so leave them alone unless a new measurement at the value in force says otherwise. MAX_RAISE 0.35 -> 0.3 gave +1%, -20% and -17%. 0.35 -> 0.25 gave -2%. 0.35 -> 0.4 gave -5% and +0%. 0.4 -> 0.35 gave +3% (F46). RAISE_FOOD 1.2 -> 1.3 gave -14% and -4%. RAISE_GOODS 0.8 -> 0.9 gave -3% and +15%.", "evidence": ["F46", "F54", "F62", "F69", "F76", "F79", "F83", "F65", "F81", "F63", "F74"], "status": "verified", "trap": "0.35 -> 0.4 on 11/15 02:53 had +2.6 sd on the saved difference and saved/deal 0.3942 -> 0.4259, which looks like a win, but points/h was +0%; the earlier 11/13 11:32 trial with +2.1 sd gave -5%. RAISE_GOODS +15% on 11/13 02:10 came from a negative base (-0.001027 -> -0.000873) at -0.1 sd, against -3% earlier."},\n{"rule": "FIRM_GAP: 0.07 has no winning neighbour. Cutting 0.07 -> 0.05 gave -35%, -18%, +6% and +6% points/h. Raising 0.07 -> 0.09 gave +2% and -42%. Do not move it without a new measurement at the value in force.", "evidence": ["F50", "F52", "F61", "F68", "F78", "F82"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The two +6% reads (11/13 14:35 at -0.4 sd, 11/14 18:55 at +0.5 sd) are small and sit on negative bases, while the 11/9 23:48 read was -35% at -1.1 sd and 11/11 11:18 was -18%. Calling the cut a winner from the last two would ignore the larger losses."},\n{"rule": "FOOD_MARGIN 1.15 -> 1.1 has conflicting points/h reads: +9% (+1.6 sd), +33% (+1.2 sd) and -24% (+1.4 sd, negative base). It is unsettled, so read the value now and re-test only as a new measurement. 1.15 -> 1.2 was not taken (saved/deal 0.3619 -> 0.3536).", "evidence": ["F45", "F57", "F64", "F73"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Saved/deal rose in all three 1.1 trials (0.3722 -> 0.3889, 0.3877 -> 0.3996, 0.3836 -> 0.3967) and the saved difference was positive each time, yet points/h went -24% in the last. Two of three being positive does not settle it."},\n{"rule": "Treat new ranking, penalty, scouting or plan-mode code that promises a gain with doubt, and prefer a small, targeted rule over a re-ranking. Re-rankings and penalties measured at or below zero on their own metric: F39 -6%, F42 -4% (reverted), F55 -2%, F59 -5% (reverted), F66 -9% (reverted), F75 -3% points/h, F77 -1%. The one clear gain was the small food-penalty change F58 (+3% close rate).", "evidence": ["F37", "F39", "F42", "F55", "F58", "F59", "F66", "F75", "F77"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The meta-agent expected gains nearly every time (11/13 07:58 expected +10%, measured -3%). \'Kept\' with a negative measurement is not a win, only a failure to clearly lose, so it should not be cited as support for similar code."},\n{"rule": "Code meant to shorten talks (early cancel, earlier walk-away, scout drops) must show that it shortens them. Seconds per order is a part, not the aim (order 1), so also check points/h before counting it a win. Only the scout drop of 11/12 21:47 clearly shortened talks (expected +10%, measured +22%).", "evidence": ["F16", "F49", "F72"], "status": "verified", "trap": "11/05 17:22 (expected -8%, measured +1%) and 11/09 16:37 (expected -5%, measured +13%) were marked kept although seconds per order got no better or got worse. A kept label is not proof of the intended effect."},\n{"rule": "MAX_TRIES 6 -> 5 has one points/h read: +14% at +0.5 sd (11/12 19:00), with close rate 0.866 -> 0.8 and both arms negative. This is a single weak result, so do not rely on it without a new measurement. Read the value now first and judge on points/h.", "evidence": ["F71"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The row says \'not taken\' and close rate fell, so it is easy to dismiss. It is also easy to overrate: +14% from a negative base (-0.001089 -> -0.000936) at +0.5 sd is within noise."}\n]}'
