[11/15 09:28:09] HARNESS: try 1: 29.0 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [{"rule": "Judge every buyer change on buyer points/h and its sd (board_pts_h, standing order 1). Close rate, saved/deal, the saved difference and the kept/not taken label are parts, never the aim. Read the number\'s value now before moving it (order 5), and do not step it a second time in the same direction before the last change has a closed verdict (order 9).", "evidence": ["F54", "F57", "F64", "F68", "F73", "F76", "F79", "F80", "F83"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The parts and points/h keep disagreeing. 11/10 08:39: close rate fell 0.775 -> 0.664 while points/h was +1%. 11/15 02:53: the saved difference was +2.6 sd and saved/deal 0.3942 -> 0.4259, but points/h was +0%. 11/13 23:57: +1.3 sd and saved/deal up, but points/h -17%. Acting on the parts would have kept losers.", "status": "verified"}, {"rule": "CAP: no neighbour of the value now has clearly beaten it. Read the value first and spend no cycle on CAP without a new measurement at the value in force. 0.75 -> 0.8 gave -5% points/h. 0.75 -> 0.7 gave +2% (+0.5 sd), +0% (+0.5 sd) and -11% (-0.0 sd).", "evidence": ["F53", "F56", "F67", "F80"], "status": "verified", "trap": "On 11/12 05:22 saved/deal (0.3993 -> 0.4044) and close rate (0.733 -> 0.787) rose while points/h was flat at +0%. Reading those parts as a win, or the lone +2% as a trend, would have moved CAP to a value that then read -11%."}, {"rule": "MAX_RAISE 0.35 stays unless a new measurement at the value in force says otherwise. 0.35 -> 0.3 gave +1%, -20% and -17% points/h. 0.35 -> 0.4 gave -5% and +0%. 0.35 -> 0.25 gave -2%. Only the 0.4 -> 0.35 step (+3%) ever read positive.", "evidence": ["F46", "F54", "F62", "F69", "F76", "F79", "F83"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Both 0.4 trials showed a strongly positive saved difference (+2.1 sd, +2.6 sd) and higher saved/deal, yet points/h was -5% and +0%. The 0.3 trial on 11/13 23:57 also had +1.3 sd and closed -17%.}", "status": "verified"}, {"rule": "RAISE_FOOD 1.2 -> 1.3 lost on points/h both times (-14%, -4%), so do not retry it. RAISE_GOODS 0.8 -> 0.9 is split (-3%, then +15% at -0.1 sd on a negative base), and MAX_TRIES 6 -> 5 has one +14% read at +0.5 sd: all three are weak, so change them only on a new measurement at the value in force.", "evidence": ["F65", "F81", "F63", "F74", "F71"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The +15% and +14% reads come from negative bases (-0.001027 -> -0.000873, -0.001089 -> -0.000936) with sd near zero or +0.5, and each row says \'not taken\' with close rate falling. Dismissing them is wrong, but so is treating either as a settled gain."}, {"rule": "FIRM_GAP: 0.07 has no winning neighbour. Cutting 0.07 -> 0.05 gave -35%, -18%, +6% and +6% points/h. Raising 0.07 -> 0.09 gave +2% and -42%. Do not move it without a new measurement at the value in force.", "evidence": ["F50", "F52", "F61", "F68", "F78", "F82"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The two +6% reads (11/13 14:35 at -0.4 sd, 11/14 18:55 at +0.5 sd) are small and sit on negative bases, while 11/9 23:48 was -35% at -1.1 sd and 11/12 11:03 was -42% at -2.6 sd. The big losses outweigh the small gains."}, {"rule": "FOOD_MARGIN 1.15 -> 1.1 has conflicting points/h reads: +9% (+1.6 sd), +33% (+1.2 sd) and -24% (+1.4 sd, negative base). It is unsettled, so read the value now and re-test only as a new measurement under order 9.", "evidence": ["F57", "F64", "F73"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Saved/deal rose in all three 1.1 trials (0.3722 -> 0.3889, 0.3877 -> 0.3996, 0.3836 -> 0.3967) and the saved difference was positive each time, yet points/h went the other way on 11/12 22:18. A positive saved difference does not predict points/h."}, {"rule": "Treat new ranking, penalty, scouting or plan-mode code that promises a gain with doubt, and prefer a small targeted rule over a re-ranking. Re-rankings and penalties measured at or below zero on their own metric: F39 -6%, F42 -4% (reverted), F55 -2%, F59 -5% (reverted), F66 -9% (reverted), F75 -3% (buyer_pts_h), F77 -1%. The small food-penalty change (0.3 to 0.05) measured +3% as expected.", "evidence": ["F37", "F39", "F42", "F55", "F58", "F59", "F66", "F75", "F77"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The meta-agent expected gains nearly every time (11/13 07:58 expected +10%, measured -3%). \'Kept\' with a negative measurement is not a win, only a failure to clear the revert bar. Most of these were judged on saved/deal or close rate, parts of the aim, not points/h."}, {"rule": "Code meant to shorten talks (early cancel, earlier walk-away, scout drops) must show that it shortens them. Seconds per order is a part, not the aim (order 1), so also check points/h before counting it a win. Only the scout drop of 11/12 21:47 delivered (expected +10%, measured +22%).", "evidence": ["F16", "F49", "F72"], "status": "verified", "trap": "11/05 17:22 (expected -8%, measured +1%) and 11/09 16:37 (expected -5%, measured +13%) were marked kept although seconds per order got no better or got worse. A kept label did not mean the talks got shorter."}]}'
