[11/15 12:43:38] HARNESS: try 1: 23.5 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Judge every buyer change on buyer points/h and its sd (board_pts_h, standing order 1). Close rate, saved/deal, the saved difference and the kept/not taken label are parts, never the aim. Read the number\'s value now before moving it (order 5) and do not repeat a step in the same direction before a closed verdict (order 9).","evidence":["F54","F57","F64","F68","F73","F76","F79","F83"],"status":"verified","trap":"The parts and points/h keep disagreeing. F54: close rate fell 0.775 -> 0.664 while points/h was +1%. F83: the saved difference was +2.6 sd and saved/deal rose 0.3942 -> 0.4259, yet points/h was +0%. F64: points/h +33% was still \'not taken\'. Reading the parts or the label as the result picks the wrong number."},{"rule":"CAP: no neighbour of the value now has clearly beaten it. Read the value first and spend no cycle on CAP without a new measurement at the value in force. 0.75 -> 0.8 gave -5% points/h. 0.75 -> 0.7 gave +2%, +0% and -11%.","evidence":["F53","F56","F67","F80"],"status":"verified","trap":"F67: saved/deal (0.3993 -> 0.4044) and close rate (0.733 -> 0.787) rose while points/h was +0%. F56\'s +2% came with +0.5 sd. Treating either as a win, or the lone +2%, would have moved CAP on noise, and F80 then read -11%."},{"rule":"MAX_RAISE 0.35 stays unless a new measurement at the value in force says otherwise. 0.35 -> 0.3 gave +1%, -20% and -17% points/h. 0.35 -> 0.4 gave -5% and +0%. 0.35 -> 0.25 gave -2%. Only the 0.4 -> 0.35 step (+3%) ever read positive.","evidence":["F46","F54","F62","F69","F76","F79","F83"],"status":"verified","trap":"Both 0.4 trials showed a strongly positive saved difference (+2.1 sd in F76, +2.6 sd in F83) and higher saved/deal, yet points/h was -5% and +0%. F79 (0.3) had +1.3 sd and higher saved/deal but -17% points/h. A strong saved difference is not a points/h gain."},{"rule":"RAISE_FOOD 1.2 -> 1.3 lost on points/h both times (-14%, -4%), so do not retry it. RAISE_GOODS 0.8 -> 0.9 is split (-3%, then +15%), and MAX_TRIES 6 -> 5 has one +14% read. These last two are weak, so change them only with a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F65","F81","F63","F74","F71"],"status":"verified","trap":"The +15% and +14% reads come from negative bases (-0.001027 -> -0.000873, -0.001089 -> -0.000936) with a saved difference of -0.1 sd and +0.5 sd, and each row still says \'not taken\'. A percentage on a negative base looks like a gain without being one."},{"rule":"FIRM_GAP: 0.07 has no winning neighbour. Cutting 0.07 -> 0.05 gave -35%, -18%, +6% and +6% points/h. Raising 0.07 -> 0.09 gave +2% and -42%. Do not move it without a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F50","F52","F61","F68","F78","F82"],"status":"verified","trap":"The two +6% reads (F78 at -0.4 sd, F82 at +0.5 sd) are small and sit on negative bases, while F52 was -35% at -1.1 sd and F68 was -42% at -2.6 sd. Reading the recent small gains as a trend would repeat the large losses."},{"rule":"FOOD_MARGIN 1.15 -> 1.1 has conflicting points/h reads: +9% (+1.6 sd), +33% (+1.2 sd) and -24% (+1.4 sd, negative base). It is unsettled, so read the value now and re-test only as a new measurement under order 9.","evidence":["F57","F64","F73"],"status":"verified","trap":"Saved/deal rose in all three 1.1 trials (0.3722 -> 0.3889, 0.3877 -> 0.3996, 0.3836 -> 0.3967) and the saved difference was positive each time, yet points/h went -24% in F73. Two of three reads were positive but the rows were still \'not taken\', so neither the label nor the parts settle it."},{"rule":"Treat new ranking, penalty, scouting or plan-mode code that promises a gain with doubt, and prefer a small targeted rule over a re-ranking. Measured on their own metric, re-rankings and penalties came out at or below zero: F39 -6%, F42 -4% (reverted), F59 -5% (reverted), F66 -9% (reverted), F75 -3% points/h, F55 -2%, F37 -2%, F77 -1%. The small targeted rule F58 (food penalty 0.3 -> 0.05) read +3%.","evidence":["F37","F39","F42","F55","F58","F59","F66","F75","F77"],"status":"verified","trap":"The meta-agent expected a gain nearly every time (F75 expected +10%, measured -3%; F59 expected +2%, measured -5%). \'Kept\' with a negative measurement is not a win, only a failure to clear a revert bar, so do not stack such code on its expectation."},{"rule":"Code meant to shorten talks (early cancel, earlier walk-away, scout drops) must show that it shortens them. Seconds per order is a part, not the aim (order 1), so also check points/h before counting it a win. Only the scout drop F72 (expected +10%, measured +22%) delivered.","evidence":["F16","F49","F72"],"status":"verified","trap":"F16 (expected -8%, measured +1%) and F49 (expected -5%, measured +13%) were marked kept although seconds per order got no better or got worse. A faster talk can also cost closes, so the kept label does not show a board gain."}]}'
