[11/15 15:45:19] HARNESS: try 1: 25.1 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Judge every buyer change on buyer points/h and its sd (board_pts_h, standing order 1). Close rate, saved/deal, the saved difference and the kept/not taken label are parts, never the aim. Read the number\'s value now before moving it (order 5), and do not step a number a second time in the same direction before its last change has a closed 2 h verdict (order 9).","evidence":["F54","F57","F64","F68","F73","F76","F79","F83","F85"],"status":"verified","trap":"The parts and points/h keep disagreeing. 11/10 08:39: close rate fell 0.775 -> 0.664 while points/h was +1%. 11/15 02:53: the saved difference was +2.6 sd and saved/deal rose 0.3942 -> 0.4259, yet points/h was +0%. 11/15 11:23: close rate fell 0.791 -> 0.731 while points/h was +28%. Reading any part as the verdict gets the call wrong in both directions."},{"rule":"CAP: lowering 0.75 -> 0.7 is the only direction with a lean toward a gain; raising it has not paid. 0.75 -> 0.7 read +2%, +0%, -11% and then +28% points/h (saved difference +0.5, +0.5, -0.0 and +1.0 sd). 0.75 -> 0.8 read -5%. Read the value now before testing it again, and measure at the value in force.","evidence":["F53","F56","F67","F80","F85"],"status":"verified","trap":"Every 0.7 trial was labelled \'not taken\', which hides that three of four reads were at or above zero on points/h and the newest was +28%. Equally, the -11% read (11/14 04:38) shows one good window is not proof: close rate fell 0.837 -> 0.769 there. Do not call it settled either way, and do not move it again before the last change has a closed verdict (order 9).","when":["11/10 03:43","11/10 12:26","11/12 05:22","11/14 04:38","11/15 11:23"]},{"rule":"MAX_RAISE 0.35 has no winning neighbour. 0.35 -> 0.3 read +1%, -20%, -17%; 0.35 -> 0.25 read -2%; 0.35 -> 0.4 read -5% and +0%. Do not move it without a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F54","F62","F69","F76","F79","F83"],"status":"verified","trap":"0.35 -> 0.4 on 11/15 02:53 showed +2.6 sd on the saved difference and saved/deal 0.3942 -> 0.4259, which looks like a win, but points/h was +0% (-0.000761 -> -0.000758). 11/13 11:32 had +2.1 sd with -5%. A big saved sd has not turned into points."},{"rule":"RAISE_FOOD 1.2 -> 1.3 lost on points/h both times (-14%, -4%), so do not retry it. RAISE_GOODS 0.8 -> 0.9 is split (-3%, then +15%), and MAX_TRIES 6 -> 5 has one +14% read. These last two are weak, so change them only with a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F65","F81","F63","F74","F71"],"status":"verified","trap":"The +15% and +14% reads come from negative bases (-0.001027 -> -0.000873, -0.001089 -> -0.000936) with a saved difference of -0.1 sd and +0.5 sd, so a percentage on a negative base looks like a gain without being one. Each row also had a different close rate result."},{"rule":"FIRM_GAP: 0.07 has no winning neighbour. Cutting 0.07 -> 0.05 gave -35%, -18%, +6% and +6% points/h. Raising 0.07 -> 0.09 gave +2% and -42%. Do not move it without a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F50","F52","F61","F68","F78","F82"],"status":"verified","trap":"The two +6% reads (11/13 14:35 at -0.4 sd, 11/14 18:55 at +0.5 sd) are small and sit on negative bases, while 11/09 23:48 was -35% at -1.1 sd and 11/12 11:03 was -42% at -2.6 sd. Reading the recent small gains as a trend repeats the losses.","when":["11/09 18:04","11/09 23:48","11/11 11:18","11/12 11:03","11/13 14:35","11/14 18:55"]},{"rule":"FOOD_MARGIN 1.15 -> 1.1 has conflicting points/h reads: +9% (+1.6 sd), +33% (+1.2 sd) and -24% (+1.4 sd, negative base). It is unsettled, so read the value now and re-test only as a new measurement under order 9.","evidence":["F57","F64","F73"],"status":"verified","trap":"Saved/deal rose in all three 1.1 trials (0.3722 -> 0.3889, 0.3877 -> 0.3996, 0.3836 -> 0.3967) and the saved difference was positive each time, yet points/h went the other way once. Trusting saved/deal alone would have called all three wins.","when":["11/10 16:04","11/11 22:09","11/12 22:18"]},{"rule":"Treat new ranking, penalty, scouting or plan-mode code that promises a gain with doubt, and prefer a small targeted rule over a re-ranking. On their own metric, re-rankings and penalties came out at or below zero: F39 -6%, F42 -4%, F55 -2%, F59 -5%, F66 -9%, F75 -3%, F77 -1%, F37 -2%. The small targeted food-penalty cut gained +3% (F58). Code meant to shorten talks must show it does: only the scout drop (F72, +22% on seconds per order) did, while early cancel and earlier walk-away did not (F16 +1%, F49 +13%, where lower is better). Seconds per order is a part, not the aim, so also check points/h.","evidence":["F37","F39","F42","F55","F58","F59","F66","F75","F77","F16","F49","F72","F84"],"status":"verified","trap":"The meta-agent expected a gain nearly every time (F75 expected +10%, measured -3%; F59 expected +2%, measured -5%; F84 expected +3%, measured +1%). \'Kept\' with a negative or near-zero measurement is not a win. Most code verdicts are on buyer_saved_deal or close rate, not points/h, so even a positive one may not move the board."}]}'
