.07 -> 0.05 gave -35%, -18%, +6% and +6% points/h; 0.07 -> 0.09 gave +2% and -42%. Do not move it without a new measurement at the value in force.", "evidence": ["F50", "F52", "F61", "F68", "F78", "F82"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The two +6% reads (-0.4 sd and +0.5 sd) are small and sit on negative bases. The -35% (-1.1 sd) and -42% (-2.6 sd) reads are larger and sit on the same two numbers, so a cut to 0.05 looks cheaper than it is."},\n{"rule": "FOOD_MARGIN 1.15 -> 1.1 is unsettled on points/h: +9% (+1.6 sd), +33% (+1.2 sd), -24% (+1.4 sd, negative base). Re-test only as a new measurement at the value in force (order 9), not as a proven win.", "evidence": ["F57", "F64", "F73"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Saved/deal rose in all three 1.1 trials (0.3722 -> 0.3889, 0.3877 -> 0.3996, 0.3836 -> 0.3967) and the saved difference was positive each time, yet points/h went the other way on 11/12 22:18. All three were labelled \'not taken\'."},\n{"rule": "CAP is unsettled. 0.75 -> 0.7 read +2%, +0%, -11% and +28% on points/h; 0.75 -> 0.8 read -5%. Treat 0.8 as a loser and do not move CAP again without a new measurement at the value in force. The latest read (+28%, +1.0 sd) is the only large one and has not been repeated.", "evidence": ["F53", "F56", "F67", "F80", "F85"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Every 0.7 trial was labelled \'not taken\' although three of four did not lose on points/h, and the single large read (+28%) rests on 129 vs 104 orders. Neither the label nor the lone +28% settles it."},\n{"rule": "Be doubtful of new ranking, penalty, scouting-order or plan-mode code. On their own metric these came out at or below zero: F37 -2%, F39 -6%, F42 -4%, F55 -2%, F59 -5%, F66 -9%, F77 -1%, F75 -3% on points/h. Prefer a small targeted rule over a re-ranking.", "evidence": ["F37", "F39", "F42", "F55", "F59", "F66", "F75", "F77"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The meta-agent expected a gain nearly every time (11/13 07:58 expected +10%, measured -3%; 11/11 00:28