[11/15 18:48:51] HARNESS: try 1: 15.1 s, exit 0, answer '{"proposal": {"best_value": 2.8, "weather": 1.0, "claims": 0.8, "haggle": 0.8}, "why": "Mean votes rank fun 6.42, pay_tips 6.40, weather 6.37, best_value 6.35 above claims 6.11 and haggle 6.19, so weight moves toward the higher-voted kinds, with weather lifted because it has few posts (160). Dislikes per post are close across kinds (claims 0.57, haggle 0.61, best_value 0.61 vs pay_tips 0.65), so this hour\'s data doesn\'t show the extra claims/haggle dislikes noted for 11/9; the spread is small, so these are small steps and fun stays at its 3.0 cap.", "ideas": ["tool: a per-post log of dislike stances by voter account, kept across the full round, since the API shows only the last ~100 posts (~12 min); without it we cannot see which posts cost the 0.918 rating (leader 0.94), and no weight change can show that.", "A new kind \'shelf-life watch\' (유통기한 임박 감시) built only from ledger refs: remaining hours per settled SKU and the warranty floor the market applies. Buyers\' own complaints in the feed cite short remaining hours, so the kind would be useful, and every fact would link to a ledger number."], "lessons_used": ["none"]}'
[11/15 18:48:51] HARNESS: try 1: 15.7 s, exit 0, answer '{"proposal": {}, "ab": null, "recruit": null, "playbook": "none", "why": "Food opens at the floor in 35% of talks, so floor_frac_food matters there, but it was last moved to 0.48 and has no closed 2 h verdict yet, so order 9 blocks a second cut; our food list (0.617) already sits above the market median (0.593), so raising ask_frac_food would push further from market. Goods open on the market line in 99% of talks, market_ask is held at 1.0 by order 15, and min_margin is already at its 0.02 floor, so no goods number reaches a sale.", "ideas": ["tool: a dear-stock sell-through view (units bought vs sold per category, with age), so dear_depth and buy-side changes can be judged on sell rate (about 45/h) instead of on raw stock growth, which rose from 58M to 92M at cost since 06:00 and is the main drag on Book.", "A clearance route for dear stock that is not a general price cut: sell only the aged units that have passed clear_age_hours and are at risk of never selling, at cost, so Book is not lowered on the rest of the stock."], "lessons_used": ["L2", "L4"]}'
[11/15 18:48:52] HARNESS: try 1: 16.1 s, exit 0, answer '{"proposal": {"MAX_RAISE": 0.4}, "recruit": {"MAX_RAISE": 0.4, "FIRM_GAP": 0.05, "OPEN": "p25"}, "why": "Lost talks end a median 0.31 below the ask, and 355 of about 1,000 talks ended with us walking, so a higher raise cap should convert some of those into deals. All four buyer-team styles on the rivals table have negative reward (about -0.105), so a different opening (p25 instead of low) is worth one trial. Expect some drop in saved per deal as the cost of closing more talks.", "ideas": ["tool: a per-talk log of our last offer, the shop\'s ask, and the outcome, so walk-aways can be split by SKU and grade and the cause of the 0.31 gap can be measured instead of guessed.", "Stock, not haggling, ends 167 talks (\'other_shop_none_in_stock\'), so restocking the goods and food that sell out is a shop-side change that no buyer number can make."], "lessons_used": ["none"]}'
[11/15 18:48:52] HARNESS: try 1: 16.7 s, exit 0, answer '{"proposal": {"stock_value": 120000000}, "why": "Dear stock is accumulating: our 150k+ goods were bought faster than they sold (63 vs 47 per hour over 15:00-16:00, and 30 vs 13 over 16:00-16:31), taking stock at cost from 58M to 92M, and storage now costs about 0.9M a day. Trimming the cap to 120M (a one-cycle step of 10M, the largest allowed) slows that build-up while cash stays at 140M and well above the 500k line, and I am not touching dear_depth, max_list or dear_first because their nearby values have closed negative verdicts (dear_depth 4, dear_first 2.5, max_list 600k and 1.15M+).", "ideas": ["tool: a per-SKU sell-through and age report for dear goods (bought, sold and aged by hour), so the dear buy rate can be matched to the sell rate (about 45 a hour) instead of inferred from hourly totals.", "A clearance rule that sells goods older than the stuck threshold down to cost (never under) would free the capital in the unsold dear pile; no stock number does this, because the floor on grade-A units priced above market sits at cost/(1-WARRANTY_Q), so lowering market_ask only cuts the price of units that already sell."], "lessons_used": ["none"]}'
