[11/15 21:34:35] HARNESS: try 1: 20.3 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Never credit a number with the raw margin swing listed beside it. Every shop number row from F119 to F198 (11/12 05:38 to 11/15 18:32) is MIXED or has no verdict, so none of them is evidence for or against a value. Judge a move on board_pts_h, the rivals table and the edges table. Treat a raw swing only as a hint about where to look.","evidence":["F152","F165","F170","F176","F185"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Raw swings of +83%, +163%, +290%, +86% and +212% each sat beside other changes in the same hours. Reading any one as the effect of the number moved would have credited the wrong change. The same applies to negative swings: F167 at -72% and F147 at -41% also had co-changes."},{"rule":"Before proposing any number, check order 14\'s list of values whose own verdict closed negative. Returning to one needs a new measurement taken after that verdict, cited with its window. Stepping away from such a value and back does not make it a free \'different number\'.","evidence":["F133","F157","F171","F177","F160","F163"],"status":"unverified","trap":"fresh_premium went to 0.2 (F133, 11/12 12:09) and back to 0.15 three more times (F157, F171, F177). market_ask went to 0.95 (F160, F163). Order 14 lists all of these values as closed negative, and the supervisor reverted several of these moves. The rows themselves are MIXED, so the closed verdicts come from order 14, not from these facts."},{"rule":"Send one net value per number per cycle. Do not send a change and its undo in the same minute: the pair carries no information and invites a supervisor revert. If a step cannot be held for a full 2 h window, do not send it.","evidence":["F130","F131","F139","F140","F149","F150","F154","F155","F171","F172","F177","F178","F182","F183"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Same-minute change/undo pairs appeared on floor_frac (11/12 11:36, 14:51), floor_frac_food (11/12 20:23, 22:18/22:19), fresh_premium (11/13 20:54/20:55, 11/14 10:13) and clear_hours (11/14 11:18). Every one is MIXED, so the pairs taught nothing and only added noise and reverts."},{"rule":"Do not step a number a second time in the same direction before its last step has a closed 2 h verdict (order 9). Measure the next step\'s evidence at the value now in force, not at an older one.","evidence":["F152","F159","F162","F189","F191"],"status":"unverified","trap":"clear_hours went 14 -> 12 -> 10 -> 8 (F152, F159, F162) and market_ask went 1.0 -> 1.05 -> 1.08 (F189, F191), each step taken before the previous one had a closed verdict. The supervisor had to revert earlier chains of this kind, such as the food floor and ask_frac on 11/12."},{"rule":"Leave market_ask at 1.0 for the rest of the round (order 15). Only a closed A/B can move it, not a play-mode step. Its closed positive verdict is the +63% at 1.0, cited by orders 11 and 15.","evidence":["F186","F187","F189","F191","F192","F193","F197","F198"],"status":"unverified","trap":"From 11/14 03:48 to 11/15 18:32 market_ask flipped between 1.0, 1.03, 1.05 and 1.08 more than eight times, often back within minutes (F197 then F198 within 18 minutes). Every row is MIXED, so no value got a clean verdict and the moves only spent cycles."},{"rule":"Keep window_depth at 2.0 or more and sku_depth at 3 or more for the rest of the round (orders 12 and 13). Cutting either left the best-selling food short.","evidence":["F163","F165"],"status":"unverified","trap":"window_depth 2.0->1.5 and sku_depth 3->2 each cut our food share (3.6% and 3.3% against 4.5-5.8% and 5.1% before), and each was reverted. The share numbers come from the orders, not from these MIXED rows. A cut is tempting because it frees capital quickly, but the capital is lost back in food sales."}]}'
