[11/15 21:52:04] HARNESS: try 1: 30.8 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [\n{"rule": "Judge every buyer change on buyer points/h and its sd (board_pts_h, standing order 1). Close rate, saved/deal, the saved difference and the kept/not-taken label are parts, not the aim. Before moving a number, read its value now (order 5), and do not step a number again in the same direction before its last change has a closed verdict (order 9).", "evidence": ["F54", "F57", "F64", "F68", "F73", "F76", "F79", "F83", "F85", "F86"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The parts and points/h disagree. On 11/10 08:39 close rate fell 0.775 -> 0.664 while points/h was +1%. On 11/15 02:53 the saved difference was +2.6 sd and saved/deal 0.3942 -> 0.4259, yet points/h was +0%. Recent points/h bases are negative (e.g. -0.000901 -> -0.000647 is shown as +28%), so a positive percent can mean only a smaller loss.", "when": ["11/10 08:39", "11/10 16:04", "11/11 22:09", "11/12 11:03", "11/12 22:18", "11/13 11:32", "11/13 23:57", "11/15 02:53", "11/15 11:23", "11/15 18:32"]},\n{"rule": "MAX_RAISE 0.35 has no winning neighbour. 0.35 -> 0.3 read +1%, -20%, -17% and -19%; 0.35 -> 0.25 read -2%; 0.35 -> 0.4 read -5% and +0%. Leave it at 0.35 unless a new measurement at the value in force says otherwise.", "evidence": ["F54", "F62", "F69", "F76", "F79", "F83", "F86"], "status": "verified", "trap": "0.35 -> 0.3 (F79 +1.3 sd, F86 +1.3 sd), 0.35 -> 0.4 (F76 +2.1 sd, F83 +2.6 sd) all showed a better saved difference and saved/deal, yet points/h lost or tied. Acting on saved/deal alone would have cost points four times.", "when": ["11/10 08:39", "11/11 14:49", "11/12 14:51", "11/13 11:32", "11/13 23:57", "11/15 02:53", "11/15 18:32"]},\n{"rule": "RAISE_FOOD 1.2 -> 1.3 lost on points/h both times (-14%, -4%): do not retry it. RAISE_GOODS 0.8 -> 0.9 is split (-3%, then +15%) and MAX_TRIES 6 -> 5 has one +14% read. Both of those are weak, so change them only with a new measurement at the value in force.", "evidence": ["F65", "F81", "F63", "F74", "F71"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The +15% and +14% reads sit on negative bases (-0.001027 -> -0.000873, -0.001089 -> -0.000936) with saved differences of -0.1 sd and +0.5 sd. Reading them as clear wins would repeat a step the other read contradicts.", "when": ["11/12 01:27", "11/14 12:10", "11/11 19:08", "11/13 02:10", "11/12 19:00"]},\n{"rule": "FIRM_GAP 0.07 has no winning neighbour. 0.07 -> 0.05 gave -35%, -18%, +6% and +6% points/h; 0.07 -> 0.09 gave +2% and -42%. Do not move it without a new measurement at the value in force.", "evidence": ["F50", "F52", "F61", "F68", "F78", "F82"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The two +6% reads (-0.4 sd and +0.5 sd) are small and sit on negative bases. The -35% (-1.1 sd) and -42% (-2.6 sd) reads are larger and sit on the same two numbers, so a single small positive read is not a reason to move.", "when": ["11/09 18:04", "11/09 23:48", "11/11 11:18", "11/12 11:03", "11/13 14:35", "11/14 18:55"]},\n{"rule": "FOOD_MARGIN 1.15 -> 1.1 is unsettled on points/h: +9% (+1.6 sd), +33% (+1.2 sd), -24% (+1.4 sd, negative base). Re-test only as a new measurement at the value in force (order 9), not as a proven win.", "evidence": ["F57", "F64", "F73"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Saved/deal rose in all three 1.1 trials (0.3722 -> 0.3889, 0.3877 -> 0.3996, 0.3836 -> 0.3967) and the saved difference was positive each time, yet points/h went the other way in the last one. Do not call it a win from saved/deal.", "when": ["11/10 16:04", "11/11 22:09", "11/12 22:18"]},\n{"rule": "CAP 0.75 is unsettled. 0.75 -> 0.7 read +2%, +0%, -11% and +28% points/h; 0.75 -> 0.8 read -5%. Do not step CAP again without a new measurement at the value in force.", "evidence": ["F53", "F56", "F67", "F80", "F85"], "status": "verified", "trap": "0.7 showed better saved/deal in F56, F67 and F85 (e.g. 0.4032 -> 0.4146) and a lower close rate in two of them, so it looks like a clean trade. The +28% sits on a negative base (-0.000901 -> -0.000647) and F80 read -11%, so one good read is not a rule.", "when": ["11/10 03:43", "11/10 12:26", "11/12 05:22", "11/14 04:38", "11/15 11:23"]},\n{"rule": "Do not add more break-rate, grade or over-cap penalties to the buyer\'s ranking (candidates, scout_wave). Every such A/B lost on the board\'s buyer term: sort by surplus/list -2%, break-rate weighting -6%, grade penalty -4%, soft-break ban -2%, scouted ranking -5%, over-cap exponent 8 -9% close rate. Judge any new ranking change on its measured points/h, not on the expected gain.", "evidence": ["F37", "F39", "F42", "F55", "F59", "F66"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Each of these was written with an expected +1% to +4% and measured negative. F37, F39, F42, F55 and F59 were judged on saved/deal and F66 on close rate, not points/h, so they are weaker as board evidence.", "when": ["11/08 11:55", "11/08 16:36", "11/08 21:36", "11/10 09:28", "11/11 00:28", "11/12 05:22"]},\n{"rule": "A code change labelled kept can still read zero or negative on the aim. Plan mode on half the orders was kept at -3% buyer_pts_h (expected +10%), per-grade deal_limit at -1% saved/deal, and the 6 h-warranty receipt rule at +0%. Treat these as unproven, not as wins to build on.", "evidence": ["F70", "F75", "F77"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Building a follow-up on the kept label would stack changes on a measured -3% or +0%. Read the measured number and sd, not the label.", "when": ["11/12 16:48", "11/13 07:58", "11/13 13:13"]}\n]}'
