nces of -0.1 sd and +0.5 sd. Reading them as clean wins would ignore that RAISE_GOODS was -3% on its other trial."},\n{"rule": "FIRM_GAP 0.07 has no winning neighbour. 0.07 -> 0.05 gave -35%, -18%, +6% and +6% points/h; 0.07 -> 0.09 gave +2% and -42%. Do not move it without a new measurement at the value in force.", "evidence": ["F50", "F52", "F61", "F68", "F78", "F82"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The two +6% reads (-0.4 sd and +0.5 sd) are small and sit on negative bases. The -35% (-1.1 sd) and -42% (-2.6 sd) reads are large. Citing the +6% reads as proof for 0.05 hides the two large losses."},\n{"rule": "FOOD_MARGIN 1.15 -> 1.1 is unsettled on points/h: +9% (+1.6 sd), +33% (+1.2 sd), -24% (+1.4 sd, negative base). Re-test only as a new measurement at the value in force (order 9), not as a proven win.", "evidence": ["F57", "F64", "F73"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Saved/deal rose in all three 1.1 trials (0.3722 -> 0.3889, 0.3877 -> 0.3996, 0.3836 -> 0.3967) and the saved difference was positive each time, yet points/h went -24% in the third. Two of three wins is not a settled direction."},\n{"rule": "CAP 0.75 is unsettled. 0.75 -> 0.7 read +2%, +0%, -11% and +28% points/h; 0.75 -> 0.8 read -5%. Do not step CAP again without a new measurement at the value in force.", "evidence": ["F53", "F56", "F67", "F80", "F85"], "status": "verified", "trap": "0.7 showed better saved/deal in 11/10 12:26, 11/12 05:22 and 11/15 11:23 (e.g. 0.4032 -> 0.4146) and a lower close rate in two of them, so it looks like a clean trade. The +28% sits on a negative base (-0.000901 -> -0.000647) and the -11% read (11/14 04:38) is the opposite, so one trial does not decide it."},\n{"rule": "Do not add more break-rate, grade or over-cap penalties to the buyer\'s ranking (candidates, scout_wave). Every such A/B lost: sort by surplus/list -2%, break-rate weighting -6%, grade penalty -4%, soft-break ban -2%, scout expected-saved-rate ranking -5%, over-cap exponent 8 -9% close rate.", "eviden