[11/16 04:08:44] HARNESS: try 1: 24.2 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Judge every buyer change on buyer points/h and its sd (standing order 1). Close rate, saved/deal, the saved difference and the kept/not-taken label are parts, not the aim. Read the number\'s value now before moving it (order 5).","evidence":["F54","F57","F64","F68","F73","F76","F79","F83","F85","F86","F87"],"status":"verified","trap":"The parts and points/h often disagree. F54: close rate fell 0.775 -> 0.664 while points/h was +1%. F83: the saved difference was +2.6 sd and saved/deal 0.3942 -> 0.4259, yet points/h was +0%. F86: +1.3 sd and saved/deal 0.4004 -> 0.4148, yet points/h was -19%. Reading a better saved/deal or sd as a win would have shipped losers."},{"rule":"Leave MAX_RAISE at 0.35. 0.4 -> 0.35 was kept at +3% points/h (F46). Since then 0.35 -> 0.3 read +1%, -20%, -17% and -19%, 0.35 -> 0.25 read -2%, and 0.35 -> 0.4 read -5% and +0%. Move it only with a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F46","F54","F62","F69","F76","F79","F83","F86"],"status":"verified","trap":"Both 0.3 (F79 +1.3 sd, F86 +1.3 sd) and 0.4 (F76 +2.1 sd, F83 +2.6 sd) showed a better saved difference and saved/deal while points/h was flat or negative. Citing those sd values as proof would repeat a losing trial."},{"rule":"Do not retry RAISE_FOOD 1.2 -> 1.3: it lost on points/h both times (-14%, -4%). RAISE_GOODS 0.8 -> 0.9 is split (-3%, then +15%) and MAX_TRIES 6 -> 5 has one +14% read. Treat those two as weak and change them only with a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F65","F81","F63","F74","F71"],"status":"verified","trap":"The +15% and +14% reads sit on negative bases (-0.001027 -> -0.000873, -0.001089 -> -0.000936) with saved differences of -0.1 sd and +0.5 sd. Reading them as clear wins would be a mistake: both bases are negative and the sd values are small."},{"rule":"FIRM_GAP 0.07 has no winning neighbour. 0.07 -> 0.05 gave -35%, -18%, +6% and +6% points/h; 0.07 -> 0.09 gave +2% and -42%. Do not move it without a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F50","F52","F61","F68","F78","F82"],"status":"verified","trap":"The two +6% reads (-0.4 sd and +0.5 sd) are small and sit on negative bases, while the -35% (-1.1 sd) and -42% (-2.6 sd) reads are large. Citing the +6% reads as proof that 0.05 is safe ignores the large losses."},{"rule":"FOOD_MARGIN 1.15 -> 1.1 is unsettled on points/h: +9% (+1.6 sd), +33% (+1.2 sd), -24% (+1.4 sd, negative base) and -29% (-1.9 sd). Two reads are positive and two negative, so it is no proven win. Re-test only as a new measurement at the value in force (order 9).","evidence":["F57","F64","F73","F87"],"status":"verified","trap":"Saved/deal rose in the first three 1.1 trials (e.g. 0.3722 -> 0.3889) and the saved difference was positive each time, yet points/h went -24% in the third. In F87 saved/deal fell 0.8696 -> 0.8356 and points/h was -29%. Neither the saved/deal rise nor the sd predicts points/h."},{"rule":"CAP 0.75 is unsettled. 0.75 -> 0.7 read +2%, +0%, -11% and +28% points/h; 0.75 -> 0.8 read -5%. Do not step CAP again without a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F53","F56","F67","F80","F85"],"status":"verified","trap":"0.7 showed better saved/deal in F56, F67 and F85 (e.g. 0.4032 -> 0.4146) and a lower close rate in two of them, so it looks like a clean trade. Points/h was still -11% in F80, and the +28% in F85 sits on a negative base (-0.000901 -> -0.000647)."},{"rule":"Do not add more break-rate, grade or over-cap penalties to the buyer\'s ranking (candidates, scout_wave). Every such A/B lost: sort by surplus/list -2%, break-rate weighting -6%, grade penalty -4%, soft-break ban -2%, scout expected-saved-rate ranking -5%, scout over-cap exponent 8 -9% close rate.","evidence":["F37","F39","F42","F55","F59","F66"],"status":"verified","trap":"Each was written with an expected +1% to +4% and measured negative. They were judged on saved/deal or close rate, not points/h, so they are code verdicts on parts. A new ranking tweak built on the same idea would likely lose again."},{"rule":"A code change labelled kept can still read zero or negative on the aim, and a verdict on a part is not a points result. Plan mode on half the orders was kept at -3% buyer_pts_h (expected +10%), per-grade deal_limit at -1% saved/deal, the 6 h-warranty receipt rule at +0%, and the first-repeat walk-away rule at +13% secs/order against an expected -5%. The 11/15 22:11 rule replacing the plan-mode Haiku call (F88) was judged only on secs/order (+37%), with no points/h verdict.","evidence":["F49","F70","F75","F77","F88","F72","F84"],"status":"verified","trap":"Stacking a follow-up on a kept label builds on a measured -3% or +0%. F88\'s +37% is a speed gain, not a points gain, and it replaces the plan-mode step that F75 kept at -3% points/h. Do not call it a win until points/h is read."}]}'
