[11/16 04:09:19] HARNESS: try 1: 12.2 s, exit 0, answer '{"proposal": {}, "why": "Rank 22 and falling revenue per hour (33.6M to 13.2M) say the shop needs a change, but every number I could move now either has a negative verdict (max_list 900k, sku_cap 18, dear_depth 4 or 7), repeats a same-direction step before its last change closed (min_shelf_hours, surge_max), or has no measured effect (stock_value, since stock at cost is 90M against a 110M cap). The next useful change is a code fix to buyer order speed, not a number move.", "ideas": ["tool: a per-batch sales ledger that tags each unit with the number values in force when it was bought, so each change can be judged on its own units instead of on mixed hours (lessons L1 and L4 show every recent verdict was confounded).", "The buyer completes about 66 deals an hour against 135-154 for the leading buyers, and the limit is our own order time (about 42 s per order, of which the plan call is about 10 s), not the number of orders arriving. A code change to the plan step is the lever that no number can reach, and it is already under test as code A/B f6970f79d0d1."], "lessons_used": ["L1", "L2", "L3", "L4"]}'
