[11/16 10:11:43] HARNESS: try 1: 26.2 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Judge every buyer change on buyer points/h and its sd (standing order 1). Close rate, saved/deal, the saved difference and the kept/not-taken label are only parts. Read the value now in force before moving a number (order 5), and never step a number a second time in the same direction before its last change has a closed verdict (order 9).","evidence":["F54","F73","F83","F85","F87"],"status":"verified","trap":"The parts and the aim often disagree. 11/10 08:39: close rate fell 0.775 -> 0.664 while points/h was +1%. 11/12 22:18: saved difference +1.4 sd and saved/deal 0.3836 -> 0.3967, yet points/h was -24%. 11/15 02:53: saved difference +2.6 sd, points/h +0%. 11/15 11:23: points/h +28% with a lower close rate. Picking whichever part agrees with the idea gives the wrong call.","when":["11/10 08:39","11/12 22:18","11/15 02:53","11/15 11:23","11/15 21:53"]},{"rule":"Leave MAX_RAISE at 0.35. 0.4 -> 0.35 was kept at +3% points/h (F46). Since then 0.35 -> 0.3 read +1%, -20%, -17% and -19%, 0.35 -> 0.25 read -2%, and 0.35 -> 0.4 read -5% and +0%. Move it only with a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F46","F54","F62","F69","F76","F79","F83","F86"],"status":"verified","trap":"Both 0.3 (11/13 23:57 +1.3 sd, 11/15 18:32 +1.3 sd) and 0.4 (11/13 11:32 +2.1 sd, 11/15 02:53 +2.6 sd) showed a better saved difference and higher saved/deal while points/h was flat or negative. Citing the saved side supports either direction, and the aim has not backed it.","when":["11/09 10:35","11/10 08:39","11/11 14:49","11/12 14:51","11/13 11:32","11/13 23:57","11/15 02:53","11/15 18:32"]},{"rule":"Do not retry RAISE_FOOD 1.2 -> 1.3: it lost on points/h both times (-14%, -4%). RAISE_GOODS 0.8 -> 0.9 is split (-3%, then +15%) and MAX_TRIES 6 -> 5 has a single +14% read on points/h. Treat those two as weak and change them only after a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F65","F81","F63","F74","F71"],"status":"verified","trap":"The +15% (-0.001027 -> -0.000873, -0.1 sd) and +14% (-0.001089 -> -0.000936, +0.5 sd) reads sit on negative bases with small saved differences, and RAISE_GOODS has a -3% read at -1.4 sd. Reading them as wins is a mistake; one read each is no proof.","when":["11/12 01:27","11/14 12:10","11/11 19:08","11/13 02:10","11/12 19:00"]},{"rule":"FIRM_GAP 0.07 has no winning neighbour. 0.07 -> 0.05 gave -35%, -18%, +6% and +6% points/h; 0.07 -> 0.09 gave +2% and -42%. Do not move it without a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F50","F52","F61","F68","F78","F82"],"status":"verified","trap":"The two +6% reads (-0.4 sd and +0.5 sd) are small and sit on negative bases, while -35% (-1.1 sd) and -42% (-2.6 sd) are large. Citing only the +6% reads to justify 0.05 ignores the large losses.","when":["11/09 18:04","11/09 23:48","11/11 11:18","11/12 11:03","11/13 14:35","11/14 18:55"]},{"rule":"FOOD_MARGIN 1.15 -> 1.1 is unsettled on points/h: +9% (+1.6 sd), +33% (+1.2 sd), -24% (+1.4 sd, negative base) and -29% (-1.9 sd). Two reads are positive and two negative, so it is no proven win. Re-test it only as a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F57","F64","F73","F87"],"status":"verified","trap":"Saved/deal rose in the first three 1.1 trials (e.g. 0.3722 -> 0.3889) and the saved difference was positive each time, yet points/h fell 24% in the third. The latest read is the worst (-29%), so leaning on the early good reads would be wrong.","when":["11/10 16:04","11/11 22:09","11/12 22:18","11/15 21:53"]},{"rule":"CAP 0.75 is unsettled. 0.75 -> 0.7 read +2%, +0%, -11% and +28% points/h; 0.75 -> 0.8 read -5%. Do not step CAP again without a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F53","F56","F67","F80","F85"],"status":"verified","trap":"0.7 showed better saved/deal in 11/10 12:26, 11/12 05:22 and 11/15 11:23 (e.g. 0.4032 -> 0.4146) and a lower close rate in 11/10 12:26 and 11/15 11:23, so it looks like a clean trade. Points/h was still -11% on 11/14 04:38, and the one +28% read came from a negative base, so one good read is not a trend.","when":["11/10 03:43","11/10 12:26","11/12 05:22","11/14 04:38","11/15 11:23"]},{"rule":"Do not add more break-rate, grade or over-cap penalties or re-rankings to the buyer\'s candidate or scout ordering. Every such A/B lost: sort by surplus/list -2%, break-rate weighting -6%, grade penalty -4%, soft-break ban -2%, scout expected-rate ranking -5%, scout exponent 8 -9% close rate. The one gain came from lowering a penalty (short-shelf-life food 0.3 -> 0.05, +3% close rate).","evidence":["F37","F39","F42","F55","F59","F66","F58"],"status":"verified","trap":"Each was written with an expected +1% to +4% and measured negative, and F37, F39 and F55 were still labelled kept. They were judged on saved/deal or close rate, not points/h, so even F58\'s +3% is only a part, not a points result.","when":["11/08 11:55","11/08 16:36","11/08 21:36","11/10 09:28","11/11 00:28","11/12 05:07","11/10 17:41"]},{"rule":"A code change labelled kept can still read zero or negative on the aim, and a speed or part verdict is not a points result. Plan mode on half the orders was kept at -3% buyer_pts_h (expected +10%), per-grade deal_limit at -1% saved/deal, the 6 h warranty receipt rule at +0% saved/deal and the second scout wave at +1% close rate. The +37% (F88) and +22% (F72) are buyer_secs_order speed gains. Do not stack follow-ups on them as if points had risen.","evidence":["F70","F75","F77","F88","F72","F84"],"status":"verified","trap":"Stacking a follow-up on a kept label builds on a measured -3% or +0%. The +37% of 11/15 22:11 and the +22% of 11/12 21:47 measure seconds per order, not points, so they say nothing about the board aim.","when":["11/12 16:48","11/13 07:58","11/13 13:13","11/15 22:11","11/12 21:47","11/15 10:20"]}]}'
