[11/16 16:26:16] HARNESS: try 1: 21.4 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Judge every buyer change on buyer points/h and its sd (standing order 1). Close rate, saved/deal, the saved difference and the kept/not-taken label are only parts of the aim. Read the value now in force before moving a number (order 5), and do not step the same number again in the same direction before its last change has a closed verdict (order 9).","evidence":["F54","F73","F83","F85","F87"],"status":"verified","trap":"The parts and the aim disagree. On 11/10 08:39 close rate fell 0.775 -> 0.664 while points/h was +1%. On 11/12 22:18 the saved difference was +1.4 sd, yet points/h was -24%. On 11/15 02:53 the saved difference was +2.6 sd, yet points/h was +0%. On 11/15 11:23 and 11/15 21:53 the parts and the aim also pointed different ways. A change picked on the parts can lose on the aim."},{"rule":"Leave MAX_RAISE at 0.35. 0.4 -> 0.35 was kept at +3% points/h (11/09 10:35). Since then 0.35 -> 0.3 read +1%, -20%, -17% and -19%, and 0.35 -> 0.25 read -2%. 0.35 -> 0.4 read -5% and +0%. Move it only with a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F46","F54","F62","F69","F76","F79","F83","F86"],"status":"verified","trap":"Both 0.3 (+1.3 sd on 11/13 23:57 and 11/15 18:32) and 0.4 (+2.1 sd on 11/13 11:32, +2.6 sd on 11/15 02:53) showed a better saved difference and higher saved/deal, but points/h was -17%, -19%, -5% and +0%. Reading the saved difference alone would have moved a number that was already best."},{"rule":"Do not retry RAISE_FOOD 1.2 -> 1.3: it lost on points/h both times (-14%, -4%). RAISE_GOODS 0.8 -> 0.9 is split (-3%, then +15%). MAX_TRIES 6 -> 5 is split too (+14%, then -9%). Treat the last two as unsettled and change them only after a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F65","F81","F63","F74","F71","F92"],"status":"verified","trap":"The +15% (-0.001027 -> -0.000873, -0.1 sd) and +14% (-0.001089 -> -0.000936, +0.5 sd) reads sit on negative bases with small saved differences. MAX_TRIES then read -9% on a positive base. A single positive read on a negative base is not a win."},{"rule":"FIRM_GAP 0.07 has no clear winning neighbour. 0.07 -> 0.05 gave -35%, -18%, +6%, +6% and +2% points/h. 0.07 -> 0.09 gave +2% and -42%. Do not move it without a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F50","F52","F61","F68","F78","F82","F90"],"status":"verified","trap":"The three latest 0.05 reads (+6%, +6%, +2%, all within about 0.5 sd) are small and two sit on negative bases. The -35% (-1.1 sd) and -42% (-2.6 sd) reads are larger. Calling 0.05 a win from the recent small positives ignores the big losses."},{"rule":"FOOD_MARGIN 1.15 -> 1.1 is unsettled on points/h: +9% (+1.6 sd), +33% (+1.2 sd), -24% (+1.4 sd, negative base) and -29% (-1.9 sd). Two reads are positive and two negative, so it is no proven win. Re-test it only as a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F57","F64","F73","F87"],"status":"verified","trap":"Saved/deal rose in the first three 1.1 trials (e.g. 0.3722 -> 0.3889) and the saved difference was positive each time, yet points/h fell 24% in the third. The last read went the other way entirely (-29%, -1.9 sd). A streak of good saved/deal does not make it a win."},{"rule":"CAP 0.75 is unsettled. 0.75 -> 0.7 read +2%, +0%, -11% and +28% points/h. 0.75 -> 0.8 read -5%. Do not step CAP again without a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F53","F56","F67","F80","F85"],"status":"verified","trap":"0.7 showed better saved/deal on 11/10 12:26, 11/12 05:22 and 11/15 11:23 (e.g. 0.4032 -> 0.4146) and a lower close rate on 11/10 12:26 and 11/15 11:23, so it looks like a clean trade. Points/h still read -11% on 11/14 04:38 and only +28% once, so it is no stable gain."},{"rule":"Do not add more break-rate, grade or over-cap penalties or re-rankings to the buyer\'s candidate or scout ordering. Every such A/B lost: sort by surplus/list -2%, break-rate weighting -6%, grade penalty -4%, soft-break ban -2%, scout expected-saved-rate ranking -5%, over-cap exponent 8 -9% close rate. The one exception is F58, which removed a penalty (food shelf-life 0.3 -> 0.05) and held +3% close rate.","evidence":["F37","F39","F42","F55","F59","F66","F58"],"status":"verified","trap":"Each was written with an expected +1% to +4% and measured negative. F37, F39 and F55 were still labelled kept. They were judged on saved/deal and close rate, not on points/h. A kept label on such a change does not make it a win."},{"rule":"A code change labelled kept can still read zero or negative on the aim, and a speed or part verdict is not a points result. Plan mode on half the orders was kept at -3% buyer_pts_h (expected +10%). Per-grade deal_limit was kept at -1% saved/deal. The grade-warranty accept rule was kept at +0%. The shorter RETRY_UNTIL was kept at -1% buyer_paid_h (expected +8%). Do not stack follow-ups on these, and credit seconds-per-order gains only as speed.","evidence":["F70","F75","F77","F88","F72","F84","F91"],"status":"verified","trap":"Stacking a follow-up on a kept label builds on a measured -3%, -1% or +0%. The +37% of 11/15 22:11 and the +22% of 11/12 21:47 measure seconds per order, not points. The 11/15 10:20 change was +1% on close rate. None of these shows a gain on board points/h."}]}'
