[11/16 19:13:30] HARNESS: try 1: 23.2 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [{"rule": "Send one net value per number per cycle. If you change your mind inside the cycle, send only the final value, never a change and its undo minutes apart.", "evidence": ["F149", "F150", "F154", "F155", "F171", "F172", "F177", "F178", "F182", "F183", "F212", "F213", "F216", "F217", "F219", "F220", "F221"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Change-and-undo pairs went out within a minute or two: floor_frac_food 0.56 -> 0.52 (11/12 20:23), fresh_premium 0.18 -> 0.15 then 0.15 -> 0.18 (11/14 10:13), step 0.6 -> 0.5 then 0.5 -> 0.6 (11/16 10:13), c_first flipped 1 -> 0.0 -> 1 -> 0.0 (11/16 15:16-15:33). Each pair costs two windows and leaves no clean verdict. Rests only on UNVERIFIED/MIXED rows, so it is weak."}, {"rule": "Do not step a number again in the same direction until its last step has a closed 2 h verdict (order 9). Take the evidence for the next step from the value now in force, not from an older value.", "evidence": ["F152", "F159", "F162", "F176", "F190", "F203", "F188", "F196", "F200", "F209", "F199", "F201"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Chains went out with no verdict between steps: clear_hours 14 -> 12 -> 10 -> 8, ask_frac_food 0.78 -> 0.75 -> 0.7, floor_frac_food 0.5 -> 0.48 -> 0.46 -> 0.45, grade_frac_b 0.94 -> 0.92 -> 0.88. Every step was MIXED, so nobody could tell which step helped or hurt. Rests only on MIXED/UNVERIFIED rows, so it is weak."}, {"rule": "Before proposing a number, check order 14\'s list of values whose own verdict closed negative. A return to one needs a new measurement taken after it. \'The opposite direction is free\' does not cover such a return.", "evidence": ["F146", "F149", "F154", "F157", "F171", "F177"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Returns went out as \'a different or opposite number\': clear_hours back to 14 (11/12 17:54), floor_frac_food up to 0.57 (11/12 22:18), fresh_premium down to 0.15 (11/12 23:41, 11/13 20:54, 11/14 10:13). The supervisor reverted several. The rows are MIXED, so they show only that the returns were tried, not how they ended."}, {"rule": "Do not cite a row marked [supervisor] as proof that a change worked or failed. It is the supervisor\'s own revert or move and carries no verdict. Judge a number only on its own closed window.", "evidence": ["F151", "F156", "F169", "F211"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "These rows (floor_frac_food 0.56 -> 0.52 and 0.57 -> 0.52, ask_frac_food 0.83 -> 0.8, floor_frac 0.62 -> 0.61) are marked \'no verdict\'. Reading a revert as proof the earlier step was bad, or the revert good, is circular."}, {"rule": "Do not read the raw margin beside a row as the effect of the number moved. Judge a step only on its closed board_pts_h verdict, never on the raw margin.", "evidence": ["F165", "F170", "F185", "F209", "F210", "F212", "F213", "F214"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Raw margin swung +163% (11/13 09:37), +290% (11/13 18:09) and +212% (11/14 16:09) on single-number steps. On 11/16 09:39-10:29 every row sat between -44% and -53% whichever number moved, so it followed the hour, not the number."}, {"rule": "Treat every row F143-F222 as \'no verdict\': all are MIXED, so none is evidence for or against its number. Write new evidence only from a number moved alone in its hours, with a closed board_pts_h verdict, and say which other changes share its window.", "evidence": ["F143", "F144", "F152", "F188", "F209", "F222"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Other changes fell in the same hours for every row from 11/12 to 11/16 (e.g. F222 grade_frac_c 0.74 -> 0.76 beside c_first and a code change to own_floor), so nobody learned what any number did. Quoting one of these rows as \'it worked\' or \'it failed\' repeats the old mistake."}]}'
