[11/16 19:30:16] HARNESS: try 1: 30.1 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Judge every buyer change on buyer points/h and its sd (standing order 1), not on its parts. Close rate, saved/deal, the saved difference and the kept/not-taken label are parts only. Read the value now in force before moving a number (order 5). Do not step a number a second time in the same direction before its last change has a closed verdict (order 9).","evidence":["F54","F73","F83","F85","F87"],"status":"verified","trap":"The parts and the aim disagree. F54: close rate fell 0.775 -> 0.664 while points/h was +1%. F73: the saved difference was +1.4 sd, yet points/h read -24%. F83: the saved difference was +2.6 sd and saved/deal rose 0.3942 -> 0.4259, yet points/h read +0%. F85: close rate fell 0.791 -> 0.731 and points/h still rose 28%. Choosing on any one part gets the wrong answer.","when":["11/10 08:39","11/12 22:18","11/15 02:53","11/15 11:23","11/15 21:53"]},{"rule":"Leave MAX_RAISE at 0.35. 0.4 -> 0.35 was kept at +3% points/h (F46). Since then 0.35 -> 0.3 read +1%, -20%, -17% and -19%, and 0.35 -> 0.25 read -2%. 0.35 -> 0.4 read -5% and +0%. Move it only with a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F46","F54","F62","F69","F76","F79","F83","F86"],"status":"verified","trap":"Both 0.3 (+1.3 sd in F79 and F86) and 0.4 (+2.1 sd in F76, +2.6 sd in F83) showed a better saved difference and higher saved/deal, which invites a move. Points/h fell or stayed flat in every one of those trials.","when":["11/09 10:35","11/10 08:39","11/11 14:49","11/12 14:51","11/13 11:32","11/13 23:57","11/15 02:53","11/15 18:32"]},{"rule":"Do not retry RAISE_FOOD 1.2 -> 1.3: it lost on points/h both times (-14%, -4%). RAISE_GOODS 0.8 -> 0.9 is split (-3%, then +15%). MAX_TRIES 6 -> 5 is split too (+14%, then -9%). Treat the last two as unsettled. Change them only on a new measurement at the value in force, and only as a different number.","evidence":["F65","F81","F63","F74","F71","F92"],"status":"verified","trap":"The +15% (-0.001027 -> -0.000873, -0.1 sd) and +14% (-0.001089 -> -0.000936, +0.5 sd) reads sit on negative bases with small saved differences, so they look like wins but are weak. MAX_TRIES also read +14% and then -9%, so quoting either alone misleads.","when":["11/12 01:27","11/14 12:10","11/11 19:08","11/13 02:10","11/12 19:00","11/16 12:10"]},{"rule":"FIRM_GAP 0.07 has no clear winning neighbour. 0.07 -> 0.05 gave -35%, -18%, +6%, +6% and +2% points/h. 0.07 -> 0.09 gave +2% and -42%. Do not move it without a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F50","F52","F61","F68","F78","F82","F90"],"status":"verified","trap":"The three latest 0.05 reads (+6%, +6%, +2%, all within about 0.5 sd) are small and two sit on negative bases. The -35% (-1.1 sd) and -42% (-2.6 sd) reads are larger. Counting the recent small positives as a trend, or the old large negatives as the whole story, would both be wrong.","when":["11/09 18:04","11/09 23:48","11/11 11:18","11/12 11:03","11/13 14:35","11/14 18:55","11/16 09:05"]},{"rule":"FOOD_MARGIN 1.15 -> 1.1 is unsettled on points/h: +9% (+1.6 sd), +33% (+1.2 sd), -24% (+1.4 sd, negative base) and -29% (-1.9 sd). It is no proven win. Re-test only as a new measurement at the value in force, and never on saved/deal alone.","evidence":["F57","F64","F73","F87"],"status":"verified","trap":"Saved/deal rose in the first three 1.1 trials (e.g. 0.3722 -> 0.3889) and the saved difference was positive each time, yet points/h fell 24% in the third. The latest read, -29% at -1.9 sd, is the only one measured on the current saved/deal scale (0.8696 -> 0.8356), where saved/deal fell too.","when":["11/10 16:04","11/11 22:09","11/12 22:18","11/15 21:53"]},{"rule":"CAP 0.75 is unsettled. 0.75 -> 0.7 read +2%, +0%, -11% and +28% points/h. 0.75 -> 0.8 read -5%. Do not step CAP again without a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F53","F56","F67","F80","F85"],"status":"verified","trap":"0.7 gave better saved/deal on 11/10 12:26, 11/12 05:22 and 11/15 11:23 (e.g. 0.4032 -> 0.4146) and a lower close rate on 11/10 12:26 and 11/15 11:23. The one large win (+28%) sits on a negative base, and the -11% read came in between. Citing the +28% alone would overstate it.","when":["11/10 03:43","11/10 12:26","11/12 05:22","11/14 04:38","11/15 11:23"]},{"rule":"Do not add more break-rate, grade or over-cap penalties or re-rankings to the buyer\'s candidate or scout ordering. Every such A/B lost: sort by surplus/list -2%, break-rate weighting -6%, grade penalty -4%, soft-break ban -2%, scout expected-rate ranking -5%, over-cap exponent 8 -9% close rate. The only win in this family was lowering a penalty (short-shelf-life food 0.3 -> 0.05, +3% close rate).","evidence":["F37","F39","F42","F55","F59","F66","F58"],"status":"verified","trap":"Each was written with an expected +1% to +4% and measured negative. F37, F39 and F55 were still labelled kept. They were judged on saved/deal and close rate, not buyer points/h, so a kept label here is no evidence of a gain.","when":["11/08 11:55","11/08 16:36","11/08 21:36","11/10 09:28","11/11 00:28","11/12 05:22","11/10 17:41"]},{"rule":"A code change labelled kept can still read zero or negative on the aim, and a speed or part verdict is not a points result. Plan mode on half the orders was kept at -3% buyer_pts_h (expected +10%). Per-grade deal_limit was kept at -1% saved/deal, the warranty-grade rule at +0%, the 60 s retry cut at -1% paid/h (expected +8%), and the second scout wave at +1% close rate. Seconds-per-order gains (+37%, +22%, +13%) show speed only. Build on one only after its points/h read is checked.","evidence":["F70","F75","F77","F88","F72","F84","F91","F49"],"status":"verified","trap":"Stacking a follow-up on a kept label builds on a measured -3%, -1% or +0%. The +37% of F88 and the +22% of F72 measure seconds per order, not points. F49 measured +13% secs/order where -5% was expected, and was still kept.","when":["11/12 16:48","11/13 07