ement at the value in force.", "evidence": ["F65", "F81", "F63", "F74", "F71", "F92"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The +15% (F74, saved difference -0.1 sd) and +14% (F71, +0.5 sd) reads sit on negative points/h bases with small saved differences, so they look like wins but are weak. The later MAX_TRIES read (F92) reversed the sign.", "when": ["11/12 01:27", "11/14 12:10", "11/11 19:08", "11/13 02:10", "11/12 19:00", "11/16 12:10"]},\n{"rule": "FIRM_GAP 0.07 has no clear winning neighbour. 0.07 -> 0.05 gave -35%, -18%, +6%, +6% and +2% points/h. 0.07 -> 0.09 gave +2% and -42%. Do not move it without a new measurement at the value in force.", "evidence": ["F50", "F52", "F61", "F68", "F78", "F82", "F90"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The three latest 0.05 reads (+6%, +6%, +2%, all within about 0.5 sd) are small and two sit on negative bases, so they do not justify a move. The -35% (F52, -1.1 sd) and -42% (F68, -2.6 sd) reads are large losses, and the downside is bigger than the upside.", "when": ["11/09 18:04", "11/09 23:48", "11/11 11:18", "11/12 11:03", "11/13 14:35", "11/14 18:55", "11/16 09:05"]},\n{"rule": "FOOD_MARGIN 1.15 -> 1.1 is unsettled on points/h: +9% (+1.6 sd), +33% (+1.2 sd), -24% (+1.4 sd, negative base) and -29% (-1.9 sd). It is no proven win. Re-test only as a new measurement at the value in force, and never on saved/deal alone.", "evidence": ["F57", "F64", "F73", "F87"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Saved/deal rose in the first three 1.1 trials (e.g. 0.3722 -> 0.3889) and the saved difference was positive each time, yet points/h fell 24% in the third. The latest read (F87) was -29% at -1.9 sd.", "when": ["11/10 16:04", "11/11 22:09", "11/12 22:18", "11/15 21:53"]},\n{"rule": "CAP 0.75 is unsettled but leans toward 0.7 lately. 0.75 -> 0.7 read +2%, +0%, -11%, +28% and +14% points/h (the last two at +1.0 sd and +0.7 sd). 0.75 -> 0.8 read -5%. Step it again only as a new measurement at the value in force, judged on points/h.", "evidence": ["F53"