[11/17 01:19:45] HARNESS: try 1: 18.8 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [\n{"rule": "Send one net value per number per cycle. If you change your mind inside the cycle, send only the final value, never a change and its undo minutes apart.", "evidence": ["F149", "F150", "F177", "F178", "F182", "F183", "F186", "F187", "F197", "F198", "F212", "F213", "F219", "F220", "F221"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Change-and-undo pairs went out within minutes: fresh_premium 0.18 -> 0.15 and back at 11/14 10:13, step 0.6 -> 0.5 and back at 11/16 10:13, c_first 1 -> 0.0, then 0.0 -> 1, then 1 -> 0.0 between 15:16 and 15:33. Each window then holds several changes, so every row is MIXED and gives no verdict. These rows are weak: all are MIXED or unverified."},\n{"rule": "Do not step a number again in the same direction until its last step has a closed 2 h verdict (order 9). Take the evidence for the next step from the value now in force, not from an older value.", "evidence": ["F152", "F159", "F162", "F176", "F190", "F203", "F188", "F196", "F200", "F209", "F199", "F201"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Chains went out with no verdict between steps: clear_hours 14 -> 12 -> 10 -> 8, ask_frac_food 0.8 -> 0.78 -> 0.75 -> 0.7, floor_frac_food 0.52 -> 0.5 -> 0.48 -> 0.46 -> 0.45, grade_frac_b 0.94 -> 0.92 -> 0.88. Every step was MIXED, so none of the chain was measured. Weak evidence."},\n{"rule": "Before proposing a number, check order 14\'s list of values whose own verdict closed negative. A return to one needs a new measurement taken after it. \'The opposite direction is free\' does not cover such a return.", "evidence": ["F149", "F154", "F157", "F171", "F177"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Returns went out as \'a different or opposite number\': floor_frac_food up to 0.56 and 0.57, dear_depth back to 7, fresh_premium back down to 0.15 (11/13 20:54, 11/14 10:13). The supervisor reverted these. The rows are MIXED, so they show the process mistake, not the effect of the numbers."},\n{"rule": "Keep market_ask at 1.0 (order 15). Do not use a play-mode step on it. Only a closed A/B can move it.", "evidence": ["F186", "F187", "F189", "F191", "F192", "F193", "F197", "F198"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "market_ask moved 1.0 <-> 1.03 / 1.05 / 1.08 between 11/14 18:22 and 11/15 18:32, often back within an hour. Each move shared its hours with other changes (raw margin swings from -23% to +20%), so no value earned a clean verdict."},\n{"rule": "Do not cite a row marked [supervisor] as proof that a change worked or failed. It is the supervisor\'s own revert or move and carries \'no verdict\'. Judge a number only on its own closed window.", "evidence": ["F151", "F156", "F169", "F211", "F226"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Rows such as floor_frac_food 0.56 -> 0.52, ask_frac_food 0.83 -> 0.8 and ask_frac_food 0.72 -> 0.7 say \'no verdict\'. Reading a revert as proof that the earlier move was bad, or the revert as good, is circular."},\n{"rule": "Never cite a raw margin % on a MIXED row as evidence that a change worked. It mixes the effects of every change in those hours. Write a lesson only from a closed one-at-a-time verdict on our share of paid sales.", "evidence": ["F165", "F170", "F185", "F167", "F209", "F210"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Raw swings such as +163%, +290%, +212% (up) and -72%, -49%, -53% (down) sat on rows with 2-4 other changes in the same hours. Acting on them, for example keeping a change because of +290%, rests on no verdict."}\n]}'
