[11/17 07:26:12] HARNESS: try 1: 15.2 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Send one net value per number per cycle. If you change your mind inside the cycle, send only the final value, not a change and its undo minutes apart. Each such pair leaves two rows that share their hours with each other, so neither can be judged.","evidence":["F177","F178","F182","F183","F186","F187","F197","F198","F212","F213","F219","F220","F221","F224","F225"],"status":"unverified","trap":"fresh_premium 0.18 -> 0.15 and back at 11/14 10:13, step 0.6 -> 0.5 and back at 11/16 10:13, and c_first 1 -> 0.0 -> 1 -> 0.0 between 11/16 15:16 and 15:33 all came out MIXED with no verdict. The same happened with ask_frac_food 0.72 -> 0.7 and 0.7 -> 0.72 at 11/16 20:54. Each pair spent changes and taught nothing. These rows are weak evidence, since none has a verdict."},{"rule":"Do not step a number again in the same direction until its last step has a closed 2 h verdict (order 9). Take the evidence for the next step from the value now in force, not from an older value.","evidence":["F152","F159","F162","F188","F196","F200","F209","F190","F203","F199","F201"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Chains went out with no verdict between steps: clear_hours 14 -> 12 -> 10 -> 8, ask_frac_food 0.78 -> 0.75 -> 0.7, floor_frac_food 0.5 -> 0.48 -> 0.46 -> 0.45, and grade_frac_b 0.94 -> 0.92 -> 0.88. Every step was MIXED, so the chain cannot show which step helped or hurt."},{"rule":"Before proposing a number, check order 14\'s list of values whose own verdict closed negative. \'The opposite direction is free\' does not cover a return to one of them. A return needs a new measurement taken after it.","evidence":["F154","F157","F171","F177"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Returns were sent as \'a different or opposite number\': floor_frac_food back up to 0.57, dear_depth 6 -> 7, and fresh_premium 0.18 -> 0.15 (at 11/13 20:54 and again at 11/14 10:13). The supervisor reverted or undid them, and all four rows are MIXED."},{"rule":"Leave market_ask at 1.0 (order 15). Do not take a play-mode step on it. Any other value needs a closed A/B first.","evidence":["F186","F187","F189","F191","F192","F193","F197","F198"],"status":"unverified","trap":"market_ask moved between 1.0 and 1.03, 1.05 or 1.08 from 11/14 18:22 to 11/15 18:32, often back within an hour. Every move shared its hours with other changes (all MIXED), so no value got a clean verdict. The only closed positive verdict, +63% for 1.0, sits outside these rows."},{"rule":"Do not cite a [supervisor] revert row or a MIXED row\'s raw margin as proof that a change worked or failed. Judge a number only on its own closed, non-MIXED window. Until one exists, treat the number as untested.","evidence":["F151","F156","F165","F169","F170","F211","F226"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Supervisor reverts such as floor_frac_food 0.56 -> 0.52 and ask_frac_food 0.72 -> 0.7 say \'no verdict\'. Raw margins like +290% (11/13 18:09) and +163% (11/13 09:37) sat beside other changes and read the hour of day. Quoting them as wins would lock in noise."}]}'
