[11/17 07:43:01] HARNESS: try 1: 23.7 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Judge every buyer change on buyer points/h and its sd (standing order 1). Close rate, saved/deal, the saved difference and the kept/not-taken label are parts only. Read the value now in force before moving a number (order 5). Never step a number a second time in the same direction before its last change has a closed verdict (order 9).","evidence":["F54","F73","F83","F85","F87"],"status":"verified","trap":"The parts and the aim disagree. F54: close rate fell 0.775 -> 0.664 while points/h read +1%. F73: the saved difference was +1.4 sd but points/h fell 24%. F83: +2.6 sd on the saved difference while points/h read +0%. F87: -1.9 sd and -29%. Reading saved/deal or sd alone gives the wrong call."},{"rule":"Leave MAX_RAISE at 0.35. 0.35 -> 0.3 read +1%, -20%, -17% and -19% points/h. 0.35 -> 0.25 read -2%. 0.35 -> 0.4 read -5% and +0%. Only the first 0.4 -> 0.35 step was kept (+3%). Move it only with a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F46","F54","F62","F69","F76","F79","F83","F86"],"status":"verified","trap":"Both 0.3 (+1.3 sd in F79 and F86) and 0.4 (+2.1 sd in F76, +2.6 sd in F83) showed a better saved difference and higher saved/deal, so they look like wins. Points/h still fell or stayed flat each time."},{"rule":"Do not retry RAISE_FOOD 1.2 -> 1.3: it lost on points/h both times (-14%, -4%). RAISE_GOODS 0.8 -> 0.9 is split (-3%, +15%) and MAX_TRIES 6 -> 5 is split (+14%, -9%). SCOUT_WAIT 10 -> 8 has one read, +31% points/h (+1.2 sd) with close rate flat, but it was labelled not taken. Treat these three as unsettled and change them only on a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F65","F81","F63","F74","F71","F92","F95"],"status":"verified","trap":"The +15% (F74, -0.1 sd) and +14% (F71) reads sit on negative points/h bases with small saved differences, so they are weak. A single +31% read (F95) is also not a settled win, so do not treat it as one in either direction without a repeat."},{"rule":"FIRM_GAP 0.07 has no clear winning neighbour. 0.07 -> 0.05 gave -35%, -18%, +6%, +6% and +2% points/h. 0.07 -> 0.09 gave +2% and -42%. Do not move it without a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F50","F52","F61","F68","F78","F82","F90"],"status":"verified","trap":"The three latest 0.05 reads (+6%, +6%, +2%, all within about 0.5 sd) are small and two sit on negative bases, so they do not justify a move. The earlier -35% (F52) and -18% (F61) show the downside is large."},{"rule":"FOOD_MARGIN 1.15 -> 1.1 is unsettled on points/h: +9% (+1.6 sd), +33% (+1.2 sd), -24% (+1.4 sd, negative base) and -29% (-1.9 sd). It is no proven win. Re-test only as a new measurement at the value in force, and never on saved/deal alone.","evidence":["F57","F64","F73","F87"],"status":"verified","trap":"Saved/deal rose in the first three 1.1 trials (e.g. 0.3722 -> 0.3889) and the saved difference was positive each time, yet points/h fell 24% in the third. The latest read (F87) went the other way on both sd and points/h."},{"rule":"CAP 0.75 is unsettled but leans toward 0.7 lately. 0.75 -> 0.7 read +2%, +0%, -11%, +28% and +14% points/h (the last two at +1.0 sd and +0.7 sd). 0.75 -> 0.8 read -5%. Step it again only as a new measurement at the value in force, judged on points/h.","evidence":["F53","F56","F67","F80","F85","F93"],"status":"verified","trap":"0.7 usually shows better saved/deal and a lower close rate (F56, F85, F93), which makes it look like a safe win. F80 read -11% on points/h with no saved difference (-0.0 sd), so the pattern does not always hold."},{"rule":"Do not add more break-rate, grade or over-cap penalties or re-rankings to the buyer\'s candidate or scout ordering. Every such A/B lost on saved_deal or close rate: sort by surplus/list -2%, break-rate weighting -6%, grade penalty -4%, soft-break ban -2%, scout expected-saved ranking -5%, over-cap exponent 8 -9%. The one win was lowering a penalty (short-shelf-life food 0.3 -> 0.05, close rate +3%).","evidence":["F37","F39","F42","F55","F59","F66","F58"],"status":"verified","trap":"Each was written with an expected +1% to +4% and measured negative. F37, F39 and F55 were still labelled kept because they were judged on other terms. The kept label did not mean the change helped."},{"rule":"A code change labelled kept can still read zero or negative on the aim, or move its target metric the wrong way. A speed or part verdict is not a points result. Judge a follow-up on the aim before stacking it on a kept label, and treat F94 (+0%), F70 (+0%), F77 (-1%) and F75 (-3%) as no gain.","evidence":["F70","F75","F77","F88","F72","F84","F91","F49","F94","F16"],"status":"verified","trap":"Plan mode on half the orders was kept at -3% buyer_pts_h (expected +10%, F75). The rule-based plan step was kept for +37% on seconds/order (F88) with no points result. The 60 s retry cut read -1% paid/h against +8% expected (F91). The first-repeat walk-away rule was kept at +13% buyer_secs_order when -5% was expected (F49), and the early cancel rule read +1% against -8% expected (F16). Stacking on these gives false progress."}]}'
