ve. \'The opposite direction is free\' does not cover a return to one of them. Leave market_ask at 1.0 (order 15); any other value needs a closed A/B.","evidence":["F154","F157","F171","F177","F186","F187","F189","F191","F192","F193","F197","F198"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Returns went out as \'a different or opposite number\': floor_frac_food 0.52 -> 0.57, dear_depth 6 -> 7, fresh_premium 0.18 -> 0.15. market_ask moved between 1.0 and 1.03, 1.05 or 1.08 from 11/14 18:22 to 11/15 18:32, often back within an hour, and every move is MIXED. Facts only record the moves; the negative verdicts come from the supervisor\'s orders."},{"rule":"Do not cite a [supervisor] revert row or a MIXED row\'s raw margin as proof that a change worked or failed. Judge a number only on its own closed, non-MIXED window. Until one exists, treat the number as untested.","evidence":["F151","F156","F165","F169","F170","F211","F226"],"status":"unverified","trap":"Supervisor revert rows (F151, F156, F169, F211, F226) say \'no verdict\'. Raw margins such as +163% (F165) and +290% (F170) sat beside other changes in the same hours and read the hour of day. Quoting them as wins, or the reverts as losses, builds a lesson on nothing."}]}'
