[11/17 10:51:27] HARNESS: try 1: 28.1 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [{"rule": "Judge every buyer change on buyer points/h and its sd (standing order 1). Close rate, saved/deal, the saved difference and the kept/not-taken label are parts only. Read the value now in force before moving a number (order 5), and never step a number a second time in the same direction before its last change has a closed verdict (order 9).", "evidence": ["F54", "F73", "F83", "F85", "F87"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The parts and the aim disagree. 11/10 08:39 (F54): close rate fell 0.775 -> 0.664 while points/h read +1%. 11/12 22:18 (F73): the saved difference was +1.4 sd but points/h fell 24%. 11/15 02:53 (F83): the saved difference was +2.6 sd and saved/deal rose 0.3942 -> 0.4259, but points/h read +0%. 11/15 11:23 (F85): points/h +28% with only +1.0 sd. 11/15 21:53 (F87): close rate rose while points/h fell 29%. Choosing by saved/deal or sd would have picked wrongly in several of these.", "when": ["11/10 08:39", "11/12 22:18", "11/15 02:53", "11/15 11:23", "11/15 21:53"]}, {"rule": "Leave MAX_RAISE at 0.35. 0.35 -> 0.3 read +1%, -20%, -17% and -19% points/h. 0.35 -> 0.25 read -2%. 0.35 -> 0.4 read -5% and +0%. Only the first 0.4 -> 0.35 step was kept (+3%). Move it only with a new measurement at the value in force.", "evidence": ["F46", "F54", "F62", "F69", "F76", "F79", "F83", "F86"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Both 0.3 (+1.3 sd in F79 and F86) and 0.4 (+2.1 sd in F76, +2.6 sd in F83) showed a better saved difference and often higher saved/deal, so they look like wins. Points/h did not follow: 0.3 lost 17-20% in three trials, and 0.4 read -5% and +0%.", "when": ["11/09 10:35", "11/10 08:39", "11/11 14:49", "11/12 14:51", "11/13 11:32", "11/13 23:57", "11/15 02:53", "11/15 18:32"]}, {"rule": "Do not retry RAISE_FOOD 1.2 -> 1.3: it lost on points/h both times (-14%, -4%). RAISE_GOODS 0.8 -> 0.9 is split (-3%, +15%) and MAX_TRIES 6 -> 5 is split (+14%, -9%). SCOUT_WAIT 10 -> 8 has one read, +31% points/h (+1.2 sd), with close rate flat (0.691 -> 0.693). It is the only fresh lead, but a single read is not a proven win.", "evidence": ["F65", "F81", "F63", "F74", "F71", "F92", "F95"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The +15% (F74, -0.1 sd) and +14% (F71) reads sit on negative points/h bases with small saved differences, so they are weak. The single +31% read (F95) is also not settled: the same pattern of one good read followed by a bad one happened with MAX_TRIES and FOOD_MARGIN.", "when": ["11/12 01:27", "11/14 12:10", "11/11 19:08", "11/13 02:10", "11/12 19:00", "11/16 12:10", "11/17 03:51"]}, {"rule": "FIRM_GAP 0.07 has no clear winning neighbour. 0.07 -> 0.05 gave -35%, -18%, +6%, +6% and +2% points/h. 0.07 -> 0.09 gave +2% and -42%. Do not move it without a new measurement at the value in force.", "evidence": ["F50", "F52", "F61", "F68", "F78", "F82", "F90"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The three latest 0.05 reads (+6%, +6%, +2%, all within about 0.5 sd) are small and two sit on negative bases, so they do not justify a move. The earlier -35% (F52, -1.1 sd) and -18% (F61) show the downside. 0.09 lost 42% in F68 (-2.6 sd) after a +2% read in F50.", "when": ["11/09 18:04", "11/09 23:48", "11/11 11:18", "11/12 11:03", "11/13 14:35", "11/14 18:55", "11/16 09:05"]}, {"rule": "FOOD_MARGIN 1.15 -> 1.1 is unsettled on points/h: +9% (+1.6 sd), +33% (+1.2 sd), -24% (+1.4 sd, negative base) and -29% (-1.9 sd). It is no proven win. Re-test only as a new measurement at the value in force, and never on saved/deal alone.", "evidence": ["F57", "F64", "F73", "F87"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Saved/deal rose in the first three 1.1 trials (e.g. 0.3722 -> 0.3889) and the saved difference was positive each time, yet points/h fell 24% in the third. The latest read (F87) was -29% at -1.9 sd, so the early wins do not carry over.", "when": ["11/10 16:04", "11/11 22:09", "11/12 22:18", "11/15 21:53"]}, {"rule": "CAP 0.75 is unsettled but leans toward 0.7 lately. 0.75 -> 0.7 read +2%, +0%, -11%, +28% and +14% points/h (the last two at +1.0 sd and +0.7 sd). 0.75 -> 0.8 read -5%. Step it again only as a new measurement at the value in force, judged on points/h.", "evidence": ["F53", "F56", "F67", "F80", "F85", "F93"], "status": "verified", "trap": "0.7 usually shows better saved/deal and a lower close rate (F56, F85, F93), which makes it look like a safe win. F80 read -11% on points/h with no saved difference (-0.0 sd), and F56 and F67 read only +2% and +0%. Two good recent reads do not undo that.", "when": ["11/10 03:43", "11/10 12:26", "11/12 05:22", "11/14 04:38", "11/15 11:23", "11/16 17:01"]}, {"rule": "Do not add more break-rate, grade or over-cap penalties, or re-rankings by expected saved rate, to the buyer\'s candidate or scout ordering. Every such A/B lost on saved_deal or close rate: sort by surplus/list -2%, break-rate weighting -6%, grade penalty -4%, soft-break rule -2%, scout re-rank -5%, over-cap exponent 8 -9%. The one ranking win was lowering a penalty (short-shelf-life food 0.3 -> 0.05, +3% close rate).", "evidence": ["F37", "F39", "F42", "F55", "F59", "F66", "F58"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Each was written with an expected +1% to +4% and measured negative. F37, F39 and F55 were still labelled kept because they were judged on other terms. The kept label hid the negative saved_deal. The F58 win came from removing a penalty, so the direction to try is fewer penalties, not more.", "when": ["11/08 11:55", "11/08 16:36", "11/08 21:36", "11/10 09:28", "11/11 00:28", "11/12 05:07", "11/10 17:41"]}, {"rule": "A code change labelled kept can still read zero or negative on the aim, or move its target metric opposite to the expectation. A speed or part verdict is not a points result. Judge a follow-up on points/h before stacking it on a kept label, and treat F94 (+0% saved_deal) and F70 (+0%) as neutral, not as wins.", "evidence": ["F70", "F75", "F77", "F88", "F72", "F84", "F91", "F49", "F94", "F16"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Plan mode on half the orders was kept at -3% buyer_pts_h (expected +10%, F75). The rule-based plan step was kept for +37% on seconds/order (F88) with no points verdict. Cutting RETRY_UNTIL expected +8% paid/h and measured -1% (F91). F49 expected -5% secs/order and measured +13%, and F16 expected -8% and measured +1%, both the opposite of the expectation yet kept. F77 and F70 were kept at -1% and +0% saved_deal.", "when": ["11/12 16:48", "11/13 07:58", "11/13 13:13", "11/15 22:11", "11/12 21:47", "11/15 10:20", "11/16 10:13", "11/09 16:37", "11/17 01:21", "11/05 17:22"]}]}'
