[11/17 10:52:00] HARNESS: try 1: 14.4 s, exit 0, answer '{"proposal": {}, "ab": null, "recruit": null, "playbook": "none", "why": "The stars gap (4.34 at p0.31 on stars_rank) comes from low reviews about food shelf life and grade B quality, and no number I can see maps to those complaints. Every move I considered either repeats a value whose own verdict closed negative (order 14) or cannot be judged from the evidence (L1), so I am holding all numbers this cycle.", "ideas": ["tool: a per-buyer shelf-life check at quote time, so food is never offered with fewer hours left than the buyer\'s stated need (reviews: 2.6 h and 23 h left against 24 h needed). No single number can filter units by hours left against a buyer\'s requirement.", "tool: a grade-need filter before quoting, so a grade B unit is not offered to a buyer whose words ask for a higher grade (review: \'accepted grade B was below my preferred quality grade\'). Quoting by grade is a per-buyer decision that no shared floor or ask can express."], "lessons_used": ["L1"]}'
