[11/17 13:54:57] HARNESS: try 1: 33.4 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Judge every buyer change on buyer points/h and its sd (standing order 1). Close rate, saved/deal, the saved difference and the kept/not-taken label are only parts. Read the value now in force before moving a number (order 5), and do not step a number again in the same direction before its last change has a closed verdict (order 9). Saved/deal moved to a new scale (about 0.87 instead of about 0.4) by 11/15 21:53, so compare it only within one A/B.","evidence":["F54","F73","F83","F85","F87"],"status":"verified","trap":"The parts and the aim disagree. 11/10 08:39: close rate fell 0.775 -> 0.664 while points/h read +1%. 11/12 22:18: the saved difference was +1.4 sd but points/h was -24%. 11/15 02:53: +2.6 sd on the saved difference but points/h +0%. 11/15 21:53: saved/deal and close rate both rose in the 1.1 arm, yet points/h was -29%. Choosing on the parts would have kept losers.","when":["11/10 08:39","11/12 22:18","11/15 02:53","11/15 11:23","11/15 21:53"]},{"rule":"Leave MAX_RAISE at 0.35. 0.35 -> 0.3 read +1%, -20%, -17% and -19% points/h. 0.35 -> 0.25 read -2%. 0.35 -> 0.4 read -5% and +0%. Only the first 0.4 -> 0.35 step was kept (+3%). Move it only with a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F46","F54","F62","F69","F76","F79","F83","F86"],"status":"verified","trap":"Both 0.3 (+1.3 sd on 11/13 23:57 and 11/15 18:32) and 0.4 (+2.1 sd on 11/13 11:32, +2.6 sd on 11/15 02:53) showed a better saved difference and often higher saved/deal, so they look like wins. On points/h they did not win.","when":["11/09 10:35","11/10 08:39","11/11 14:49","11/12 14:51","11/13 11:32","11/13 23:57","11/15 02:53","11/15 18:32"]},{"rule":"Do not retry RAISE_FOOD 1.2 -> 1.3: it lost on points/h both times (-14%, -4%). RAISE_GOODS 0.8 -> 0.9 is split (-3%, +15%) and MAX_TRIES 6 -> 5 is split (+14%, -9%), so neither is a proven move. SCOUT_WAIT 10 -> 8 has one read, +31% points/h (+1.2 sd) with close rate flat (0.691 -> 0.693). It is promising but unrepeated. Re-measure it at the value in force before stacking anything on it.","evidence":["F65","F81","F63","F74","F71","F92","F95"],"status":"verified","trap":"The +15% (11/13 02:10, -0.1 sd) and +14% (11/12 19:00) reads sit on negative points/h bases with small saved differences, so they are weak and flip sign on repeat. The single +31% read is also one window and could be the same kind of noise.","when":["11/12 01:27","11/14 12:10","11/11 19:08","11/13 02:10","11/12 19:00","11/16 12:10","11/17 03:51"]},{"rule":"FIRM_GAP 0.07 has no clear winning neighbour. 0.07 -> 0.05 gave -35%, -18%, +6%, +6%, +2% and -16% points/h. 0.07 -> 0.09 gave +2% and -42%. Do not move it without a new measurement at the value in force.","evidence":["F50","F52","F61","F68","F78","F82","F90","F96"],"status":"verified","trap":"The small positive 0.05 reads (+6%, +6%, +2%) are all within about 0.5 sd, and two sit on negative bases. The latest 0.05 read (11/17 10:26) had +0.8 sd on the saved difference and a higher saved/deal (0.8606 -> 0.8727) yet points/h fell 16%. Citing the small wins or the saved side would repeat a coin flip.","when":["11/09 18:04","11/09 23:48","11/11 11:18","11/12 11:03","11/13 14:35","11/14 18:55","11/16 09:05","11/17 10:26"]},{"rule":"FOOD_MARGIN 1.15 -> 1.1 is unsettled on points/h: +9% (+1.6 sd), +33% (+1.2 sd), -24% (+1.4 sd, negative base) and -29% (-1.9 sd). It is no proven win. Re-test only as a new measurement at the value in force, and never on saved/deal alone.","evidence":["F57","F64","F73","F87"],"status":"verified","trap":"Saved/deal rose in the first three 1.1 trials (e.g. 0.3722 -> 0.3889) and the saved difference was positive each time, yet points/h fell 24% in the third. The latest read had both close rate and saved/deal up (0.8696 -> 0.8356 on saved/deal, but -1.9 sd) and points/h -29%.","when":["11/10 16:04","11/11 22:09","11/12 22:18","11/15 21:53"]},{"rule":"CAP 0.75 -> 0.7 leans positive lately but is unsettled: +2%, +0%, -11%, +28% and +14% points/h (the last two at +1.0 sd and +0.7 sd). 0.75 -> 0.8 read -5%. Step it only as a new measurement at the value in force, judged on points/h, and take the next step only after the last has a closed verdict.","evidence":["F53","F56","F67","F80","F85","F93"],"status":"verified","trap":"0.7 usually shows better saved/deal and a lower close rate (11/10 12:26, 11/15 11:23, 11/16 17:01), which makes it look like a safe win. 11/14 04:38 read -11% on points/h with no saved difference (-0.0 sd), so the pattern is not reliable.","when":["11/10 03:43","11/10 12:26","11/12 05:22","11/14 04:38","11/15 11:23","11/16 17:01"]},{"rule":"Do not add more break-rate, grade or over-cap penalties, or re-rankings by expected saved rate, to the buyer\'s candidate or scout ordering. Every such A/B lost: sort by surplus/list -2%, break-rate weighting -6%, grade penalty -4%, soft-breaks weighting -2%, scout re-rank -5%, exponent 8 on the over-cap penalty -9% close rate. The one gain came from lowering a penalty (short-shelf-life food 0.3 -> 0.05, +3% close rate).","evidence":["F37","F39","F42","F55","F59","F66","F58"],"status":"verified","trap":"Each was written with an expected +1% to +4% and measured negative. 11/08 11:55, 11/08 16:36 and 11/10 09:28 were still labelled kept because they were judged on other terms, so a kept label does not mean the ranking helped.","when":["11/08 11:55","11/08 16:36","11/08 21:36","11/10 09:28","11/11 00:28","11/12 05:07","11/10 17:41"]},{"rule":"A code change labelled kept can read zero or negative on the aim, or improve only a speed or part metric. Judge each code change on points/h, and do not stack a follow-up on a kept label whose own target metric missed its expectation. Treat the expected % as a guess: it overshot in most of these.","evidence":["F70","F75","F77","F88","F72","F84","F91","F49","F94"],"status":"verified","trap":"Plan mode on half the orders was kept at -3% buyer_pts_h (expected +