[11/17 16:39:57] HARNESS: try 1: 27.2 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons":[{"rule":"Judge a number only on its own closed, non-MIXED window. A MIXED row\'s raw margin and a [supervisor] revert row (\'no verdict\') are not proof that a change worked or failed. Until a clean window exists, treat the number as untested.","evidence":["F156","F165","F169","F170","F211","F226","F230","F227"],"status":"verified","trap":"Raw margins such as +163% (F165) and +290% (F170) sat beside other changes in the same hours, so they say nothing about the number. Only F227 in this record is VERIFIED. Citing a MIXED margin or a revert row as evidence builds a lesson on nothing."},{"rule":"clear_hours 10 -> 12 closed VERIFIED as no difference beyond noise (365/7040 -> 372/6848 sales). Do not treat clear_hours as a lever for board points. Look for gains in the rivals and edges tables instead.","evidence":["F227"],"status":"verified","trap":"The row shows value share -26% and raw margin -26%, which can be misread as a loss or as proof that 10 is better. The verdict is noise, not a loss. Earlier clear_hours rows (F152, F159, F162, F166, F179, F182, F183) are all MIXED and prove nothing."},{"rule":"Do not flip a number back within minutes of changing it. Let the new value run a closed window, or do not move it. Same-minute pairs leave only MIXED rows, so the evidence is lost.","evidence":["F177","F178","F212","F213","F215","F219","F220","F221","F224","F225"],"status":"unverified","trap":"fresh_premium, step and c_first were each reversed within 1-40 minutes, and ask_frac_food was lowered, raised and lowered again. Every row listed the other flips as confounds, so none gave a verdict and the changes cost effort for no information. These rows are MIXED, so they show the pattern, not which value is better."},{"rule":"Before moving ask_frac_food, read its value now (0.7 after F229) and check orders 9 and 10. Do not step it again in the same direction before the last change has a closed verdict. Treat ask_frac (all goods, F231) as a separate number.","evidence":["F224","F225","F226","F228","F229","F230","F231"],"status":"unverified","trap":"ask_frac_food was raised 0.7 -> 0.75 at 11:42 on 11/17 and put back to 0.7 a minute later, and 0.72 -> 0.7 was reverted at 11/16 20:54. Both ran beside stock_value or other changes, so the raw margins (-37%, -35%) say nothing about the number."},{"rule":"Raising floor_frac_food runs only as an A/B in one 0.01-0.02 step. A cut is a normal play-mode move under order 9. Read the value now before moving it.","evidence":["F154","F155","F156","F188","F196","F200"],"status":"unverified","trap":"0.52 -> 0.57 was done together with depth and other changes, and was undone a minute later by the supervisor (F156 \'no verdict\'). A 5-point raise is not a step. The later cuts (0.5, 0.48, 0.46) were all MIXED, so they are not proof that lower is better."},{"rule":"Keep market_ask at 1.0 for the rest of the round (order 15). Do not propose 1.03, 1.05 or 1.08 without a closed A/B.","evidence":["F186","F187","F189","F191","F192","F193","F197","F198"],"status":"unverified","trap":"market_ask moved among 1.0, 1.03, 1.05 and 1.08 many times, often back within 16-50 minutes, always beside other changes. All of these rows are MIXED (raw margins -23% to +20%), so none can justify a value. They only show that stepping it in play mode produces no clean verdict."},{"rule":"Check order 14\'s list of failed values before proposing a number, including fresh_premium 0.15. A return needs a new measurement taken after the earlier verdict.","evidence":["F171","F172","F177","F178"],"status":"unverified","trap":"fresh_premium 0.18 -> 0.15 was proposed twice (11/13 20:54, 11/14 10:13) and put back to 0.18 within a minute each time. Order 14 records 0.15 as closed negative (0.15 -> 0.18 judged +33%). Proposing it again wastes a cycle."}]}'
