[11/17 16:56:45] HARNESS: try 1: 29.4 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [\n{"rule": "Judge every buyer change on buyer points/h and its sd (standing order 1). Close rate, saved/deal, the saved difference and the kept/not-taken label are only parts. Read the value now in force before moving a number (order 5), and do not step a number again before its last change has a closed verdict (order 9).", "evidence": ["F54", "F73", "F83", "F85", "F87"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The parts and the aim disagree. 11/10 08:39: close rate fell 0.775 -> 0.664 while points/h read +1%. 11/12 22:18: the saved difference was +1.4 sd but points/h fell 24%. 11/15 02:53: +2.6 sd on the saved difference but points/h +0%. 11/15 21:53: saved/deal 0.8696 -> 0.8356 with points/h -29%. Acting on a part metric alone would have picked the wrong arm."},\n{"rule": "Leave MAX_RAISE at 0.35. 0.35 -> 0.3 read +1%, -20%, -17% and -19% points/h. 0.35 -> 0.25 read -2%. 0.35 -> 0.4 read -5% and +0%. Only the first 0.4 -> 0.35 step was kept (+3%). Move it only with a new measurement at the value in force.", "evidence": ["F46", "F54", "F62", "F69", "F76", "F79", "F83", "F86"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Both 0.3 (+1.3 sd on 11/13 23:57 and 11/15 18:32) and 0.4 (+2.1 sd on 11/13 11:32, +2.6 sd on 11/15 02:53) showed a better saved difference and often higher saved/deal, yet points/h was negative or flat. Reading the saved difference alone makes either neighbour look like a win."},\n{"rule": "Do not retry RAISE_FOOD 1.2 -> 1.3: it lost on points/h both times (-14%, -4%). RAISE_GOODS 0.8 -> 0.9 is split (-3%, +15%) and MAX_TRIES 6 -> 5 is split (+14%, -9%), so neither is a proven move. SCOUT_WAIT 10 -> 8 has one read, +31% points/h at +1.2 sd; it is the only open lead here, but a single read needs a repeat at the value in force before it counts as a win.", "evidence": ["F65", "F81", "F63", "F74", "F71", "F92", "F95"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The +15% (11/13 02:10, -0.1 sd) and +14% (11/12 19:00) reads sit on negative points/h bases with small saved differences, so they are weak and flip sign on repeat (-3%, -9%). Treating one positive read as proof repeats the MAX_TRIES and RAISE_GOODS flip-flop."},\n{"rule": "FIRM_GAP 0.07 has no clear winning neighbour. 0.07 -> 0.05 gave -35%, -18%, +6%, +6%, +2% and -16% points/h. 0.07 -> 0.09 gave +2% and -42%. Do not move it without a new measurement at the value in force.", "evidence": ["F50", "F52", "F61", "F68", "F78", "F82", "F90", "F96"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The small positive 0.05 reads (+6%, +6%, +2%) are all within about 0.5 sd, and two sit on negative bases. The latest 0.05 read (11/17 10:26) had +0.8 sd on the saved difference and a higher saved/deal (0.8606 -> 0.8727) but points/h fell 16%. The 0.09 side lost 42% at -2.6 sd."},\n{"rule": "FOOD_MARGIN 1.15 -> 1.1 is unsettled on points/h: +9% (+1.6 sd), +33% (+1.2 sd), -24% (+1.4 sd, negative base) and -29% (-1.9 sd). It is no proven win. 1.15 -> 1.2 was not taken. Re-test only as a new measurement at the value in force, and never on saved/deal alone.", "evidence": ["F45", "F57", "F64", "F73", "F87"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Saved/deal rose in the first three 1.1 trials (e.g. 0.3722 -> 0.3889) and the saved difference was positive each time, yet points/h fell 24% in the third. The latest read went the other way on every part (-1.9 sd, -29%). Two of the four labels said not taken despite +33%, so labels do not settle it either."},\n{"rule": "CAP 0.75 -> 0.7 leans positive lately but is unsettled: +2%, +0%, -11%, +28% and +14% points/h (the last two at +1.0 sd and +0.7 sd). 0.75 -> 0.8 read -5%. Step it only as a new measurement at the value in force, judged on points/h, and take the lower close rate it brings into account.", "evidence": ["F53", "F56", "F67", "F80", "F85", "F93"], "status": "verified", "trap": "0.7 usually shows better saved/deal and a lower close rate (11/10 12:26, 11/15 11:23, 11/16 17:01), which makes it look like a safe win. 11/14 04:38 read -11% on a flat saved difference (-0.0 sd) and a close rate drop 0.837 -> 0.769. Two of the five reads were about zero, so it is not a sure gain."},\n{"rule": "Do not add more break-rate, grade or over-cap penalties, or re-rankings by expected saved rate, to the buyer\'s candidate or scout ordering. Every such A/B lost: sort by surplus/list -2%, break-rate weighting -6%, grade penalty -4%, soft-break weighting -2%, scout re-rank by expected saved rate -5%, stronger over-cap exponent -9% close rate. The one gain went the other way: lowering the short-shelf-life food penalty from 0.3 to 0.05 gave +3% close rate.", "evidence": ["F37", "F39", "F42", "F55", "F59", "F66", "F58"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Each was written with an expected +1% to +4% and measured negative. 11/08 11:55, 11/08 16:36 and 11/10 09:28 were still labelled kept because they were judged on a part, not on the aim, so a kept label hid a loss. A new penalty is more likely to cost closes than to save money."},\n{"rule": "A code change labelled kept can read zero or negative on the aim, or improve only a speed or part metric. Judge each code change on points/h, and do not stack a follow-up on a kept label whose own target metric missed its expectation. Treat speed wins (seconds/order) as parts, not as board gains.", "evidence": ["F70", "F75", "F77", "F88", "F72", "F84", "F91", "F49", "F94"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Plan mode on half the orders was kept at -3% buyer_pts_h (expected +10%, 11/13 07:58). The rule-based plan step was kept for +37% seconds/order (expected +25%, 11/15 22:11), and the shop-drop rule for +22%; neither is a points gain. The 60 s retry cut was kept at -1% paid/h (expected +8%). Warranty, grade-cost and grade-C refusal changes read +0%, -1% and +0%, so kept meant no harm, not a win."}\n]}'
