h-cap / full-bar work in restock_r3.py until a clean read of points/h exists.","evidence":["F311","F339","F358","F362"],"status":"unverified","trap":"All four were \'kept\' and all four were MIXED. Shop points/h was negative every time (-35%, -58%, -2%, -42%). Measured revenue missed its +3% expectation every time (-3%, -40%, -29%, -38%). Building on \'kept\' would push further in a direction that has not paid."},{"rule":"Treat the buyer plan-mode rule (11/15 22:11) as evidence of cheaper buyer time only. Check board points per hour before building on it.","evidence":["F319"],"status":"unverified","trap":"It won a same-hours A/B on buyer_secs_order (+37% measured against +25% expected) on 120 and 132 orders. That is a part of the aim, not the aim (order 1), and it carries no board points, so calling it a board win would be wrong."},{"rule":"Before proposing a number, check the supervisor\'s pins and the negative-value list. market_ask stays at 1.0 (order 15), window_depth stays at 2.0 or more (order 12), sku_depth stays at 3 or more (order 13), and order 14 lists values whose own verdict closed negative (for example dear_depth 7 and 4).","evidence":["F295","F300","F313"],"status":"contradicted","trap":"market_ask was moved to 1.03 at 11/15 19:39, after the 11/15 18:32 pin at 1.0, and dear_depth went 6 -> 7 although 7 was a closed negative. Both were MIXED, so they left no verdict and only made a mess of the record."}]}'
