with small saved differences, so they are weak and the sign flipped on repeat (MAX_TRIES -9%). A single +31% read labelled not taken could be read as a win or a loss; it is neither until repeated."},\n{"rule": "FIRM_GAP 0.07 has no clear winning neighbour. 0.07 -> 0.05 gave -35%, -18%, +6%, +6%, +2% and -16% points/h. 0.07 -> 0.09 gave +2% and -42%. Do not move it without a new measurement at the value in force.", "evidence": ["F50", "F52", "F61", "F68", "F78", "F82", "F90", "F96"], "status": "verified", "trap": "The small positive 0.05 reads (+6%, +6%, +2%) are all within about 0.5 sd, and two sit on negative bases. The latest 0.05 read (11/17 10:26) had +0.8 sd on the saved difference and saved/deal up, yet points/h fell 16%. Counting small wins as a trend repeats a coin flip."},\n{"rule": "FOOD_MARGIN 1.15 -> 1.1 is unsettled on points/h: +9% (+1.6 sd), +33% (+1.2 sd), -24% (+1.4 sd, negative base) and -29% (-1.9 sd). It is no proven win. 1.15 -> 1.2 was not taken. Re-test only as a new measurement at the value in force, judged on points/h.", "evidence": ["F45", "F57", "F64", "F73", "F87"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Saved/deal rose in the first three 1.1 trials (e.g. 0.3722 -> 0.3889) and the saved difference was positive each time, yet points/h fell 24% in the third. The latest read (11/15 21:53) was -29% at -1.9 sd, so the earlier positive reads did not hold."},\n{"rule": "CAP 0.75 -> 0.7 leans positive lately but is unsettled: +2%, +0%, -11%, +28% and +14% points/h (the last two at +1.0 sd and +0.7 sd). 0.75 -> 0.8 read -5%. Step it only as a new measurement at the value in force, judged on points/h, and take the sd into account.", "evidence": ["F53", "F56", "F67", "F80", "F85", "F93"], "status": "verified", "trap": "0.7 usually shows better saved/deal and a lower close rate (11/10 12:26, 11/15 11:23, 11/16 17:01), which makes it look like a safe win. 11/14 04:38 read -11% on the same pattern, so the pattern is not proof. The two big positive reads came from bases that were negative or small."},\n{"rule": "Do not add more break-rate, grade or over-cap penalties, or re-rankings by expected saved rate, to the buyer\'s candidate or scout ordering. Every such A/B lost: sort by surplus/list -2%, break-rate weighting -6%, grade penalty -4%, soft-break shop record -2%, scout re-rank by saved rate -5%, scout exponent 8 -9% close rate. The one ranking change that won loosened a penalty (short-shelf-life food 0.3 -> 0.05, +3% close rate).", "evidence": ["F37", "F39", "F42", "F55", "F59", "F66", "F58"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Each loser was written with an expected +1% to +4% and measured negative. 11/08 11:55, 11/08 16:36 and 11/10 09:28 were still labelled kept because they were judged against a weak bar, so a kept label did not protect against a ranking that cost points. Stacking a new penalty on the same idea repeats the loss."},\n{"rule": "A code change labelled kept can read zero or negative on the aim, or improve only a speed or part metric. Judge each code change on points/h, and do not stack a follow-up on a kept label whose own target metric missed its expectation. Treat speed gains (seconds/order) as parts, not wins, until points/h confirms.", "evidence": ["F70", "F75", "F77", "F88", "F72", "F84", "F91", "F49", "F94", "F26", "F30"], "status": "verified", "trap": "Plan mode on half the orders was kept at -3% buyer_pts_h (expected +10%, 11/13 07:58). The rule-based plan step was kept for +37% seconds/order (expected +25%, 11/15 22:11), built on that plan mode. The 60 s retry cap read -1% paid/h against +8% expected, the 7cc785db92f2 warranty rule read +0%, and the grade-C refusal read +0%. F26 and F30 were kept at -2% saved/deal against expected +5% and +4%. A kept label is not an aim verdict."}\n]}'
