[11/17 23:25:01] HARNESS: try 1: 9.9 s, exit 0, answer '{"proposal": {}, "why": "Every recent cycle left the numbers unchanged, and the supervisor\'s 16:0x note says no shop number can move board rank before 23:59, with Book and revenue out of reach. Paid sales fell from 161 to 58 per hour without a number change to blame, so a new move now would be confounded, and every value I could reach is either closed-negative (max_list 600k or 1.15M+, dear_depth 4 or 7, sku_depth 4, window_depth 1.5 or 2.8, sku_cap 18) or pinned (window_depth 2.0+, sku_depth 3+, ask_frac_food above 0.70).", "ideas": ["tool: a clearance rule (clear_floor) for the 83 of 91 300k+ A units sitting above the market median (49.9M at cost). It would sell stuck stock down to cost, which the number set cannot do, since the A floor is cost/(1-WARRANTY_Q) and market_ask only cuts units that already sell.", "tool: the 22:29 alert shows buyer dyishappy rating our last 5 deals 2.40 against 4.13 elsewhere. A per-buyer block list (blocked_buyers_r3.json, read per checkout) could stop that drag on stars_rank, which is the only term still movable, with no number change needed."], "lessons_used": ["L5", "L1", "L3"]}'
[11/17 23:25:03] HARNESS: try 1: 12.4 s, exit 0, answer '{"proposal": {}, "recruit": null, "why": "Buyer saved is pinned near 0.745 and the board ranks cannot move before 23:59, so the buyer numbers have no closed verdict that justifies a move; the evidence (504 deals from 671 orders, 823 walks, lost-talk gap median 0.26) is not enough to say which direction helps. The rival buyer teams all show negative reward at MAX_RAISE 0.25-0.4 and FIRM_GAP 0.03-0.05, which does not show their style beats ours, so no recruit.", "ideas": ["tool: a per-talk log of each deal\'s saving against the running mean, with the walk-away price and the seller\'s last offer, so FIRM_GAP and CLOSE_GAP can be judged per talk instead of from pinned board totals", "Walked talks (823 against 504 deals) are where buyer saved is lost, but no number can tell a good walk from a bad one; the lever is the reason we walk, which needs the log above"], "lessons_used": []}'
