[11/17 23:56:44] HARNESS: try 1: 9.3 s, exit 0, answer '{"lessons": [{"rule": "Judge forum changes on the forum rating (0-1, counted as itself) and on which of our posts draw dislike stances, split by post kind, as standing order 6 says. Do not judge them on forum_votes_post read as the hour before against the hour after.", "evidence": ["F3", "F4"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "F3 was reverted on forum_votes_post -20% and F4 was kept despite -9%. Both are raw before/after readings that read the hour of day, so neither the revert nor the keep is evidence about the change."}, {"rule": "Treat the our_deals cap (F4: a post goes to our_deals only when neither of our last two posts was, about 1 post in 3, still in force) and the narrowed note() (F3, reverted) as open questions with no valid verdict. To retune either, compare post kinds over the same hours and judge on the forum rating and on dislike stances, not on forum_votes_post.", "evidence": ["F3", "F4"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Taking the F3 revert as proof that the narrowed note() was bad, or keeping the F4 cap because its tests passed (14/14). Passing tests show the code runs, not that the posts draw fewer dislikes."}, {"rule": "The 310 s post cadence is fixed by code and the market\'s limit (F5, F6), so it is not a lever. F5 has no verdict and F6 is MIXED, so neither is evidence about cadence or post quality. Spend effort on which post kinds draw dislike stances, never trade post quality for count, and do not ship a forum change in the same hours as a shop number change.", "evidence": ["F5", "F6"], "status": "unverified", "trap": "Citing F6\'s buyer points/h +8% or its forum_votes_post None -> None as a result of the cadence change. open_gap and dear_depth also changed in the same hours (MIXED), so the +8% cannot be pinned on FORMAT_EVERY 360 -> 310."}]}'
